{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:27:29.686Z","ordinal":389981,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1789b-f716-7531-abbb-eff4801a4d2c","call_id":"call_02e23d8bec5f44eca9bd81c6553b4feb","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a` against base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421` (diff SHA-256 `c87acdb9e218d5a894014350495038e3815fa88843bb5bfdda88baf5fc16d683`).\\n\\nThe store checks now reject unsupported versions and malformed target credentials before writing. In-flight cancellation also prevents a late discovery result from activating setup.\\n\\nOne issue remains: [provider_connect.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/provider_connect.ts:61) resets the provisional endpoint unconditionally, even when the supplied request ID is unrelated or unknown. Since [sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/sidecar.ts:215) calls this for every provider cancellation, canceling another request can clear a separate local setup. Make reset conditional on matching the local setup request, while preserving an explicit clear for closing its picker; add coverage for both matching and unrelated cancellation.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1789b-d3a0-7dd1-894e-ea6b5edaaa62","create_time":1793024849.6861572}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
