{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:32:23.554Z","ordinal":390233,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1789b-d3a0-7dd1-894e-ea6b5edaaa62","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7d02cc4a-d713-4ab8-ac9f-508ddc431f86","process_id":"86242","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short --branch && git log -3 --oneline --decorate && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/READINESS_POST_RC8_REFRESH_20261026/owner.json && rg -n -C 3 'RC8|Terminal|acceptance|OpenRouter|held-out|installed' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-post-rc8-pr254","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short --branch && git log -3 --oneline --decorate && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/READINESS_POST_RC8_REFRESH_20261026/owner.json && rg -n -C 3 'RC8|Terminal|acceptance|OpenRouter|held-out|installed' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254...origin/v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254 [gone]\n4564ac6 (HEAD -> v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254) docs(release): refresh readiness after PR254\nb73b6ec Merge pull request #254 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-provider-stream-integration\n24774a1 (v1/defect-provider-stream-integration) fix(cli): preserve provider output and error-code semantics\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254\",\"scope\":\"refresh current v1 release checkpoint after PR252/PR254 integration and post-merge CI; docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md only\",\"base\":\"b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421\",\"since\":\"2026-10-26T13:42:03Z\"}\n325-## Historical evidence: Node 20 full-suite follow-up (2026-10-17 07:13 UTC)\n326-\n327-- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\n328:- A four-file follow-up in the PR #10 worktree avoids exposing external launcher paths in packaged doctor evidence and recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries while rejecting zero-test, all-skipped, and cancelled-only summaries. The cancelled-only edge case was found during independent review and fixed before acceptance; the reviewer accepted the corrected parser/test diff. Build succeeded, the focused four-file selection passed **47/47**, staged `git diff --check` passed, and staged Gitleaks found zero findings.\n329-- One full-suite attempt on the pre-correction working tree was intentionally interrupted after review found the cancelled-only edge case. It is classified as interrupted, not passed or failed. The prior 1,097/7 result remains historical evidence and is not erased.\n330-\n331-## Historical evidence: Release validation update (2026-10-17 06:40 UTC)\n--\n335-\n336-## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\n337-\n338:This section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures remain historical evidence and are not erased; the active sealed held-out corpus is `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, SHA-256 `50895b84…`, PR #16).\n339-\n340-- At 03:10 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412` and `v1/candidate-1` was `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n341-- Independent inspection of pilot candidate v17 verified manifest digest `ce44dd2066dc4dec6c5e1f56021e3b442aa293510cbf9f217cf2c2e2256d83fe`, all 227 listed file hashes/sizes, no unlisted package files, 40 parseable tasks, 20 repository/20 fixture tasks, and 80/80 validator-command digest coverage. That author-exposed set was not independently held out or accepted and was retired as development/pilot material when `heldout-v2` was commissioned.\n342-- Independent inspection of Node 24.11.1 supplement v2 verified its manifest digest (`fc8fe753272bdd2b66e17e84f6f910b1aa4230b4f9284f022e09eff0df0afd7c`), payload `SUPPLEMENTARY_VALIDATION.json` digest (`aec9651dac09d38867201d0c37163fb25213222f912114bfbda49f50e096ce36`), and binding to v17. Its three specified tasks passed the recorded base-failure/reference-pass checks.\n343:- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\n344-\n345-## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\n346-\n--\n362-- `make build` completed successfully in an isolated candidate worktree. The produced TUI and CLI entrypoint hashes were respectively `ca20da9214db8dcb130cfa35f25f2e76f9caad63dcf3dfbefe49132fcaa9e52f` and `8da0ccf909d5432de22d62459168f21a22b4360607cbf47259338cc144758f42`.\n363-- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repository at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-built-6151.log` (SHA-256 `b72e0e15819985fc48f39998d2adc5ce90e9dd125519784c25a2a2b4d2db9521`).\n364-- The earlier unbuilt `make test` failed (Rust 281 passed; CLI 1060/1087 passed, 27 failed, zero skipped) because required generated build outputs were absent. It is preserved at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-6151.log` (SHA-256 `7c4a364daedc3b26bd6b0392f6e0466c581c33ae5ef9d04c11348129e0abbb31`) and is superseded only for the source-suite result by the correctly ordered build-then-test run.\n365:- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n366-- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n367-\n368-## Requirements below their required gate (reconciled at `a7126aa`)\n369-\n370-| ID | Current state | Remaining behavior or evidence | Dependency | Owner role | Exact next action |\n371-|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n372:| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\n373:| `REQ-AGT-004` | tested (depth 0; work-unit mechanism landed in PR-4b) | `AGT-02a` archive→task→session commit ordering is applied to durable work units by PR-4b (`agent.ts:3339-3402`, `operation_runner.ts:566`, `durable_continuity.test.ts:359`, `dispositions.md` M2); work-unit pressure-forced compaction + SIGKILL crash-boundary test is in flight under `PLAN-04 PR-4g`, and live long-task `ACC-CONT-10` remains pending RC qualification. | `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (`ACC-CONT-03` SIGKILL), `ACC-CONT-10` on installed RC | Continuity implementer, independent reviewer, and qualification operator | Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (M1/M3/L5), then execute `ACC-CONT-10` on the installed RC during M5. |\n374:| `REQ-AGT-010` | partial (RR; v1 subset independently accepted at `f68b5bc`) | `ACC-TRUST-04` v1 subset (workspace skills/knowledge trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted (PR #17 `f68b5bc`); `DEC-04` defers the full `CTX-001` provenance graph and `CTX-002` to post-v1. | Installed-RC verification; post-v1 deferral recorded | Requirement owner | Preserve the `DEC-04` v1 subset / post-v1 boundary in release notes and verify no regression on the installed RC. |\n375-| `REQ-AGT-111` | open (post-v1 shared-loop refactor; v1 behavior still required) | `PLAN-04` defers the full shared step implementation, while v1 requires documented main/subagent divergences and `measureAdmission` in the subagent loop. Calls exist in both loops, and divergence documentation is tracked under `PLAN-04`. | `PLAN-04` task 6 and source evidence | Continuity implementer, then requirement owner | Verify both `measureAdmission` calls satisfy strict-counting behavior and ensure main/subagent divergence documentation is reconciled in the ledger. |\n376-| `REQ-PRV-003` | implemented | Standalone behavior has scripted tests but no qualifying live standalone evidence (HIST-08). | Installed RC; standalone matrix | Provider qualification operator | Run `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 for supported server profiles and archive sanitized receipts. |\n377:| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\n378-| `REQ-REL-106` | open (post-v1; manual path defined for v1) | `SPEC-06` marks self-uninstall/prune post-v1 and retains the quickstart manual uninstall as the v1 path. The ledger's open status is a roadmap deferral, not a v1 implementation blocker. | Post-v1 scope; release documentation | Release/documentation owner | Preserve the documented manual uninstall path for v1 and record this item as explicitly deferred in the final release ledger. |\n379:| `REQ-AGT-118` | tested (source level; `DEC-17` exceptions preserved) | Conflict resolved by `DEC-17` (PR #11 `f771a3c`): the `≥ 1` token-per-CJK/Hangul-character admission-safety floor takes precedence over the `≤ 1.5×` band, which applies to corpora not dominated by the floor; Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) floor exceptions remain recorded. Source tests (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3) and independent review records (PRs #12, #14, #15) are integrated. | Installed-RC qualification | Qualification operator | Retain the `DEC-17` exception record; source-level `tested` status does not substitute for installed-RC product qualification. |\n380:| `REQ-AGT-110` | open | Independent continuity/compaction/truncation acceptance under `ACCEPTANCE.md` §8, including an independent long task with two compactions and kill/resume. | Installed RC and reviewer who did not implement the work | Owner-supplied independent reviewer | After RC freeze, execute the reviewer procedure and archive a per-area verdict; this cannot be self-signed. |\n381-| `REQ-PER-107` | implemented (post-v1 optional item) | `SPEC-08` marks parent-directory fsync post-v1 and optional. Source evidence exists; this is not a v1 gate under the accepted spec. | Post-v1 scope | Persistence implementer and requirement owner | Keep recorded as optional post-v1 scope. |\n382:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n383-| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n384:| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n385:| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n386-| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n387-| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n388-| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n389:| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n390:| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\n391:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n392-| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n393-\n394-At `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121 rows; 107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open**. In `--enforce` mode (the G6 release gate), the checker remains fail-closed until the remaining blocker and release-required rows above reach their required post-qualification states.\n--\n400-| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\n401-| G1 safety | Full source suite (`1,152/1,152` CLI, `281/281` Rust, 0 skipped) and `scripts/security_gates.sh` pass in CI run `39108774170`. | Source gate green; artifact-bound checks run at Stage 3 after RC construction. |\n402-| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n403:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n404:| G4 persistence | Source persistence and retention tests pass in CI (`39108774170`). | Source gate green; independent RC acceptance (§8) pending Stage 4. |\n405-\n406-## Release and qualification sequence (`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1)\n407-\n--\n409-2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\n410-3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\n411-4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n412:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n413-6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\n414-\n415-## RC5 qualification checkpoint (2026-10-25)\n--\n424-### RC5 artifacts and installation\n425-\n426-- Release workflow [40193772994](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40193772994) completed successfully and published `v1.0.0-rc.5` as a prerelease. The archive SHA-256 is `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `2206b35a0aed8a4b9635012c0ad55a6eae34d12fe3255c53d43ab8b1d8e7a8c1`.\n427:- Published asset hashes and provenance attestations verified against the release workflow and exact tag. The official installer installed the archive on the authenticated engineering host; its version, package manifest and provenance sidecar matched the candidate.\n428:- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n429-- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n430-\n431-### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\n432-\n433:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\n434:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n435-- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n436-\n437-### Remaining qualification gates\n438-\n439-| Gate | State at RC5 | Next executable step / completion condition |\n440-|---|---|---|\n441:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n442:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n443:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n444-| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n445:| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n446-| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n447-| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n448:| Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n449-| Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\n450-\n451:Public metadata updates were added to issues [#3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3) and [#5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/5). Publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance; no additional authorization is requested here.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":839568226}},"started_at_ms":1793025142711,"completed_at_ms":1793025143552}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:32:24.576Z","ordinal":390234,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a178a0-7700-7aa3-b940-11b7a9c33340","call_id":"call_110da43e810f44df9faa32718eef1a74","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"80db40\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.839627004,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6560,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6560)\\nTotal output lines: 105\\n\\n## v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254...origin/v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254 [gone]\\n4564ac6 (HEAD -> v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254) docs(release): refresh readiness after PR254\\nb73b6ec Merge pull request #254 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-provider-stream-integration\\n24774a1 (v1/defect-provider-stream-integration) fix(cli): preserve provider output and error-code semantics\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"codex-root\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"mike-dev\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/readiness-post-rc8-pr254\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"refresh current v1 release checkpoint after PR252/PR254 integration and post-merge CI; docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md only\\\",\\\"base\\\":\\\"b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-10-26T13:42:03Z\\\"}\\n325-## Historical evidence: Node 20 full-suite follow-up (2026-10-17 07:13 UTC)\\n326-\\n327-- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\\n328:- A four-file follow-up in the PR #10 worktree avoids exposing external launcher paths in packaged doctor evidence and recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries while rejecting zero-test, all-skipped, and cancelled-only summaries. The cancelled-only edge case was found during independent review and fixed before acceptance; the reviewer accepted the corrected parser/test diff. Build succeeded, the focused four-file selection passed **47/47**, staged `git diff --check` passed, and staged Gitleaks found zero findings.\\n329-- One full-suite attempt on the pre-correction working tree was intentionally interrupted after review found the cancelled-only edge case. It is classified as interrupted, not passed or failed. The prior 1,097/7 result remains historical evidence and is not erased.\\n330-\\n331-## Historical evidence: Release validation update (2026-10-17 06:40 UTC)\\n--\\n335-\\n336-## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\\n337-\\n338:This section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures remain historical evidence and are not erased; the active sealed held-out corpus is `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, SHA-256 `50895b84…`, PR #16).\\n339-\\n340-- At 03:10 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412` and `v1/candidate-1` was `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\\n341-- Independent inspection of pilot candidate v17 verified manifest digest `ce44dd2066dc4dec6c5e1f56021e3b442aa293510cbf9f217cf2c2e2256d83fe`, all 227 listed file hashes/sizes, no unlisted package files, 40 parseable tasks, 20 repository/20 fixture tasks, and 80/80 validator-command digest coverage. That author-exposed set was not independently held out or accepted and was retired as development/pilot material when `heldout-v2` was commissioned.\\n342-- Independent inspection of Node 24.11.1 supplement v2 verified its manifest digest (`fc8fe753272bdd2b66e17e84f6f910b1aa4230b4f9284f022e09eff0df0afd7c`), payload `SUPPLEMENTARY_VALIDATION.json` digest (`aec9651dac09d38867201d0c37163fb25213222f912114bfbda49f50e096ce36`), and binding to v17. Its three specified tasks passed the recorded base-failure/reference-pass checks.\\n343:- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\\n344-\\n345-## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\\n346-\\n--\\n362-- `make build` completed successfully in an isolated candidate worktree. The produced TUI and CLI entrypoint hashes were respectively `ca20da9214db8dcb130cfa35f25f2e76f9caad63dcf3dfbefe49132fcaa9e52f` and `8da0ccf909d5432de22d62459168f21a22b4360607cbf47259338cc144758f42`.\\n363-- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repo…4060 tokens truncated… evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\\n429-- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\\n430-\\n431-### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\\n432-\\n433:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\\n434:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\\n435-- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\\n436-\\n437-### Remaining qualification gates\\n438-\\n439-| Gate | State at RC5 | Next executable step / completion condition |\\n440-|---|---|---|\\n441:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\\n442:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\\n443:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\\n444-| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\\n445:| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\\n446-| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\\n447-| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\\n448:| Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\\n449-| Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\\n450-\\n451:Public metadata updates were added to issues [#3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3) and [#5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/5). Publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance; no additional authorization is requested here.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1789b-d3a0-7dd1-894e-ea6b5edaaa62","create_time":1793025144.576091}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
