{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:37:44.029Z","ordinal":390487,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1789b-d3a0-7dd1-894e-ea6b5edaaa62","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5b97061a-d6ea-4c63-9a75-231c9abe0537","process_id":"88419","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i '15 cell|per-cell|80×24.*40×14|terminal matrix worksheet|approval screenshot' docs scripts | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i '15 cell|per-cell|80×24.*40×14|terminal matrix worksheet|approval screenshot' docs scripts","query":"15 cell|per-cell|80×24.*40×14|terminal matrix worksheet|approval screenshot","path":"docs"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:5:**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:86:  \"approval.png\": \"approval screenshot\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:114:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:128:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:142:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:184:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:198:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:294:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:403:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:458:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:67:- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:69:- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:83:Mark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:84:required screenshots and per-cell evidence are archived. Mark it FAIL if any\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":794288126}},"started_at_ms":1793025463234,"completed_at_ms":1793025464028}}
