{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:55:51.835Z","ordinal":391103,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a178b5-f01b-7ee3-90f3-604a5d58aa2d","call_id":"call_2190f20e204e4cbaa245fc63db6360ff","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Committed the local endpoint remediation for independent review:\\n\\n- **Commit:** `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa`\\n- **Base:** `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`\\n- **Diff SHA-256:** `7d3dbe88cdb33f4d094268567b0e52ae38da6fd0fc492428d7bd2ad122a51869`\\n- **Status:** clean worktree; not pushed; all owned claims released and logged.\\n\\nThe changes address legacy credential origin binding, invalid replacement-key fallback, cloud disclosure and endpoint echo, model-cache isolation by full endpoint, and persistence failure handling. The PTY test now traverses the added appliance row before selecting Anthropic.\\n\\n**Validation:** `npm run build` passed. The six focused test files passed **105/105**, including the corrected PTY journey. Rust `nexus-tui` release and `harness-core` debug builds succeeded; `git diff --check` passed. The earlier 9 sidecar failures were from running before the isolated worktree had a `harness-core` binary; they passed after it was built.\\n\\nThe hosted PR run’s single failure was also traced to the stale PTY navigation: two Down presses selected OpenAI and sent it the Anthropic fixture key. No full suite was rerun locally.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","create_time":1793026551.835303}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
