{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:03:08.630Z","ordinal":391304,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a178bc-9a56-7a03-9303-223a7074f51b","call_id":"call_2b145aa44451416bb7790b942f67acd2","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed exact head `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa` against base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`. The diff SHA-256 is `586a27e1fec5ccf04a4c6065744717d2ef7ac2452677694cfe32fc245045f3f2`. It touches the intended 16 feature, test, protocol, and TUI files; I did not run tests.\\n\\n1. **TUI Escape does not cancel an in-flight endpoint check.** In [`models.rs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/models.rs:482), Escape returns a cancellation intent only when `auth.is_some()`. Local endpoint discovery has `auth: None` ([`live_state.rs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:621)), so Escape backs out without sending `provider.cancel`. The sidecar can then finish `prepareLocalEndpoint`, activate the provisional endpoint and key, and return after the UI has discarded that request’s setup ID. The existing tests exercise sidecar cancellation directly, but not Escape from the TUI while discovery is pending. Make that Escape path cancel the matching request and add a TUI regression for a late response.\\n\\n2. **Malformed credential-origin metadata can rebind a legacy key.** [`config.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/config.ts:178) treats any nonempty `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGIN` as authoritative when deciding whether to preserve the old endpoint origin. If that value is invalid, [`client.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/client.ts:120) discards it and falls back to the newly written endpoint, binding an existing `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` or gateway token to the new origin. Validate the existing origin before treating it as a prior binding; fail closed or preserve the old endpoint origin when metadata is invalid. Add a malformed-origin regression.\\n\\n3. **The TUI describes the key as already stored before model selection.** [`live_view.rs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3362) says the key is stored during discovery, but the implementation keeps it provisional until selection. Update the prompt to match that lifecycle.\\n\\n4. **Catalog error handling can turn a provider configuration error into a catalog-wide failure.** In [`model_catalog.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/model_catalog.ts:173), the error handler calls `providerConfig` again. If a connected provider has an invalid base URL, that second call throws and rejects `buildCatalog` instead of marking just that provider as errored. Cache identity is only endpoint-specific for the appliance; avoid recomputing cloud provider config in this path and cover an invalid provider URL.\\n\\nThe prior focused evidence does not cover these gaps, and it predates this exact local head. The branch is based on `b73b6ec`; `origin/main` is now `ff349383`, so refresh the candidate and rerun exact-head checks before merge.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","create_time":1793026988.630294}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
