{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:03:21.604Z","ordinal":391310,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf6bb8d38c81a0ad934849f0b3fa94","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"While the Linux job runs, I’m recording the new exact-main CI results and the review disposition in the existing readiness artifact. I’ll keep the candidate findings marked as unresolved until the owner’s fixes are reviewed; the local focused-test results won’t be promoted to release acceptance evidence."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793027000851,"completed_at_ms":1793027001604}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:03:21.611Z","ordinal":391311,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf6bb8d38c81a0ad934849f0b3fa94","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"While the Linux job runs, I’m recording the new exact-main CI results and the review disposition in the existing readiness artifact. I’ll keep the candidate findings marked as unresolved until the owner’s fixes are reviewed; the local focused-test results won’t be promoted to release acceptance evidence.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","create_time":1793027000.8286777,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf6bb8d38c81a0ad934849f0b3fa94","turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a178bc-cd0a-7fe2-bf04-c586c09801d0","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19245}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:03:29.005Z","ordinal":391312,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf6bb9963881a083a14e8a00edb6a8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a2cee6e5843b4da5a89e5b45c28642e7","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md')\\ns=p.read_text()\\nmarker='# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\\\\n'\\nassert s.startswith(marker)\\nblock='''# v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\\n\\n## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 15:02 UTC)\\n\\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is bound to that exact commit: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. The requirements-enforcement and version synchronization checks previously passed on exact `ff349383`; the version remains `1.0.0-rc.8`. Do not call source CI complete until the Linux job terminates successfully.\\n\\n**PR #256 local-provider change:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains at head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`, based on `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`; its exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed the same PTY model-picker test on Node 22 and 24 because the fixture navigated past the newly added Appliance row incorrectly. The owner’s local candidate `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa` was normally updated with current `main` by merge commit `9d898eb`; it is not pushed. Its focused build/test results (105/105) were reported by the implementer on the pre-merge head. Independent review of `0490db3` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with four findings: pending Escape must cancel the matching setup, malformed credential-origin metadata must not rebind legacy keys, provisional-key UI copy is inaccurate, and invalid connected-provider URLs must not fail the entire catalog. The owner reacquired the relevant claims and is implementing regressions; no fixes are yet accepted on the refreshed branch.\\n\\n**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (12:18 UTC). Private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished. No held-out payload was accessed or run. Exact-current-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 remains an older prerelease, not a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\\n\\nThe 14:35 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its current-main CI progress and PR #256 candidate/review status.\\n\\n'''\\ns=s.replace(marker,block,1)\\np.write_text(s)\\nPY\\ngit diff --check && git diff --stat && git log --oneline ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4..HEAD\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:400});\ntext(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","create_time":1793027001.5884147}}}
