{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:11:02.250Z","ordinal":391532,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a178c3-d469-7063-8dad-5599b2cf2e69","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — source review of HEAD `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, based on merge `9d898eb9bb77a87490d6fcf47b11260193b1e315`. Full branch diff SHA-256: `7dc76f1d5d9ee3dd6ebd982eaefc250cd9862043de1f901bf73f58a26d43e376`.\n\nThe four findings are addressed:\n\n- **Cancellation:** Escape sends a matching cancel; the sidecar marks that request cancelled, suppresses its late result, and does not activate or persist its provisional setup. Coverage is in [provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:800) and [live_state.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:4081).\n- **Credential-origin metadata:** malformed nonempty bindings fail closed instead of falling back to the selected endpoint; settings updates also reject them. See [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/client.ts:118), [config.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/config.ts:176), and the regression at [provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:450).\n- **Provisional-key copy:** the TUI now says verification uses the key in memory and it is stored only after model selection ([live_view.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:3362)).\n- **Invalid provider URL:** catalog construction catches the error per provider, preserving other providers’ models ([model_catalog.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/src/model_catalog.ts:167)); the regression checks this and key redaction at [provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/local-endpoint-connect/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:538).\n\nThe local setup paths return generic errors without echoing the endpoint or key; sidecar results are additionally redacted. The picker index correction matches the new Appliance-first list. I did not run tests.\n\n**Merge-status note:** the public branch still resolves to `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`; this reviewed candidate is local and has not yet received exact-head hosted checks."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178aa-5cd4-77e2-b762-b08d50983277","create_time":1793027462.2495549}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19264}}
