6 Oct 24 23:41 FILE_scripts_repro-identity.mjs\ndrwxrwxr-x   2 mike mike   4096 Oct 24 23:37 NEXUS_PACKAGE_TAR_REPRO_20261024\n./cli/test/cloud_providers.test.ts:263:  test(\"redirects are refused on provider connections: the key never follows to another origin\", async () => {\n./nexus-session-session_20261023_134635_z1dnlfek.json:397:      \"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"content\\\": \\\"    1 | # Nexus Code v1.0.0: requirement ledger\\\\n    2 | \\\\n    3 | This is the authoritative v1 ledger (REQ-OPS-101). It supersedes the Issue #12 matrices (`docs/ISSUE12_*.md`) and the phase and work-package documents, which become historical records. All historical commitments are carried forward in §2. None are silently dropped. Each one is either retained, superseded or descoped, with a written disposition.\\\\n    4 | \\\\n    5 | **Status-evidence baseline for this ledger:** `db1ca55` (main, `v0.1.0-alpha.2-2-gdb1ca55`), audited 2026-10-14. A full isolated source-suite run also passed on candidate `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` on 2026-10-16 after `make build`; this does not reclassify behavioral, live, visual, product-qualification, or independent-acceptance statuses. See [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) and [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) for the exact evidence boundary.\\\\n    6 | \\\\n    7 | ## 1. Legend\\\\n    8 | \\\\n    9 | ### Status ladder\\\\n   10 | \\\\n   11 | | Status | Meaning |\\\\n   12 | |---|---|\\\\n   13 | | `open` | Not implemented, or contradicted at HEAD. |\\\\n   14 | | `partial` | Partly implemented, or implemented with a known defect. |\\\\n   15 | | `implemented` | Present in source. Not proven by an automated test of this requirement. |\\\\n   16 | | `tested` | An automated test exercises it and passes at the tested revision (baseline: 905/905 CLI, 266/266 Rust). |\\\\n   17 | | `visually-accepted` | A human or independent PTY review accepted the rendered behaviour. |\\\\n   18 | | `product-qualified` | Passed the v1 qualification in ACCEPTANCE.md on the RC. **No requirement holds this status today.** |\\\\n   19 | \\\\n   20 | Independent acceptance is recorded separately in the \\\\\\\"Indep.\\\\\\\" column: **Y** = an independent review accepted it; **N** = self-assessed only; **—** = not applicable.\\\\n   21 | \\\\n   22 | ### Release classes\\\\n   23 | \\\\n   24 | | Class | Meaning |\\\\n   25 | |---|---|\\\\n   26 | | **B** | BLOCKER. v1.0.0 cannot ship without it. |\\\\n   27 | | **RR** | Release-required. Must be done for v1.0.0; it is not a safety or workflow blocker on its own, but the release gate checks it. |\\\\n   28 | | **P** | Post-v1. |\\\\n   29 | | **K** | Keep: already met; protected by regression tests. |\\\\n   30 | \\\\n   31 | ### Evidence labels\\\\n   32 | \\\\n   33 | | Label | Kind of evidence |\\\\n   34 | |---|---|\\\\n   35 | | SRC | source inspection |\\\\n   36 | | TEST | automated test |\\\\n   37 | | RT | live runtime observation (including PTY) |\\\\n   38 | | MEAS | measurement |\\\\n   39 | | DOC | documentation claim |\\\\n   40 | | HIST | historical or reported evidence |\\\\n   41 | | INF | inference |\\\\n   42 | | UNV | unknown or unverified |\\\\n   43 | \\\\n   44 | ### Links\\\\n   45 | \\\\n   46 | - Findings are defined in [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md).\\\\n   47 | - Specs are in [specs/](specs/), plans in [plans/](plans/), acceptance IDs in [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md).\\\\n   48 | \\\\n   49 | ## 2. Carried-over commitments (REQ-*-0xx)\\\\n   50 | \\\\n   51 | ### 2.1 Retained commitments (already met or partly met; must not regress)\\\\n   52 | \\\\n   53 | | ID | Source | Requirement | Location | Evidence @db1ca55 | Status | Indep. | Open risk | Acceptance | Class | Links |\\\\n   54 | |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\\\n   55 | | REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\\\\n   56 | | REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\\\\n   57 | | REQ-AGT-003 | COMPACTION §B | State-aware repetition and stagnation (action/outcome/state identity; polls vs loops; compaction re-acquisition is not repetition). | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-09 | K | SPEC-04 |\\\\n   58 | | REQ-AGT-004 | COMPACTION §C | Durable compaction commit order archive → task → session (fsync). Failure stops the turn with PERSISTENCE_FAILED. Queued `/compact`. | `agent.ts:3070-3153` | TEST (`test:cli/test/durable_continuity.test.ts::\\\\\\\"ACC-CONT-03: pressure compaction of a work unit survives SIGKILL and restores archived markers\\\\\\\"`, `compaction_continuity.test.ts:533`); HIST 1 live run | tested | Y (source/CI incl. M1/M3/L5 in PR #25; see `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/INDEP-REVIEW-CONTINUITY/dispositions.md`) | Live long-task ACC-CONT-10 pending M5 instal