{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:00:34.861Z","ordinal":392809,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178d5-a588-7873-8790-fb703eb53a02","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7921d19c81a0bdbd0b4c67103423","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Confirmed: **RC7 rejected GitHub’s signed release-asset redirect**. The URL was valid; RC7’s allowlist simply didn’t include that host. RC7 also exposed the signed query string in its error.\n\nThis is fixed in **RC8**: its downloader allows only GitHub release-asset paths on that host, and its errors redact signed query strings. I verified RC8 is published and its source includes the fix and a regression test. [RC8 release](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8)\n\nIf `nexus -V` still reports RC6, retry on mike-dev with `nexus upgrade --version 1.0.0-rc.8`. The failed attempt appears to have stopped during download, after making the backup; I can’t verify remotely whether RC6 remains active. RC8 is still a prerelease, and acceptance remains in progress."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793030433859,"completed_at_ms":1793030434861}}
