{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:19:16.604Z","ordinal":393228,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17902-4dfc-7f73-bbcc-e32f5a4c79e2","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed HEAD `cfee7f561540b5e9e02f03f540614c5efcdb4b35` against base `33f7685e6e333b7a3d30cb15498357f7cd45dd4c`. Diff SHA-256: `1e7a8414b112d895345b14a7e27b9d7769428df6c904cde09ff8ef0f23061fe1`.\n\nThe fix preserves `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGIN` when resolving an operator key ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/client.ts:182)); `buildConfig` passes that origin through, and the client sends the explicit key only when the request origin matches it ([config.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/config.ts:320), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/client.ts:988)). The regression covers the persisted origin after changing endpoints, confirms the old key remains bound to the old origin, and makes an actual request to the replacement endpoint that must carry only the placeholder credential ([provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:431)).\n\nNo remaining credential-rebinding issue found. This was source review only; I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793031556.6042244}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19365}}
