thub.list_pr_changed_filenames"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_pr_diff"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","cyber_access_program":"standard","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","turn_trigger":"user"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7bc9b90881a0b9a899df70ca6007","order":19351,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a178fb-8f96-7c93-a19d-86576ca042ec","text":"PR #256 and the RC9 version-preparation PR #257 are both merged. The authoritative `main` is now `33f7685`; its CI and CodeQL are still running, so I’m keeping the suite lane clear. I also confirmed the held-out evaluator still rejects the sealed legacy corpus for qualification, and the custodian has not replied to the latest metadata request.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7bf3b55481a0a4d94d0b013b019d","order":19352,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a178fc-32a8-71f2-a970-faae27815e9e","text":"While main’s exact commit checks finish, I’m doing an isolated check of the already-published RC8 installer artifact itself. This verifies whether the redirect fix is actually present in the downloadable package, rather than relying only on the source tag.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7c0c454881a08521e2541541f90e","order":19353,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a178fc-932e-7722-902a-e4302b6c8d99","text":"RC8’s published Linux artifact hash matches GitHub’s digest, and the extracted CLI reports `1.0.0-rc.8`. Its packaged `upgrade.js` contains both the restricted signed-asset redirect rule and redacted error formatting. That confirms the fix is in the downloadable artifact; it does not qualify RC8 or substitute for testing the next exact RC.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7cab1cfc81a08811e8e16c1da54e","order":19357,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a178fe-feeb-71a3-9bf4-8bc68a58a2d1","text":"The exact-main checks have advanced: both Node 22 and Node 24 matrices now pass, and CodeQL passes on `33f7685`. The Linux packaging/reproducibility job is still running, so source-gate completion and RC9 construction remain pending that result.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7cb6590481a08e211c07b74db2f3","order":19358,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a178ff-2b32-74e0-bb9b-c54e6d234b13","text":"I’m checking whether the Ubuntu desktop is reachable through its previously supplied address so I can stage the human terminal matrix as soon as RC9 is available. This is only a read-only session and installed-terminal check; I won’t launch Nexus or record qualification results without the exact RC artifact.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7d38eba881a0a0c9f7d0997f2802","order":19360,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17901-2a78-74a2-83c9-2d10c2813731","text":"The release check uncovered a more serious issue before RC9 tagging: an independent probe found PR #256’s credential-origin handling can send a previously configured key to a newly selected endpoint. The exact-main CI run is still active, but a green result alone would not clear this defect. I’m checking the owner’s remediation branch and review state; I will keep RC9 gated until that fix is independently accepted and retested on the integrated revision.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7d6f239c81a0a94609c42b9fdc2d","order":19363,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17901-fd83-7250-bb4f-b863680223c5","text":"I caught an important versioning detail: the upgrade command was executed by the installed **RC6** binary, so RC6—not only the RC7 target—must be checked as the code that rejected the redirect. I’m verifying the RC6 tag now and will correct the diagnosis if its downloader also lacks the allowlist.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf7d79490081a0b74d320b88ce382d","order":19364,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17902-2448-75d0-ae13-4ec301754c44","text":"Correction: your command was running **RC6**, so RC6’s updater rejected the signed redirect and printed the full URL. RC7’s source also lacks that fix; RC8 is the first published release I verified with the restricted redirect allowlist and redacted diagnostics. The RC8 package hash and version check passed in an isolated download.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19367,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questio