{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:20:47.051Z","ordinal":393289,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17903-af4b-7d82-b67f-4921350ebea8","call_id":"call_cdd573c5390944458efbb6506fe86ca7","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Completed the four review remediations in local commit `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, after merging `origin/main` at `ff349383` normally. The worktree is clean, claims are released, and I requested independent re-review. No push or main merge was made.\\n\\nFocused validation passed: Node 33/33, TUI Rust tests 6/6, TypeScript build, and `git diff --check`. The Rust formatting check found existing broad formatting drift; I left unrelated formatting untouched.\\n\\nFull diff SHA-256 against `origin/main`: `a2b36f2aeb3637e7ab82831cd4c51d1d51c5ac4c919d4aaac5d3b4ee023b7199`.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed HEAD `cfee7f561540b5e9e02f03f540614c5efcdb4b35` against base `33f7685e6e333b7a3d30cb15498357f7cd45dd4c`. Diff SHA-256: `1e7a8414b112d895345b14a7e27b9d7769428df6c904cde09ff8ef0f23061fe1`.\\n\\nThe fix preserves `LOCAL_LLM_CREDENTIAL_ORIGIN` when resolving an operator key ([client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/client.ts:182)); `buildConfig` passes that origin through, and the client sends the explicit key only when the request origin matches it ([config.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/config.ts:320), [client.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/src/client.ts:988)). The regression covers the persisted origin after changing endpoints, confirms the old key remains bound to the old origin, and makes an actual request to the replacement endpoint that must carry only the placeholder credential ([provider_connect.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc9-credential-origin-binding/cli/test/provider_connect.test.ts:431)).\\n\\nNo remaining credential-rebinding issue found. This was source review only; I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793031647.051249}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
