t preflight at source `8f4504e` recorded 10/10 checks and is being documented in PR #102. Neither source fixtures nor the synthetic-host report establish access separation against the custodian's real store or permit held-out execution before custody acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:304:  - **Distinction of evidence:** Independent public metadata review (`codex-lead`) verified and accepted the committed manifest digest (`50895b84…`), 40 unique task IDs, 10×4 class/language balance, 40 full pinned commits, and schema/digest fields without inspecting private payloads. Private payload validation (2 rounds per task in bounded `SUITE` windows: fresh clone → checkout → setup → pre-patch regression pass → pre-patch hidden fail → reference patch apply → post-patch hidden pass → post-patch regression pass), rejection/quarantine of one provenance-contaminated batch (`author-b9` at `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`), per-session exec-log audits for clean replacement authors (`author-b8c`, `author-b9c`), and store access tightening (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` mode `0700`, `tasks/` and `reference/` mode `0500` read-only) are custodian-attested in `custody-report-2026-10-18.md`. Earlier author-exposed packages (`v12`, `v15`, `v16`, `v17`, `v18`) recorded in historical sections below are superseded development/pilot artifacts and are never used for held-out qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:307:  - Repository workspace history isolation (`96aeef2`, PR #18, `eval/workspace.mjs`) stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`) without `--shared`, `objects/info/alternates`, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits, preventing candidates from reading upstream fix commits in git history.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:308:  - Kernel-enforced resource contract (`91406bd`, PR #19, `eval/resources.mjs`, `eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs`, `scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh`) executes each task phase (setup, candidate sandbox, hidden/regression, oracle) inside a transient delegated `systemd --user` scope with verified cgroup v2 `CPUQuota`, `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, `TasksMax`, `memory.oom.group=1`, dedicated size-capped tmpfs `workspaceRoot` storage enforcement, and `cgroup.kill` process-tree cleanup verified to `populated == 0`. These controls are source-implemented, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152` on `0cee0b7`, run `39104943950`), not live qualification results. Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` account, narrow sudoers rule, dedicated tmpfs mount, and frozen `config.resources` profile) remains a prerequisite before running held-out T2/T3/T4 workloads.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:390:| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:400:| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:403:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:94:- **Hidden-test isolation.** Private validators and expected answers must remain outside every task process's readable namespace. A task workspace may contain only its permitted baseline and task inputs; evaluation of private expectations must be performed outside that task boundary. Corpus custody and evaluator execution isolation are separate acceptance gates: the custodian's sealed-store disposition does not establish that the runner prevents task processes from reading validators. On the current integration candidate, evaluator-boundary acceptance remains open; PR #33 is not qualified for held-out use until the actual workspace-construction and execution path demonstrates this boundary and passes independent review. Do not use filesystem ownership of the custodian store as a substitute for validating the task-process boundary.\ncli/test/recover_worktree_conversation.test.ts:152:    assert.equal(checkpoint.workspacePath, fixture.primary, \"checkpoint recorded the worktree as the task workspace\");\ncli/test/eval_hardened.test.ts:276:  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"Cargo.toml\", cargo, cargo.replace('serde = \"1\"', 'serde = { path = \"../s\" }')) ?? \"\", /local, git or alternate-registry source/);\ncli/test/eval_hardened.test.ts:550:  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"Cargo.toml\", cargo, cargo.replace('serde = \"1\"', 'serde = { version = \"1\", registry = \"evil\" }')) ?? \"\", /alternate-registry/);\ncli/test/eval_host_bubblewrap.test.ts:2: * Qualification-host preflight rejects Bubblewrap releases affected by CVE-2026-87766 (eval