EADME.md:49:A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:57:populated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\ncli/src/sidecar.ts:1092:    .option(\"--sandbox [mode]\", \"Isolate command execution using bubblewrap or Docker\")\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh:6:  local cgroup_root=\"${NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT:-/sys/fs/cgroup}\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh:21:    process_file=\"${cgroup_root%/}${control_group}/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh:29:  # A stopped, loaded unit with no remaining cgroup has no processes. An\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh:30:  # active unit with missing/unreadable cgroup data is an unknown measurement.\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:4:# The sandbox requires --disable-userns. Ubuntu 22.04's bubblewrap 0.6.1 predates\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:8:readonly SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/containers/bubblewrap/releases/download/v0.13.1/bubblewrap-0.13.1.tar.xz\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:16:  [[ \"$version_output\" =~ bubblewrap[[:space:]]+([0-9]+)\\.([0-9]+)\\.([0-9]+) ]] || return 1\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:29:work=\"$(mktemp -d \"${RUNNER_TEMP:-${TMPDIR:-/tmp}}/nexus-bubblewrap.XXXXXX\")\"\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:31:archive=\"$work/bubblewrap-0.13.1.tar.xz\"\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:36:meson setup \"$work/build\" \"$work/bubblewrap-0.13.1\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:9:mkdir -p \"$tmp/bin\" \"$tmp/cgroup/user.slice/test.scope\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:25:export PATH FIXTURE_STATE_DIR=\"$tmp/state\" NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT=\"$tmp/cgroup\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:46:: > \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:48:printf '101\\n202\\n' > \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:51:python3 -c 'import os,sys; os.unlink(sys.argv[1])' \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:53:: > \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:54:chmod 000 \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:56:chmod 600 \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:57:printf 'not-a-pid\\n' > \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:59:python3 -c 'import os,sys; os.unlink(sys.argv[1])' \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:60:mkdir \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:62:python3 -c 'import os,sys; os.rmdir(sys.argv[1])' \"$NEXUS_CGROUP_ROOT/user.slice/test.scope/cgroup.procs\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:118:# Each launch runs in its own transient systemd …2222 tokens truncated…f [\"\", undefined, \"bubblewrap 0.12\", \"bwrap 0.13.1\", \"bubblewrap 0.13.1-rc1\", \"bubblewrap 0.13.1\\nbubblewrap 0.9.0\"]) {\ncli/test/eval_host_bubblewrap.test.ts:24:    assert.match(bubblewrapVersionProblem(output), /unrecognized Bubblewrap version output/, String(output));\ncore/src/bin/nexus_tui/live.rs:310:/// Restores the terminal on every exit path. ratatui's panic hook restores raw mode and the alternate screen\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.m