{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:38:42.514Z","ordinal":394652,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-eebf81b5-4c01-4abb-b734-4a9050c7230f","process_id":"23958","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,180p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md; find scripts/terminal-acceptance -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f\\n' | sort; rg -n \"REQ-QUAL-108|15 cells|xterm|kitty|GNOME Terminal|VS Code terminal|ACCEPTANCE §5\\.3|Acceptance.*5\\.3\" docs/v1.0.0 docs scripts/terminal-acceptance | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find scripts/terminal-acceptance -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf \"%f\\\\n\"","path":"terminal-acceptance"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"REQ-QUAL-108|15 cells|xterm|kitty|GNOME Terminal|VS Code terminal|ACCEPTANCE §5\\\\.3|Acceptance.*5\\\\.3\" docs/v1.0.0 docs scripts/terminal-acceptance","query":"REQ-QUAL-108|15 cells|xterm|kitty|GNOME Terminal|VS Code terminal|ACCEPTANCE §5\\.3|Acceptance.*5\\.3","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\nREADME.md\nmockgw.py\nrun-cell.sh\nscope-procs.sh\nsummarize.mjs\ntest-scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:1:# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:5:**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:6:- xterm\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:7:- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:8:- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:10:- GNOME Terminal\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:24:Open the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:28:scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py:2:\"\"\"Deterministic OpenAI-compatible mock for the manual terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3).\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:99:for (const terminal of [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"]) {\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:107:      scopeMeasurement: process.env.MODE === \"unavailable\" && cell === \"xterm-80x24\" && launch === \"main\" ? \"unavailable\" : \"verified\",\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:136:printf '%s\\n' '{}' > \"$tmp/evidence/cell-xterm-80x24.attempt-not-a-number.json\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:137:printf '%s\\n' '{}' > \"$tmp/evidence/cell-xterm-80x24.attempt-2.json.backup\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh:140:grep -q '^| xterm-80x24 | 1 | PASS | PASS' \"$tmp/verified-summary.log\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs:2:// Gate for the manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3) over the attempt records written by run-cell.sh.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs:18:const TERMINALS = [\"xterm\", \"kitty\", \"tmux-gnome\", \"vscode\", \"gnome\"];\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs:101:console.log(`\\nREQ-QUAL-108 manual matrix gate for ${rc} (package manifest ${manifestSha.slice(0, 12)}): ${verdict}`);\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:2:# One cell of the manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3), run by a human INSIDE the terminal under test, sized\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:9:#   scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc v1.0.0-rc.N --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:27:[[ \"$terminal\" =~ ^(xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome)$ ]] || { echo \"--terminal must be xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:52:  xterm) [[ -n \"${XTERM_VERSION:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"XTERM_VERSION unset or inside tmux: not xterm\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:53:  kitty) [[ -n \"${KITTY_WINDOW_ID:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID unset or inside tmux: not kitty\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:55:  gnome) [[ -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN/SERVICE unset or inside tmux: not GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:57:    [[ -n \"${TMUX:-}\" && -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" ]] || { echo \"run inside tmux inside GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:60:kitty_protocol=\"\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:61:if [[ \"$terminal\" == kitty ]]; then\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:62:  read -r -p \"Is the kitty keyboard protocol enabled for this window? (yes/no) \" kitty_protocol\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:63:  [[ \"$kitty_protocol\" == yes ]] || { echo \"enable the kitty keyboard protocol first\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:193:KITTY_PROTOCOL=\"$kitty_protocol\" OPERATOR_NAME=\"$operator\" STEM=\"$stem\" APPROVAL_SHOT=\"$approval_copy\" EXIT_SHOT=\"$exit_copy\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:217:    \"acceptance\": \"ACCEPTANCE §5.3\", \"cell\": e[\"CELL\"], \"attempt\": int(e[\"ATTEMPT\"]), \"terminal\": e[\"TERMINAL_NAME\"], \"size\": e[\"CELL_SIZE\"],\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:221:    \"tmux\": e[\"TMUX_VERSION\"] or None, \"kittyKeyboardProtocol\": e[\"KITTY_PROTOCOL\"] or None,\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:99:- **Terminal evidence** comes from `pyte` emulation plus the repository's PTY suites. Real emulators (kitty keyboard protocol, tmux, VS Code) were not exercised.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:116:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:130:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:234:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:254:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:270:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:280:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:290:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:391:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:36:| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3. Archive screenshots. | ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:68:- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:99:- **Terminal evidence** comes from `pyte` emulation plus the repository's PTY suites. Real emulators (kitty keyboard protocol, tmux, VS Code) were not exercised.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMI