SS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:63:| 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | | | |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:67:- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:69:- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict and both required screenshots are referenced: [ ] yes  [ ] no\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:116:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:130:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed