{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:45:16.302Z","ordinal":394908,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17951-090e-78d2-b4dd-cabc6ae15e08","call_id":"call_6100009282f9445f87580cb1f57e9840","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Completed the four review remediations in local commit `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, after merging `origin/main` at `ff349383` normally. The worktree is clean, claims are released, and I requested independent re-review. No push or main merge was made.\\n\\nFocused validation passed: Node 33/33, TUI Rust tests 6/6, TypeScript build, and `git diff --check`. The Rust formatting check found existing broad formatting drift; I left unrelated formatting untouched.\\n\\nFull diff SHA-256 against `origin/main`: `a2b36f2aeb3637e7ab82831cd4c51d1d51c5ac4c919d4aaac5d3b4ee023b7199`.\\n\\n\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #259 at head `782b737796ed5c4004fedee57a9b8b969559f1e4`, based on `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. The reviewed diff SHA-256 is `938215d0cd0f3ed6d0000a16af6e1a2a5d2a7ea7fd8b02848ba44e9c90f02d30`.\\n\\nThe current checkpoint’s CI, CodeQL, PR #258, and RC8 release claims match the available records. It clearly leaves RC9 untagged and acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`; custody, exact-RC qualification, and the human terminal matrix remain gated. Earlier snapshots are preserved; the only historical edit relabels the former top checkpoint as historical. `git diff --check` is clean. No changes required.\\n\\n\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793036716.3022597}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
