{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:54:17.680Z","ordinal":395340,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c1d8c592-aef8-4b3a-8e1d-cd53552fb3b8","process_id":"58806","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"install.sh|INSTALL_DIR|--version|install.*RC|terminal-acceptance/run-cell\" /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/README.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/USER_MANUAL.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh | head -n 80; sed -n '1,180p' /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'install.sh|INSTALL_DIR|--version|install.*RC|terminal-acceptance/run-cell' /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/README.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/USER_MANUAL.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh","query":"install.sh|INSTALL_DIR|--version|install.*RC|terminal-acceptance/run-cell","path":"README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' /tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh","name":"install.sh","path":"/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:16:[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:92:    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:150:  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:203:\"$LINK\" --version\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/README.md:17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:115:| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:231:  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:273:| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:322:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:83:nexus upgrade --version v1.0.0\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:289:| `/upgrade [--check\\|--version <v>\\|--yes]` | Check for updates or safely upgrade to the latest stable or pinned release with deliberate approval |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:383:- **Build Identity**: `nexus --version` and `nexus doctor` show the commit the running build was made from, its branch, and whether the source had uncommitted changes (`1.2.1 (cc177be91d15-dirty, feat/tui-surface)`), recorded at `make build`.\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\n\nREPO=mikeholownych/nexus-code\nBASE=${NEXUS_RELEASE_BASE_URL:-\"https://github.com/$REPO/releases\"}\nVERSION=${NEXUS_VERSION:-latest}\nPREFIX=${NEXUS_PREFIX:-\"$HOME/.local\"}\n\nfail() { printf 'nexus installer: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncase \"$(uname -s):$(uname -m)\" in\n  Linux:x86_64|Linux:amd64) ;;\n  *) fail \"unsupported system $(uname -s)/$(uname -m); supported: Linux x86-64 (glibc).\" ;;\nesac\ncommand -v node >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required; install Node.js and retry.\"\nNODE_MAJOR=$(node -p 'Number(process.versions.node.split(\".\")[0])' 2>/dev/null || printf 0)\n[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\ncommand -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"curl is required.\"\ncommand -v tar >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"tar is required.\"\ncommand -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1 || fail \"sha256sum is required.\"\n\nVERIFY_ATTESTATION=${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}\ncase \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" in\n  auto|0|1) ;;\n  *) fail \"NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION must be auto (verify when a trusted GitHub CLI is present), 1 (require verification) or 0 (skip verification).\" ;;\nesac\nTRUSTED_GH=\nif [ -x /usr/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/bin/gh\nelif [ -x /usr/local/bin/gh ]; then\n  TRUSTED_GH=/usr/local/bin/gh\nfi\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ] && [ -z \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  fail \"provenance attestation is required (NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1) but no trusted GitHub CLI was found at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; install gh or set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0.\"\nfi\n\nvalidate_tag() {\n  printf '%s' \"$1\" | grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[-0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$' || fail \"version must be a release tag like v1.2.3 or v1.2.3-alpha.1 (got: $1).\"\n}\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" != \"latest\" ]; then\n  validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\nfi\n\nif [ \"$VERSION\" = \"latest\" ]; then\n  API_BASE=${NEXUS_RELEASES_API:-\"https://api.github.com/repos/$REPO/releases\"}\n  API_TMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-api.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\n  api_cleanup() { rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"; }\n  trap api_cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\n\n  LATEST_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -D \"$API_TMP/headers\" -o \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE/latest\" 2>\"$API_TMP/curl.err\" || echo \"000\")\n\n  if [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n    VERSION=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/latest.json\" | head -n 1)\n    [ -n \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"GitHub returned no stable release tag.\"\n    validate_tag \"$VERSION\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"403\" ]; then\n    if grep -qiE 'x-ratelimit-remaining:[[:space:]]*0' \"$API_TMP/headers\" 2>/dev/null; then\n      fail \"GitHub API rate limit exceeded; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup, or set GITHUB_TOKEN.\"\n    fi\n    fail \"GitHub API returned HTTP 403; set NEXUS_VERSION=vX to bypass the release lookup.\"\n  elif [ \"$LATEST_CODE\" = \"404\" ]; then\n    PREREL_CODE=$(curl -sSL --show-error -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github+json' -o \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" -w \"%{http_code}\" \"$API_BASE?per_page=1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"000\")\n    if [ \"$PREREL_CODE\" = \"200\" ]; then\n      PREREL_TAG=$(sed -n 's/.*\"tag_name\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\"\\([^\"]*\\)\".*/\\1/p' \"$API_TMP/releases.json\" | head -n 1)\n      if [ -n \"$PREREL_TAG\" ]; then\n        fail \"no stable release yet; latest prerelease is $PREREL_TAG — rerun with NEXUS_VERSION=$PREREL_TAG\"\n      fi\n    fi\n    fail \"could not find latest stable release (HTTP 404 from $API_BASE/latest).\"\n  else\n    fail \"could not query GitHub releases API (HTTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  else\n    printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: %s could not verify the attestation (it may need gh auth login); the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' \"$TRUSTED_GH\" >&2\n  fi\nelif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"auto\" ]; then\n  printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: no trusted GitHub CLI at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' >&2\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":43312}},"started_at_ms":1793037257679,"completed_at_ms":1793037257680}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:54:19.043Z","ordinal":395341,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17959-5122-7d12-a8e8-2cd36ca30a3e","call_id":"call_4192acc2a568476eb36f08f9959ba26d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5459)\nTotal output lines: 207\n\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:16:[ \"$NODE_MAJOR\" -ge 22 ] || fail \"Node.js 22 or newer is required (found $(node --version 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)).\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:92:    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:150:  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/install.sh:203:\"$LINK\" --version\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/README.md:17:curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | sh\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:18:A gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:26:3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:28:5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:34:The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n/tmp/nexus-rc9-postmerge-source-gates-4cae11c/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in …2459 tokens truncated…TTP $LATEST_CODE); network failure or host unreachable.\"\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$API_TMP\"\n  trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM\nfi\n\nARCHIVE=\"nexus-linux-x86_64-$VERSION.tar.gz\"\nNORMALIZED_VERSION=${VERSION#v}\nURL=\"$BASE/download/$VERSION\"\nTMP=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-install.XXXXXX\") || fail \"could not create temporary directory.\"\ncleanup() { rm -rf \"$TMP\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT HUP INT TERM\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/$ARCHIVE\" -o \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" || fail \"download failed for $ARCHIVE.\"\ncurl -fsSL --show-error --retry 2 \"$URL/SHA256SUMS\" -o \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" || fail \"could not download release checksums.\"\ngrep -F \"  $ARCHIVE\" \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" > \"$TMP/expected.sha256\" || fail \"checksum entry for $ARCHIVE is missing.\"\n(cd \"$TMP\" && sha256sum --check --status expected.sha256) || fail \"SHA-256 verification failed; no installation was changed.\"\nARCHIVE_SHA256=$(sha256sum \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" | awk '{print $1}')\n\nif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" != \"0\" ] && [ -n \"$TRUSTED_GH\" ]; then\n  if \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n     \"$TRUSTED_GH\" attestation verify \"$TMP/SHA256SUMS\" -R \"$REPO\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    printf 'nexus installer: verified build provenance for %s and its checksum index\\n' \"$ARCHIVE\"\n  elif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"1\" ]; then\n    fail \"provenance attestation verification failed for $ARCHIVE or SHA256SUMS.\"\n  else\n    printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: %s could not verify the attestation (it may need gh auth login); the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' \"$TRUSTED_GH\" >&2\n  fi\nelif [ \"$VERIFY_ATTESTATION\" = \"auto\" ]; then\n  printf 'nexus installer: build provenance was not verified: no trusted GitHub CLI at /usr/bin/gh or /usr/local/bin/gh; the SHA-256 checksum was verified. Set NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 to require provenance.\\n' >&2\nfi\n\nVERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"\nBIN_DIR=\"$PREFIX/bin\"\nLINK=\"$BIN_DIR/nexus\"\nmkdir -p \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus\" \"$BIN_DIR\"\nif [ -e \"$LINK\" ] && [ ! -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  fail \"$LINK exists and is not a symlink; left it unchanged.\"\nfi\nif [ -L \"$LINK\" ]; then\n  OLD=$(readlink \"$LINK\")\n  case \"$OLD\" in \"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/\"*) ;; *) fail \"$LINK points outside the Nexus installation; left it unchanged.\" ;; esac\nfi\n\nFORCE=${NEXUS_FORCE:-0}\nNEEDS_EXTRACT=1\nif [ -d \"$VERSION_DIR\" ] && [ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" ]; then\n  if [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/bin/nexus\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && \\\n     [ -x \"$VERSION_DIR/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && \\\n     [ \"$(cat \"$VERSION_DIR/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ]; then\n    if [ -f \"$VERSION_DIR/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n      if (cd \"$VERSION_DIR\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256 2>/dev/null); then\n        NEEDS_EXTRACT=0\n      fi\n      if [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"0\" ]; then\n        if ! node - \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, archiveSha256] = process.argv.slice(2);\ntry {\n  const record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\n  if (record.archiveSha256 !== archiveSha256) process.exit(1);\n} catch { process.exit(1); }\nNODE\n        then\n          NEEDS_EXTRACT=1\n        fi\n      fi\n    fi\n  fi\nfi\n\nif [ \"$NEEDS_EXTRACT\" = \"1\" ]; then\n  mkdir -p \"$TMP/unpack\"\n  tar -xzf \"$TMP/$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/unpack\" || fail \"archive extraction failed.\"\n  PACKAGE=\"$TMP/unpack/nexus\"\n  [ -x \"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/harness-core\" ] && [ -x \"$PACKAGE/lib/core/nexus-tui\" ] && [ \"$(cat \"$PACKAGE/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null || true)\" = \"$VERSION\" ] || fail \"release archive is incomplete or has a mismatched version.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/MANIFEST.sha256\" ]; then\n    (cd \"$PACKAGE\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || fail \"release archive failed manifest checksum verification.\"\n  fi\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT=$(\"$PACKAGE/bin/nexus\" --version 2>&1) || fail \"release binary failed its pre-install self-test.\"\n  PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED=$(printf '%s\\n' \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_OUTPUT\" | sed -n '1s/[[:space:]].*$//p')\n  [ \"$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED\" = \"$NORMALIZED_VERSION\" ] || fail \"release binary reported version '$PACKAGE_VERSION_REPORTED' instead of '$NORMALIZED_VERSION' during self-test.\"\n  if [ -f \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" ]; then\n    node - \"$PACKAGE/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$ARCHIVE\" <<'NODE' || fail \"release compatibility metadata is invalid or mismatched.\"\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [file, version, archive] = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\"));\nconst asset = data.platforms?.[\"linux-x86_64\"];\nconst compatible = data.schemaVersion === 1 && data.product === \"nexus-code\" &&\n  data.version === version.replace(/^v/, \"\") &&\n  typeof data.revision === \"string\" && /^[a-f0-9]{7,64}$/i.test(data.revision) &&\n  typeof data.builtAt === \"string\" && !Number.isNaN(Date.parse(data.builtAt)) &&\n  asset?.archive === archive && asset.os === \"linux\" && asset.arch === \"x86_64\" &&\n  data.compatibility && Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion) &&\n  Number.isSafeInteger(data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion) &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedConfigVersion <= data.compatibility.configSchemaVersion &&\n  data.compatibility.minSupportedStateVersion <= data.compatibility.stateSchemaVersion;\nif (!compatible) process.exit(1);\nNODE\n  fi\n  rm -rf \"$VERSION_DIR\"\n  mv \"$PACKAGE\" \"$VERSION_DIR\"\nfi\nnode - \"$VERSION_DIR/compatibility.json\" \"$VERSION\" \"$PREFIX\" \"$VERSION_DIR\" \"$LINK\" \"$ARCHIVE\" \"$ARCHIVE_SHA256\" \"$VERSION_DIR/.provenance.json\" <<'NODE'\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst [metadataPath, version, prefix, installedPath, binPath, archive, archiveSha256, output] = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet metadata = null;\ntry { metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, \"utf8\")); } catch {}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037259.0428572}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
