{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:54:56.854Z","ordinal":395385,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17959-e4d6-7a33-aa98-02ecae3441df","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for exact head `d508e1998d879dc4e0005b8c6a0cc3e2ccc2bda1` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. Diff SHA-256 matches the requested `ab494c7bf2a97bc50e5142caa49e2d2efd60618d6be11ff76f374e88a9a69ca5`.\n\n- At [READINESS.md:9](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9), the RC9 workflow is described as running `npm --prefix cli test`. Live run `40370485753` is instead in progress at `scripts/package-linux.sh ...`. Update the active step.\n- GitHub’s tag metadata reports the RC9 signature as unverified with reason `bad_email`. “Signed tag” is technically supported by the tag object, but clarify that GitHub has not verified it; don’t let the wording imply verified provenance.\n\nThe release list confirms RC8 is still the latest published prerelease, and the RC9 build has no published release assets. The checkpoint keeps acceptance gated. Earlier snapshots are preserved, and the diff passes `git diff --check`.\n\nThe RC8 session section labels its claims operator-reported and explicitly says `NOT_ESTABLISHED`; I found no public record for that session export to independently verify its classification. Its limited evidentiary role is stated accurately."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037296.8540168}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19479}}
