{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:56:06.860Z","ordinal":395437,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9435e87881a0bf87efa639c25dbf","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The latest checks confirm RC9’s tag signature verifies both locally and on GitHub; its package workflow is still running, now at package smoke tests. PR #259’s independent reviewer identified two factual updates needed in the readiness checkpoint. The Ubuntu desktop already has the required five terminals and a GNOME screenshot portal, so I’m checking whether the portal can serve as the evidence capture path before updating that checkpoint and re-running review/checks."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793037366143,"completed_at_ms":1793037366859}}
