{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:56:17.420Z","ordinal":395449,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-16367b30-0903-44be-b947-603994f2fea3","process_id":"73453","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '17:52|Signed tag|smoke|screenshot|RC9|5 terminals|terminal' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -35; sed -n '1,180p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md; tail -130 docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n '17:52|Signed tag|smoke|screenshot|RC9|5 terminals|terminal' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -35; sed -n '1,180p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md; tail -130 docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"173:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\n177:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n183:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n185:**Human terminal matrix:** The required environments remain xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with the two required screenshots for each cell. This coordination session is on `mike-dev`, an Ubuntu 24.04 remote TTY with no active display; it has tmux 3.4 and Xvfb but not the other terminal applications. Xvfb and PTY evidence do not satisfy the manual gate. The operator selected an Ubuntu/GNOME desktop as the target, but a direct SSH probe failed because `ubuntu-desktop` does not resolve from this runner and no desktop host is connected. The worksheet remains unfilled; no terminal cell is claimed passed. Matrix execution still requires the exact candidate artifact selected for qualification, installed and identified on that desktop.\n191:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n195:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\n197:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n205:**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\n209:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n215:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n227:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n231:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n241:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n251:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n259:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, PR #140's merge commit. Exact-main CI [39747222866](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222866) passed all four jobs on that exact SHA: Node 20, 22, 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging, including the CLI suite and package smoke check. Exact-main CodeQL [39747222840](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39747222840) passed. PR #140's host report is synthetic-only: 10/10 infrastructure checks passed and independent review accepted it; it does not establish held-out qualification.\n265:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n291:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n312:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n327:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n334:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\n337:- **Qualification host and terminal:** Qualification-host tooling is integrated through PR #31 (`8c0ab7b`), but this checkpoint has no evidence that the qualification host was provisioned and validated at `4bce876`. Terminal acceptance procedure is integrated; the required human matrix remains unexecuted. It requires five environments × three sizes on the exact installed RC, with per-cell PASS/FAIL and screenshots of the approval panel and post-exit state.\n338:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\n344:- **Authoritative integration and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`. The earlier reported `2c70d39` and `d2c4bfc` are ancestors of this revision; they are not competing integration heads. PR #9 and PR #23 are integrated as `64ee88b` and `886766b`; PR #24's terminal acceptance kit is integrated at `5193984`. Exact-head integration CI run [39120013759](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39120013759) is in progress, so there is no current-head green claim yet. PR #24's checks passed on its exact head `91eaee9` in run [39117464186](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39117464186); its accepted procedure does not replace the human terminal matrix.\n350:- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\n355:- **Authoritative integration revision and CI:** `origin/v1/integration` is at `a7126aa811044b45357440b5aee9228500a480a8` (draft PR [#8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/8) targeting `main`). GitHub Actions CI run [39108774170](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39108774170) on `a7126aa` completed with **success** across all five jobs (`cloudflare-contest-contract`, `test-matrix (20)`, `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64`: Rust 281/281, CLI 1,152/1,152 with 0 skipped, security gates, deterministic double-build packaging, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke). Source CI is green; installed-RC product qualification has not yet executed.\n420:- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n421:- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n444:| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n446:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n457:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n458:| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n467:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n484:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n489:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n501:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n- This full pass supersedes neither the real pre-fix failure on `bb8e673` (1,097 passed, 7 failed) nor its history. The intentionally interrupted pre-correction run remains classified as interrupted. The package leak and parser edge cases were fixed before this corrected run; tests were not skipped or relaxed.\n- At 07:40 UTC, PR #10 checks were run `39014385063` on `4439b7e` and PR #9 checks were run `39012957463` on `6220e14`; superseded runs `39010821988`, `39010709839`, and `39006853703` were cancelled after newer commits replaced their heads.\n\n## Historical evidence: Node 20 full-suite follow-up (2026-10-17 07:13 UTC)\n\n- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\n- A four-file follow-up in the PR #10 worktree avoids exposing external launcher paths in packaged doctor evidence and recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries while rejecting zero-test, all-skipped, and cancelled-only summaries. The cancelled-only edge case was found during independent review and fixed before acceptance; the reviewer accepted the corrected parser/test diff. Build succeeded, the focused four-file selection passed **47/47**, staged `git diff --check` passed, and staged Gitleaks found zero findings.\n- One full-suite attempt on the pre-correction working tree was intentionally interrupted after review found the cancelled-only edge case. It is classified as interrupted, not passed or failed. The prior 1,097/7 result remains historical evidence and is not erased.\n\n## Historical evidence: Release validation update (2026-10-17 06:40 UTC)\n\n- A focused Node 20.20.2 run of `npm --prefix cli test -- test/security_gates.test.ts` against PR #10's pre-fix snapshot reproduced an SBOM test failure: nested `npx` exited with `ENOENT` for the absent `cli/lib` directory after inheriting npm's `npm_config_local_prefix` and `npm_config_prefix`. A prior supplemental command labeled Node 20 was invalid because `node` resolved to Node 24; it is not counted as Node 20 evidence.\n- PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132` (and `59dc522` on integration) clears the lowercase and uppercase prefix variables only for the nested CycloneDX `npx` call and adds a regression that injects the lowercase values set by `npm --prefix cli`. The focused security-gate suite then passed 10/10 under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and 10/10 under Node 24.11.1/npm 11.19.0. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and staged Gitleaks also passed. Independent review accepted the scoped fix and confirmed Linux CI compatibility.\n\n## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\n\nThis section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures remain historical evidence and are not erased; the active sealed held-out corpus is `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, SHA-256 `50895b84…`, PR #16).\n\n- At 03:10 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412` and `v1/candidate-1` was `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- Independent inspection of pilot candidate v17 verified manifest digest `ce44dd2066dc4dec6c5e1f56021e3b442aa293510cbf9f217cf2c2e2256d83fe`, all 227 listed file hashes/sizes, no unlisted package files, 40 parseable tasks, 20 repository/20 fixture tasks, and 80/80 validator-command digest coverage. That author-exposed set was not independently held out or accepted and was retired as development/pilot material when `heldout-v2` was commissioned.\n- Independent inspection of Node 24.11.1 supplement v2 verified its manifest digest (`fc8fe753272bdd2b66e17e84f6f910b1aa4230b4f9284f022e09eff0df0afd7c`), payload `SUPPLEMENTARY_VALIDATION.json` digest (`aec9651dac09d38867201d0c37163fb25213222f912114bfbda49f50e096ce36`), and binding to v17. Its three specified tasks passed the recorded base-failure/reference-pass checks.\n- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\n\n## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\n\n- PR [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), initial commit `aa2cd6228303b850f1406de94c5c9ee044ff9bf5` (merged at `2c70d39`), added the `blackbox-v1` oracle boundary and regression coverage.\n- The earlier corpus author supplied pilot overlay v18 at `/tmp/nexus-v1-heldout-author/DEC-05-v1-blackbox-dev-v18` (`SHA256SUMS.json` digest `e830c82c60a7767d4d235cc53764d8298abadc2d22107a5e6ee7ed3664509dd4`), with seven fixture tasks migrated and 33 unmigrated. That overlay remains unsealed historical pilot material and is superseded by the sealed 40-task external-repository corpus `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, PR #16).\n- On historical integration `e1759ca`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` reported 121 rows (106 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reported all versioned components at `0.1.0-alpha.2`.\n\n## Historical evidence: Earlier state checkpoint (2026-10-17 02:51 UTC)\n\n- At 02:51 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was at `8c9994596144c5674d9be8e011ad1feb4109ffb4` and `v1/candidate-1` was at `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- A confirmed CI dependency defect was fixed at `642ba37`: the contest-contract job builds the CLI after installing dependencies and before running demo tests, because `cli/dist` is generated and untracked. The prior run at `10fe416` failed when `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` could not import `cli/dist/client.js`; that failure remains historical evidence.\n- `rust-toolchain.toml` is tracked and pins Rust `1.95.0` with `rustfmt` and `clippy`.\n- `REQ-DX-106` is satisfied on the integration branch: GitHub milestone [v1.0.0](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/milestone/1) has seven open plan-group issues ([#1–#7](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1)).\n- The earlier v12 (`82886448799cb9c63d28a8f5f28b940229b981a51982c49bad80b7f7d2c73092`), v15 (`6f78983cc860a4ed616f5aa5375b8d3fec5b7335ea6bac47a448924dc91af06d`), and v16 T2 pilot packages and their failed Docker validation attempts remain historical evidence only.\n\n## Historical evidence at `6151a23`\n\n- At that historical inspection, `v1/integration` and `v1/candidate-1` identified the same commit (`6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`).\n- `make build` completed successfully in an isolated candidate worktree. The produced TUI and CLI entrypoint hashes were respectively `ca20da9214db8dcb130cfa35f25f2e76f9caad63dcf3dfbefe49132fcaa9e52f` and `8da0ccf909d5432de22d62459168f21a22b4360607cbf47259338cc144758f42`.\n- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repository at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-built-6151.log` (SHA-256 `b72e0e15819985fc48f39998d2adc5ce90e9dd125519784c25a2a2b4d2db9521`).\n- The earlier unbuilt `make test` failed (Rust 281 passed; CLI 1060/1087 passed, 27 failed, zero skipped) because required generated build outputs were absent. It is preserved at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-6151.log` (SHA-256 `7c4a364daedc3b26bd6b0392f6e0466c581c33ae5ef9d04c11348129e0abbb31`) and is superseded only for the source-suite result by the correctly ordered build-then-test run.\n- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n\n## Requirements below their required gate (reconciled at `a7126aa`)\n\n| ID | Current state | Remaining behavior or evidence | Dependency | Owner role | Exact next action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\n| `REQ-AGT-004` | tested (depth 0; work-unit mechanism landed in PR-4b) | `AGT-02a` archive→task→session commit ordering is applied to durable work units by PR-4b (`agent.ts:3339-3402`, `operation_runner.ts:566`, `durable_continuity.test.ts:359`, `dispositions.md` M2); work-unit pressure-forced compaction + SIGKILL crash-boundary test is in flight under `PLAN-04 PR-4g`, and live long-task `ACC-CONT-10` remains pending RC qualification. | `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (`ACC-CONT-03` SIGKILL), `ACC-CONT-10` on installed RC | Continuity implementer, independent reviewer, and qualification operator | Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (M1/M3/L5), then execute `ACC-CONT-10` on the installed RC during M5. |\n| `REQ-AGT-010` | partial (RR; v1 subset independently accepted at `f68b5bc`) | `ACC-TRUST-04` v1 subset (workspace skills/knowledge trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted (PR #17 `f68b5bc`); `DEC-04` defers the full `CTX-001` provenance graph and `CTX-002` to post-v1. | Installed-RC verification; post-v1 deferral recorded | Requirement owner | Preserve the `DEC-04` v1 subset / post-v1 boundary in release notes and verify no regression on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-AGT-111` | open (post-v1 shared-loop refactor; v1 behavior still required) | `PLAN-04` defers the full shared step implementation, while v1 requires documented main/subagent divergences and `measureAdmission` in the subagent loop. Calls exist in both loops, and divergence documentation is tracked under `PLAN-04`. | `PLAN-04` task 6 and source evidence | Continuity implementer, then requirement owner | Verify both `measureAdmission` calls satisfy strict-counting behavior and ensure main/subagent divergence documentation is reconciled in the ledger. |\n| `REQ-PRV-003` | implemented | Standalone behavior has scripted tests but no qualifying live standalone evidence (HIST-08). | Installed RC; standalone matrix | Provider qualification operator | Run `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 for supported server profiles and archive sanitized receipts. |\n| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\n| `REQ-REL-106` | open (post-v1; manual path defined for v1) | `SPEC-06` marks self-uninstall/prune post-v1 and retains the quickstart manual uninstall as the v1 path. The ledger's open status is a roadmap deferral, not a v1 implementation blocker. | Post-v1 scope; release documentation | Release/documentation owner | Preserve the documented manual uninstall path for v1 and record this item as explicitly deferred in the final release ledger. |\n| `REQ-AGT-118` | tested (source level; `DEC-17` exceptions preserved) | Conflict resolved by `DEC-17` (PR #11 `f771a3c`): the `≥ 1` token-per-CJK/Hangul-character admission-safety floor takes precedence over the `≤ 1.5×` band, which applies to corpora not dominated by the floor; Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) floor exceptions remain recorded. Source tests (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3) and independent review records (PRs #12, #14, #15) are integrated. | Installed-RC qualification | Qualification operator | Retain the `DEC-17` exception record; source-level `tested` status does not substitute for installed-RC product qualification. |\n| `REQ-AGT-110` | open | Independent continuity/compaction/truncation acceptance under `ACCEPTANCE.md` §8, including an independent long task with two compactions and kill/resume. | Installed RC and reviewer who did not implement the work | Owner-supplied independent reviewer | After RC freeze, execute the reviewer procedure and archive a per-area verdict; this cannot be self-signed. |\n| `REQ-PER-107` | implemented (post-v1 optional item) | `SPEC-08` marks parent-directory fsync post-v1 and optional. Source evidence exists; this is not a v1 gate under the accepted spec. | Post-v1 scope | Persistence implementer and requirement owner | Keep recorded as optional post-v1 scope. |\n| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n\nAt `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121 rows; 107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open**. In `--enforce` mode (the G6 release gate), the checker remains fail-closed until the remaining blocker and release-required rows above reach their required post-qualification states.\n\n## Gate reconciliation (at `a7126aa`)\n\n| Gate | Evidence at `a7126aa` | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\n| G1 safety | Full source suite (`1,152/1,152` CLI, `281/281` Rust, 0 skipped) and `scripts/security_gates.sh` pass in CI run `39108774170`. | Source gate green; artifact-bound checks run at Stage 3 after RC construction. |\n| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n| G4 persistence | Source persistence and retention tests pass in CI (`39108774170`). | Source gate green; independent RC acceptance (§8) pending Stage 4. |\n\n## Release and qualification sequence (`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1)\n\n1. **Close remaining source & host prerequisites on `v1/integration`:** Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (Continuity M1/M3/L5), `PLAN-10 PR-10j` (dedicated-tmpfs storage preflight & canary), and `PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` (qualification-host provisioning bundle and frozen resource profile); update the stale `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 sentence now that PR #21 (`a7126aa`) implements draft-then-publish for stable tags.\n2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\n3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\n4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\n\n## RC5 qualification checkpoint (2026-10-25)\n\n### Release identity and source gates\n\n- **Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`. **Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`. RC5 is a public prerelease; neither an accepted RC nor stable v1.0.0 is claimed.\n- **Exact source:** `main` / `v1.0.0-rc.5` at `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd` (tag object `ffccefea5859db9fe5306450f891d1f137ac6c05`).\n- **Source CI:** run [40190718023](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718023) and CodeQL [40190718020](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40190718020) passed on the exact main revision. Requirements enforcement passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; the 12 mapped exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred and enforced as such.\n- **PR #216:** merged to that source revision after exact-head checks and independent source review. The unrelated shared checkout remains dirty and was not used or modified for this checkpoint.\n\n### RC5 artifacts and installation\n\n- Release workflow [40193772994](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40193772994) completed successfully and published `v1.0.0-rc.5` as a prerelease. The archive SHA-256 is `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `2206b35a0aed8a4b9635012c0ad55a6eae34d12fe3255c53d43ab8b1d8e7a8c1`.\n- Published asset hashes and provenance attestations verified against the release workflow and exact tag. The official installer installed the archive on the authenticated engineering host; its version, package manifest and provenance sidecar matched the candidate.\n- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\n- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n\n### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\n\n- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\n- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n\n### Remaining qualification gates\n\n| Gate | State at RC5 | Next executable step / completion condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n| Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n| Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\n\nPublic metadata updates were added to issues [#3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3) and [#5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/5). Publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance; no additional authorization is requested here.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":707096046}},"started_at_ms":1793037376712,"completed_at_ms":1793037377419}}
