{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:56:32.254Z","ordinal":395470,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1795b-597e-76e0-a7ae-eec868244e99","call_id":"call_599bdf3a61424261a547f4f2f99c2e87","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #256 was merged at `1aa8832`; its exact head, `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, is an ancestor of current `origin/main` at `4cae11c`. The feature branch remains clean at `987c73a`, originally based on `ff34938`. [PR #256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256)\\n\\nThe commit fixed pending local-discovery cancellation and late activation, corrected the key-storage message, and isolated invalid provider catalog errors. Its credential-origin fix was incomplete: later review reproduced a legacy key reaching the newly selected endpoint. So that commit alone does not clear the security acceptance blocker.\\n\\nCI passed on PR #256, but GitHub records no reviews, and I found no independent acceptance of exact head `987c73a`. An accepted follow-up exists on branch `v1/defect-malformed-credential-origin` at `0571266`; it has no open PR and is not in current `main`.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for exact head `d508e1998d879dc4e0005b8c6a0cc3e2ccc2bda1` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. Diff SHA-256 matches the requested `ab494c7bf2a97bc50e5142caa49e2d2efd60618d6be11ff76f374e88a9a69ca5`.\\n\\n- At [READINESS.md:9](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9), the RC9 workflow is described as running `npm --prefix cli test`. Live run `40370485753` is instead in progress at `scripts/package-linux.sh ...`. Update the active step.\\n- GitHub’s tag metadata reports the RC9 signature as unverified with reason `bad_email`. “Signed tag” is technically supported by the tag object, but clarify that GitHub has not verified it; don’t let the wording imply verified provenance.\\n\\nThe release list confirms RC8 is still the latest published prerelease, and the RC9 build has no published release assets. The checkpoint keeps acceptance gated. Earlier snapshots are preserved, and the diff passes `git diff --check`.\\n\\nThe RC8 session section labels its claims operator-reported and explicitly says `NOT_ESTABLISHED`; I found no public record for that session export to independently verify its classification. Its limited evidentiary role is stated accurately.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037392.254837}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
