{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:59:22.877Z","ordinal":395615,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf94f1e73881a08729fcab56d20856","status":"completed","call_id":"call_80352bb21b4d4255a97dc074d582fe25","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\\n@@\\n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 18:06 UTC)\\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 17:59 UTC)\\n@@\\n-**RC9 candidate build:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` (tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6`) points to source commit `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. `git verify-tag` reports a good signature from the release key, and GitHub commit verification reports `verified: true, reason: valid`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) remains in progress at package smoke tests (`scripts/smoke-package.sh`); no RC9 GitHub release assets or provenance are published yet. RC8 remains the latest published prerelease. RC9 is only a candidate build, not an accepted RC; no exact-RC qualification or stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\\n+**RC9 candidate artifact:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` (tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6`) points to source commit `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. `git verify-tag` reports a good signature from the release key, and GitHub commit verification reports `verified: true, reason: valid`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) completed SUCCESS; the prerelease was published at 17:56 UTC. The archive `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz` is 4,859,736 bytes with SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`; all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`, and GitHub attestation verification passed for the archive and checksum index. RC9 remains an unaccepted prerelease; exact-RC product qualification and stable `v1.0.0` release are not claimed.\\n@@\\n-**Qualification and terminal setup:** Held-out qualification has not started. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471) received a metadata-only custody follow-up at 17:37 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded, and Agent Mail reports no active project window identities. No private corpus payloads were accessed. The Ubuntu desktop at `10.0.8.3` is reachable over strict-host-key SSH; GitHub CLI authentication is present, the GNOME Wayland session is active, and xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are installed. The GNOME Shell screenshot D-Bus service is also available; standalone screenshot utilities are absent, so evidence capture should use the desktop screenshot UI or the available GNOME service. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15 until the workflow-produced exact RC is installed and an operator records each real terminal/size cell with required screenshots. Automated PTY checks cannot replace this evidence.\\n+**Qualification and terminal setup:** Held-out qualification has not started. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471) received a metadata-only custody follow-up at 17:37 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded, and Agent Mail reports no active project window identities. No private corpus payloads were accessed. The Ubuntu desktop at `10.0.8.3` is reachable over strict-host-key SSH; GitHub CLI authentication is present, the GNOME Wayland session is active, and xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are installed. The GNOME Shell screenshot D-Bus service is available; standalone screenshot utilities are absent, so evidence capture should use the desktop screenshot UI or the available GNOME service. The RC9 installer verified provenance for the archive and checksum index, then installed into the separate