{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:01:06.745Z","ordinal":395707,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9561a40081a0b44a907e6e9ea75d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4eb76ebdebe74982b654b0e419a8ef61","name":"exec","input":"// @exec: {\"max_output_tokens\": 1200}\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n 'read -r|Screenshot|screenshot|required|check|RC|install|NEXUS_' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | head -70; sed -n '25,135p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1100});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037665.7566166}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:01:06.792Z","ordinal":395708,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf955a630881a0b5bce19555baa9c9","usage":{"input_tokens":117940,"cached_input_tokens":117504,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":796,"reasoning_output_tokens":654,"total_tokens":118736},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":50702705,"cached_input_tokens":50172160,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":149594,"reasoning_output_tokens":83539,"total_tokens":50852299},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7273296475,"cached_input_tokens":7196197376,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20759478,"reasoning_output_tokens":12034663,"total_tokens":7294055953}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:01:08.991Z","ordinal":395709,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-be3ba969-1934-4ff5-bccb-e1d3fb746312","process_id":"1930","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'read -r|Screenshot|screenshot|required|check|RC|install|NEXUS_' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | head -70; sed -n '25,135p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'read -r|Screenshot|screenshot|required|check|RC|install|NEXUS_' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md","query":"read -r|Screenshot|screenshot|required|check|RC|install|NEXUS_","path":"run-cell.sh"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '25,135p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh","name":"run-cell.sh","path":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:3:A human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:12:**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:16:1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:17:   not resolve into a checkout.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:19:3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:31:The script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:33:the TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:38:| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:49:A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:50:`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:51:results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:61:# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:68:- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:69:- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:70:- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:3:# to the cell. It verifies the installed RC package and the terminal, launches the TUI against a deterministic local\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:8:# The human records PASS/FAIL per check and two screenshots. Every attempt is kept. Usage:\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:13:HERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:26:[[ \"$rc\" =~ ^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+-rc\\.[0-9]+$ ]] || { echo \"--rc must be an RC tag, vX.Y.Z-rc.N\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:29:[[ -n \"$out\" ]] || { echo \"--out is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:32:# Identity: the installed RC package (VERSION and its own MANIFEST.sha256), never a checkout build.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:33:nexus_bin=\"$(command -v nexus)\" || { echo \"nexus is not on PATH; install the RC with the documented one-line command\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:36:[[ \"$(cat \"$package/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$rc\" ]] || { echo \"nexus resolves to $nexus_real, which is not an installed $rc package\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:37:(cd \"$package\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || { echo \"installed package at $package fails its MANIFEST.sha256\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:38:# The manifest must also list every file: an extra file in the package would pass sha256sum --check.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:41:  || { echo \"installed package at $package has files its MANIFEST.sha256 does not list\" >&2; exit 2; }\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:48:read -r rows cols < <(stty size)\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:62:  read -r -p \"Is the kitty keyboard protocol enabled for this window? (yes/no) \" kitty_protocol\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:66:# The scope-based survivor check needs the user's systemd manager.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:146:     approve with a deliberate key. Screenshot an approval panel.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:150:  6  Quit with Ctrl-C twice. Screenshot the terminal after exit.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:153:read -r _\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:160:read -r _\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:163:# Answers are saved before anything else can fail, so a typo in a screenshot path does not lose them.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:164:: > \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:165:for check in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7; do\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:167:    read -r -p \"check $check PASS or FAIL? \" answer\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:170:  read -r -p \"check $check note (optional): \" note\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:171:  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$check\" \"$answer\" \"${note//$'\\t'/ }\" >> \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:173:cp \"$cell_home/checks.tsv\" \"$stem.answers.tsv\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:176:read -r -p \"operator name: \" operator\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:178:  read -r -p \"approval-panel screenshot path: \" shot_approval\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:179:  read -r -p \"post-exit screenshot path: \" shot_exit\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:183:  echo \"both screenshots must be .png/.jpg files taken during this attempt, and differ; try again\"\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:191:CELL=\"$cell\" ATTEMPT=\"$attempt\" TERMINAL_NAME=\"$terminal\" CELL_SIZE=\"$size\" RC=\"$rc\" NEXUS_VERSION_LINE=\"$version_line\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:192:NEXUS_PATH=\"$nexus_real\" PACKAGE_DIR=\"$package\" MANIFEST_SHA=\"$manifest_sha\" TMUX_VERSION=\"$tmux_version\" \\\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:203:checks = {}\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:205:    check, result, note = (line.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\t\") + [\"\"])[:3]\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:206:    checks[check] = {\"result\": result, \"note\": note}\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:218:    \"rc\": e[\"RC\"], \"nexusVersion\": e[\"NEXUS_VERSION_LINE\"], \"nexusPath\": e[\"NEXUS_PATH\"], \"packageDir\": e[\"PACKAGE_DIR\"],\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:222:    \"measured\": exits, \"scenarios\": scenarios, \"checks\": checks,\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh:224:              [(\"approvalScreenshot\", e[\"APPROVAL_SHOT\"]), (\"postExitScreenshot\", e[\"EXIT_SHOT\"]), (\"mockLog\", f\"{stem}.mock.log\"),\ndone\n[[ \"$rc\" =~ ^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+-rc\\.[0-9]+$ ]] || { echo \"--rc must be an RC tag, vX.Y.Z-rc.N\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ \"$terminal\" =~ ^(xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome)$ ]] || { echo \"--terminal must be xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ \"$size\" =~ ^(80x24|40x14|200x60)$ ]] || { echo \"--size must be 80x24|40x14|200x60\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ -n \"$out\" ]] || { echo \"--out is required\" >&2; exit 2; }\n[[ -t 0 && -t 1 ]] || { echo \"run this interactively in the terminal under test\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Identity: the installed RC package (VERSION and its own MANIFEST.sha256), never a checkout build.\nnexus_bin=\"$(command -v nexus)\" || { echo \"nexus is not on PATH; install the RC with the documented one-line command\" >&2; exit 2; }\nnexus_real=\"$(readlink -f \"$nexus_bin\")\"\npackage=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$nexus_real\")\")\"\n[[ \"$(cat \"$package/VERSION\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$rc\" ]] || { echo \"nexus resolves to $nexus_real, which is not an installed $rc package\" >&2; exit 2; }\n(cd \"$package\" && sha256sum --check --status MANIFEST.sha256) || { echo \"installed package at $package fails its MANIFEST.sha256\" >&2; exit 2; }\n# The manifest must also list every file: an extra file in the package would pass sha256sum --check.\ndiff <(cd \"$package\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | sed 's|^\\./||' | LC_ALL=C sort) \\\n     <(sed -E 's/^[0-9a-f]{64} [ *]//; s|^\\./||' \"$package/MANIFEST.sha256\" | LC_ALL=C sort) >/dev/null \\\n  || { echo \"installed package at $package has files its MANIFEST.sha256 does not list\" >&2; exit 2; }\nmanifest_sha=\"$(sha256sum \"$package/MANIFEST.sha256\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\"\nversion_line=\"$(nexus --version 2>&1 | head -n 1)\"\n[[ \"$(grep -oE '[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?' <<< \"$version_line\" | head -n 1)\" == \"${rc#v}\" ]] || { echo \"nexus reports '$version_line', not exactly ${rc#v}\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Terminal: the cell's size, and environment consistent with the claimed terminal.\nwant_cols=\"${size%x*}\" want_rows=\"${size#*x}\"\nread -r rows cols < <(stty size)\n[[ \"$cols\" == \"$want_cols\" && \"$rows\" == \"$want_rows\" ]] || { echo \"terminal is ${cols}x${rows}; resize it to $size first\" >&2; exit 2; }\ntmux_version=\"\"\ncase \"$terminal\" in\n  xterm) [[ -n \"${XTERM_VERSION:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"XTERM_VERSION unset or inside tmux: not xterm\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  kitty) [[ -n \"${KITTY_WINDOW_ID:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"KITTY_WINDOW_ID unset or inside tmux: not kitty\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  vscode) [[ \"${TERM_PROGRAM:-}\" == vscode ]] || { echo \"TERM_PROGRAM is not vscode\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  gnome) [[ -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" && -z \"${TMUX:-}\" ]] || { echo \"GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN/SERVICE unset or inside tmux: not GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\n  tmux-gnome)\n    [[ -n \"${TMUX:-}\" && -n \"${GNOME_TERMINAL_SCREEN:-}${GNOME_TERMINAL_SERVICE:-}\" ]] || { echo \"run inside tmux inside GNOME Terminal\" >&2; exit 2; }\n    tmux_version=\"$(tmux -V)\"; [[ \"$tmux_version\" =~ ^tmux\\ 3\\. ]] || { echo \"need tmux 3.x, have $tmux_version\" >&2; exit 2; } ;;\nesac\nkitty_protocol=\"\"\nif [[ \"$terminal\" == kitty ]]; then\n  read -r -p \"Is the kitty keyboard protocol enabled for this window? (yes/no) \" kitty_protocol\n  [[ \"$kitty_protocol\" == yes ]] || { echo \"enable the kitty keyboard protocol first\" >&2; exit 2; }\nfi\n\n# The scope-based survivor check needs the user's systemd manager.\nsystemd-run --user --scope --quiet -- true || { echo \"systemd user scopes are unavailable in this session\" >&2; exit 2; }\n\n# Attempts are numbered in one directory and never overwritten; the gate counts every attempt, including aborted ones.\ncell=\"$terminal-$size\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nattempt=1\nwhile [[ -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.json\" || -e \"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt.partial\" ]]; do attempt=$((attempt + 1)); done\nstem=\"$out/cell-$cell.attempt-$attempt\"\nattempt_start=\"$(date +%s)\"\n: > \"$stem.partial\"\n\n# Isolated HOME and workspace; nothing touches the operator's ~/.nexus or ~/.config/nexus.\ncell_home=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/nexus-terminal-$cell.XXXXXX\")\"\nws=\"$cell_home/workspace\"\nmkdir -p \"$ws\" \"$cell_home/.config/nexus\"\ngit -C \"$ws\" init -q\nprintf 'terminal matrix workspace\\n' > \"$ws/README.md\"\nmock_log=\"$cell_home/mock.log\"\npython3 \"$HERE/mockgw.py\" \"$cell_home/port\" \"$mock_log\" &\nmock_pid=$!\ncanary_pid=\"\"\ncleanup() { kill \"$mock_pid\" ${canary_pid:+\"$canary_pid\"} 2>/dev/null || true; rm -rf \"$cell_home\"; }\ntrap cleanup EXIT\nfor _ in $(seq 50); do [[ -s \"$cell_home/port\" ]] && break; sleep 0.1; done\nport=\"$(cat \"$cell_home/port\")\"\nprintf 'LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:%s/v1\\nLOCAL_LLM_MODEL=terminal-matrix\\n' \"$port\" > \"$cell_home/.config/nexus/config.env\"\n\n# The TUI sees only a whitelisted environment, so operator gateway or API settings cannot redirect it.\nlaunch_env=(env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" HOME=\"$cell_home\" XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$cell_home/.config\" XDG_DATA_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/share\"\n  XDG_STATE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.local/state\" XDG_CACHE_HOME=\"$cell_home/.cache\" LANG=\"${LANG:-C.UTF-8}\")\nfor var in TERM COLORTERM TERM_PROGRAM TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION VTE_VERSION KITTY_WINDOW_ID TMUX TMUX_PANE XTERM_VERSION DISPLAY WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_RUNTIME_DIR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS; do\n  [[ -n \"${!var:-}\" ]] && launch_env+=(\"$var=${!var}\")\ndone\n\n# Processes from this cell: HOME is the cell's HOME, or the working directory is inside the cell workspace.\ncell_processes() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in $(pgrep -u \"$(id -u)\"); do\n    [[ \"$pid\" == \"$mock_pid\" || \"$pid\" == \"$$\" || \"$pid\" == \"$BASHPID\" ]] && continue\n    if tr '\\0' '\\n' < \"/proc/$pid/environ\" 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \"HOME=$cell_home\" || [[ \"$(readlink \"/proc/$pid/cwd\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$ws\"* ]]; then\n      echo \"$pid\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n# Positive control: the scan must find a planted process before it is trusted to report zero.\n(cd \"$ws\" && exec env HOME=\"$cell_home\" sleep 600) &\ncanary_pid=$!\nsleep 0.3\ncell_processes | grep -qx \"$canary_pid\" || { echo \"survivor scan cannot see a planted cell process; refusing to measure\" >&2; exit 1; }\nkill \"$canary_pid\"; wait \"$canary_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true; canary_pid=\"\"\n\n# Each launch runs in its own transient systemd user scope. The cgroup probe\n# reports zero only for a readable empty cgroup or a scope systemd confirms is\n# stopped/gone; missing data while active remains an explicit failed measure.\nlaunch() {\n  local label=\"$1\"; shift\n  local before after status=0 survivors scoped scope_measurement=verified unit=\"nexus-terminal-$cell-$attempt-$label\"\n  before=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  (cd \"$ws\" && systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --unit=\"$unit\" -- \"${launch_env[@]}\" \"$@\" nexus) || status=$?\n  after=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  sleep 2\n  if ! scoped=\"$(nexus_terminal_scope_procs \"$unit\")\"; then\n    scoped=0\n    scope_measurement=unavailable\n  fi\n  survivors=\"$(cell_processes | wc -l)\"\n  (( scoped > survivors )) && survivors=\"$scoped\"\n  [[ \"$survivors\" == 0 && \"$scope_measurement\" == verified ]] || { cell_processes | xargs -r ps -o pid=,args= -p >&2; systemctl --user kill --signal=KILL \"$unit.scope\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$label\" \"$status\" \"$([[ \"$before\" == \"$after\" ]] && echo true || echo false)\" \"$survivors\" \"$scope_measurement\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" >> \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":898782316}},"started_at_ms":1793037668091,"completed_at_ms":1793037668991}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:01:10.096Z","ordinal":395710,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1795f-96d0-7fb0-817a-46d380fba334","call_id":"call_4eb76ebdebe74982b654b0e419a8ef61","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3585)\nTotal output lines: 164\n\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:3:A human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:12:**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:16:1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:17:   not resolve into a checkout.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:19:3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:31:The script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:33:the TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:38:| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:42:| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:49:A measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:50:`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:51:results and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:61:# M…2485 tokens truncated…RM TERM_PROGRAM TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION VTE_VERSION KITTY_WINDOW_ID TMUX TMUX_PANE XTERM_VERSION DISPLAY WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_RUNTIME_DIR DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS; do\n  [[ -n \"${!var:-}\" ]] && launch_env+=(\"$var=${!var}\")\ndone\n\n# Processes from this cell: HOME is the cell's HOME, or the working directory is inside the cell workspace.\ncell_processes() {\n  local pid\n  for pid in $(pgrep -u \"$(id -u)\"); do\n    [[ \"$pid\" == \"$mock_pid\" || \"$pid\" == \"$$\" || \"$pid\" == \"$BASHPID\" ]] && continue\n    if tr '\\0' '\\n' < \"/proc/$pid/environ\" 2>/dev/null | grep -qx \"HOME=$cell_home\" || [[ \"$(readlink \"/proc/$pid/cwd\" 2>/dev/null)\" == \"$ws\"* ]]; then\n      echo \"$pid\"\n    fi\n  done\n}\n# Positive control: the scan must find a planted process before it is trusted to report zero.\n(cd \"$ws\" && exec env HOME=\"$cell_home\" sleep 600) &\ncanary_pid=$!\nsleep 0.3\ncell_processes | grep -qx \"$canary_pid\" || { echo \"survivor scan cannot see a planted cell process; refusing to measure\" >&2; exit 1; }\nkill \"$canary_pid\"; wait \"$canary_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true; canary_pid=\"\"\n\n# Each launch runs in its own transient systemd user scope. The cgroup probe\n# reports zero only for a readable empty cgroup or a scope systemd confirms is\n# stopped/gone; missing data while active remains an explicit failed measure.\nlaunch() {\n  local label=\"$1\"; shift\n  local before after status=0 survivors scoped scope_measurement=verified unit=\"nexus-terminal-$cell-$attempt-$label\"\n  before=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  (cd \"$ws\" && systemd-run --user --scope --quiet --unit=\"$unit\" -- \"${launch_env[@]}\" \"$@\" nexus) || status=$?\n  after=\"$(stty -g)\"\n  sleep 2\n  if ! scoped=\"$(nexus_terminal_scope_procs \"$unit\")\"; then\n    scoped=0\n    scope_measurement=unavailable\n  fi\n  survivors=\"$(cell_processes | wc -l)\"\n  (( scoped > survivors )) && survivors=\"$scoped\"\n  [[ \"$survivors\" == 0 && \"$scope_measurement\" == verified ]] || { cell_processes | xargs -r ps -o pid=,args= -p >&2; systemctl --user kill --signal=KILL \"$unit.scope\" 2>/dev/null || true; }\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$label\" \"$status\" \"$([[ \"$before\" == \"$after\" ]] && echo true || echo false)\" \"$survivors\" \"$scope_measurement\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" >> \"$cell_home/exits.tsv\"\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037670.0965843}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
