{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:03:53.402Z","ordinal":395833,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17962-14ba-7e22-ba96-3d159a6e01b7","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for head `b6d39ee385aaa05e26d22383927f509ae911a568` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. Diff SHA-256: `9c4d5ab9214495388544ead09cd2e4eefc22dbef7830a4f090f5cb2ae9e6730b`.\n\n- At [READINESS.md:9](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9), the release workflow, publication time, tag target, and archive size/digest match live records. Local `git verify-tag` succeeds, and GitHub verifies the source commit. However, GitHub’s tag-object API still reports `verified: false`, reason `bad_email`. State that separately so commit verification is not read as GitHub tag verification.\n- The release API confirms published assets and their digests, but I couldn’t corroborate the claimed GitHub attestation verification or the desktop RC9 installation from the linked public records. Add a link to a sanitized verification/install record, or label those as operator-reported. The RC8 session paragraph is appropriately labeled operator-reported and says `NOT_ESTABLISHED`; it makes no qualification claim.\n\nThe release workflow is SUCCESS, RC9 is published, and the readiness text keeps acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Historical entries are preserved, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793037833.4025142}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19494}}
