{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:05:21.699Z","ordinal":395901,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-eb0fdf3e-5aca-4858-9ece-0c9195f87752","process_id":"41970","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short --branch; git diff --check; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md | sed -n '1,130p'; git log -3 --format='%h %an %s'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short --branch; git diff --check; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md | sed -n '1,130p'; git log -3 --format='%h %an %s'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026...origin/v1/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 8 ++++----\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 14d20a3..3215faf 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,18 +1,18 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 17:59 UTC)\n+## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 18:05 UTC)\n \n **Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`, the merge commit for PR #258. Exact-main CI [40363722642](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40363722642) and CodeQL [40363722565](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40363722565) completed SUCCESS on this exact commit; Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/install checks passed. In a clean detached worktree at this SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirmed all components are `1.0.0-rc.9`, and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These are source-stage results; they do not satisfy deferred qualification gates.\n \n **Integrated fixes:** PR #258 fixed the legacy local-provider credential-origin rebinding finding and updated RC9 notes. It was independently source-reviewed ACCEPT on exact diff SHA-256 `1e7a8414b112d895345b14a7e27b9d7769428df6c904cde09ff8ef0f23061fe1`; PR CI [40357724824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40357724824) and CodeQL [40357724535](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40357724535) passed before merge. The review was a GitHub COMMENT, not an APPROVE. PR #256 local endpoint setup and PR #253 one-reset release-download retry are also integrated. Installed exact-RC provider and upgrade acceptance have not run.\n \n-**RC9 candidate artifact:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` (tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6`) points to source commit `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. `git verify-tag` reports a good signature from the release key, and GitHub commit verification reports `verified: true, reason: valid`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) completed SUCCESS; the prerelease was published at 17:56 UTC. The archive `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz` is 4,859,736 bytes with SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`; all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`, and GitHub attestation verification passed for the archive and checksum index. RC9 remains an unaccepted prerelease; exact-RC product qualification and stable `v1.0.0` release are not claimed.\n+**RC9 candidate artifact:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` (tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6`) points to source commit `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature. GitHub's source-commit verification is `verified: true, reason: valid`, while its separate tag-object verification is `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) completed SUCCESS; the prerelease was published at 17:56 UTC. The archive `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz` is 4,859,736 bytes with SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`; all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`, and `gh attestation verify` exited 0 for the archive and checksum index. The archive identity and isolated desktop install are recorded in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). RC9 remains an unaccepted prerelease; exact-RC product qualification and stable `v1.0.0` release are not claimed.\n \n **Operator-reported RC8 dogfooding:** Session export `session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn` (SHA-256 `6eee8181c62cfc278183ff65f27485d5c224046b6bc5107cc95b0c849a199d87`) is attributed by the operator to RC8 on `mike-dev`. It records a codebase-review task that wrote `docs/codebase-review-enhancements.md` (14,175 bytes). The export has no candidate/package identity, worktree binding, or validation receipts; its final task outcome is `NOT_ESTABLISHED` because the `make test` verifier failed before executing tests (`hasExecutedTests=false`), and `unverifiedChangesPending=true`. This is useful exploratory dogfood feedback only, not exact-RC, requirement, or acceptance evidence.\n \n-**Qualification and terminal setup:** Held-out qualification has not started. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471) received a metadata-only custody follow-up at 17:37 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded, and Agent Mail reports no active project window identities. No private corpus payloads were accessed. The Ubuntu desktop at `10.0.8.3` is reachable over strict-host-key SSH; GitHub CLI authentication is present, the GNOME Wayland session is active, and xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are installed. The GNOME Shell screenshot D-Bus service is available; standalone screenshot utilities are absent, so evidence capture should use the desktop screenshot UI or the available GNOME service. The RC9 installer verified provenance for the archive and checksum index, then installed into the separate prefix `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification`; the installed binary reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)` and its provenance record contains archive SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. This proves package installation and identity, not product acceptance. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15 until an operator records every real terminal/size cell and required screenshots. Automated PTY checks cannot replace this evidence.\n+**Qualification and terminal setup:** Held-out qualification has not started. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471) received a metadata-only custody follow-up at 17:37 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded, and Agent Mail reports no active project window identities. No private corpus payloads were accessed. The Ubuntu desktop at `10.0.8.3` is reachable over strict-host-key SSH; GitHub CLI authentication is present, the GNOME Wayland session is active, and xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are installed. The GNOME Shell screenshot D-Bus service is available; standalone screenshot utilities are absent, so evidence capture can use the desktop screenshot UI or supplied helper. RC9 installation details are recorded in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). The package is installed in the separate prefix `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification`; its binary reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)` and its provenance record contains the verified archive SHA-256. The terminal harness and screenshot helper are staged on the desktop under `~/.cache/nexus-rc9-terminal-matrix`; the 15-cell procedure is in `START-HERE.md`. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15 until an operator records every real terminal/size cell and required screenshots. Automated PTY checks cannot replace this evidence.\n \n-**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source gates are green, and the RC9 artifact is published and installed with verified provenance. Independent held-out custody, exact-RC qualification, provider/standalone runs, cross-runner checks, the human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain pending.\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source gates are green, and the RC9 artifact is published, verified, and installed. Independent held-out custody, exact-RC qualification, provider/standalone runs, cross-runner checks, the human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain pending.\n \n ---\n \nb6d39ee Mike Holownych docs(release): record RC9 artifact verification and install\nd508e19 Mike Holownych docs(release): correct RC9 and dogfood checkpoint\n782b737 Mike Holownych docs(release): record PR258 integration and current gates\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":857691789}},"started_at_ms":1793037920841,"completed_at_ms":1793037921699}}
