{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:08.735Z","ordinal":396069,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f562da2d-a73d-4927-96f0-fd0711e6dd6d","process_id":"40062","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n '^###? 4\\.|^## 4\\.|provider|standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|live' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | head -70; sed -n '100,180p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^###? 4'\"\\\\.|\"'^## 4'\"\\\\.|provider|standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|live\" docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","query":"^###? 4\\.|^## 4\\.|provider|standalone|OpenRouter|ChatGPT|live","path":"ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '100,180p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n44:| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n47:| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n50:| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n123:## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n125:### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n135:4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n138:### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n150:### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n155:| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n156:| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n309:2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n333:- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n343:- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n\n## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":815177993}},"started_at_ms":1793038087919,"completed_at_ms":1793038088735}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:09.288Z","ordinal":396070,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f7048c47-6448-41bf-ad5f-68e21e6331c5","process_id":"28817","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'N=\"$HOME/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification/bin/nexus\"; \"$N\" --help | tail -45; printf \"\\nDOCTOR_OPTIONS\\n\"; \"$N\" doctor --help | sed -n \"1,50p\"' 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'N=\"$HOME/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification/bin/nexus\"; \"$N\" --help | tail -45; printf \"\\nDOCTOR_OPTIONS\\n\"; \"$N\" doctor --help | sed -n \"1,50p\"' 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"  --fallback <urls>                            Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n  --dry-run                                    Simulate file modifications without writing changes to disk\n  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n  --worktree                                   Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>           Trusted command that must pass before any task completion; its success may authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                              Record execution into an append-only deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n  -h, --help                                   display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  repl [options]                               Start interactive coding session (REPL / TUI)\n  run [options] [prompt...]                    Run an autonomous coding task\n  models [options]                             List loaded models from your local LM Studio or vLLM server\n  doctor [options]                             Diagnose configuration, endpoint, credentials, engine, shell, state and extensions without starting an agent\n  check [options]                              Compatibility alias for `doctor` (the former health check)\n  sessions                                     List past interactive sessions and saved transcripts\n  gc [options]                                 Clean up old sessions, tasks, checkpoints, and flights according to retention policy (REQ-PER-102, DEC-11)\n  skills [options]                             List installed agent skills and their descriptions\n  mcp [options]                                Check connected MCP servers and inspect exposed tools\n  plugins [options]                            List loaded custom plugins and lifecycle hooks\n  trust [options] [path]                       Trust a workspace so its own .mcp.json servers and plugins are loaded (they run code from the workspace)\n  checkpoints [options]                        List saved workspace snapshots and rollback checkpoints\n  audit [options]                              Inspect tool execution audit log and execution metrics\n  serve-mcp [options]                          Run Nexus Code as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio\n  flights [options]                            List recorded deterministic flight logs\n  replay [options] <flight>                    Replay a deterministic flight log step by step\n  worktrees [options]                          List active speculative git worktrees\n  stage [options]                              Inspect and manage granular git diff hunks\n  eval [options] <dataset>                     [experimental] Evaluate SWE-bench / benchmark dataset against Nexus Code harness\n  knowledge [options] [action] [key] [val...]  Inspect or manage persistent project knowledge graph\n  browse [options] <url>                       Verify local or remote web frontend using headless browser driver\n  upgrade [options]                            Compare installed version with a published release and safely upgrade\n  operation                                    [experimental] Convergence-scheduled multi-unit operations (reroute, park, wait, resume)\n  connect [options] <provider>                 Connect a cloud provider or configure a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint\n  disconnect <provider>                        Remove the credential Nexus saved for a provider (environment and other clients are untouched)\n  providers                                    List cloud inference providers, credential status and the selected destinations\n\nDOCTOR_OPTIONS\nUsage: nexus doctor [options]\n\nDiagnose configuration, endpoint, credentials, engine, shell, state and\nextensions without starting an agent\n\nOptions:\n  -e, --endpoint <url>    Endpoint to diagnose (default: as a session would\n                          resolve it)\n  -m, --model <name>      Model to check for\n  -k, --api-key <key>     Credential to test (never printed)\n  --provider <id>         Cloud inference provider (openrouter, openai,\n                          anthropic, compatible, ...)\n  --base-url <url>        Override the provider's base URL\n  -w, --workspace <path>  Workspace directory\n  --shell <type>          Shell to check\n  --json                  Emit only the versioned JSON report (schemaVersion 2)\n  --deep                  Also run deeper checks: one minimal inference request\n                          (costs model work), an engine tool call, state write\n                          probes, all session records\n  --fix                   Propose the supported repairs and apply them after\n                          confirmation\n  --yes                   With --fix: apply the supported repairs without\n                          asking (unattended)\n  --read-only             Refuse every repair (diagnosis only)\n  --timeout <ms>          Per-check time limit in milliseconds (default 4000)\n  -h, --help              display help for command\n\nExit codes: 0 healthy · 1 warnings only · 2 at least one failure · 3 the doctor itself could not run.\nStatuses: pass, warn (works, but degraded or at risk), fail (prevents normal operation), skip (not applicable or not run).\nSupported repairs (--fix): create missing ~/.nexus state directories (0700); restrict group/world-writable state\ndirectories to 0700; restrict a group/world-readable credential store or config.env to 0600. Previous modes are recorded under\n~/.nexus/doctor-backups. Nothing else is ever changed: no configuration reset, session deletion, credential rotation,\ndependency installation, TLS change or service restart.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":412131768}},"started_at_ms":1793038087875,"completed_at_ms":1793038089288}}
