{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:13.502Z","ordinal":396076,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf970aa70881a0bb50484d9cca316f","usage":{"input_tokens":163037,"cached_input_tokens":160512,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":165,"reasoning_output_tokens":21,"total_tokens":163202},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":57368894,"cached_input_tokens":56785920,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":178762,"reasoning_output_tokens":98684,"total_tokens":57547656},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7279962664,"cached_input_tokens":7202811136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20788646,"reasoning_output_tokens":12049808,"total_tokens":7300751310}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:16.343Z","ordinal":396077,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f0249a3b-b9a6-4160-8b78-a77dbd1ccb8e","process_id":"95197","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '123,153p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'N=\"$HOME/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification/bin/nexus\"; \"$N\" providers verify --help 2>&1 | head -55' 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '123,153p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'N=\"$HOME/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification/bin/nexus\"; \"$N\" providers verify --help 2>&1 | head -55' 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\nUsage: nexus providers verify [options]\n\nLive check: streamed completion and a tool round trip against a provider (sends\nno workspace content)\n\nOptions:\n  --provider <id>     Provider to check\n  -m, --model <name>  Model id (default: $NEXUS_MODEL)\n  --base-url <url>    Override the provider's base URL\n  -j, --json          Print steps and receipts as JSON\n  -h, --help          display help for command\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":790869101}},"started_at_ms":1793038094552,"completed_at_ms":1793038096343}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:17.316Z","ordinal":396078,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17966-1ba4-70a2-96cd-2574c49bd850","call_id":"call_0f17eb9e611e425287c12edc0da528fc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\nUsage: nexus providers verify [options]\n\nLive check: streamed completion and a tool round trip against a provider (sends\nno workspace content)\n\nOptions:\n  --provider <id>     Provider to check\n  -m, --model <name>  Model id (default: $NEXUS_MODEL)\n  --base-url <url>    Override the provider's base URL\n  -j, --json          Print steps and receipts as JSON\n  -h, --help          display help for command\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793038097.316807}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
