{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:33.335Z","ordinal":396093,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2e930cae-1959-4601-b576-ebd03f195041","process_id":"76836","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","for f in docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt_pinned_2026-10-16.json; do echo \"$f\"; jq '{provider,model,passed,startedAt,finishedAt,steps,receipt}' \"$f\" | head -80; done; sed -n '116,132p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"for f in docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt_pinned_2026-10-16.json; do echo \"$f\"; jq '{provider,model,passed,startedAt,finishedAt,steps,receipt}' \"$f\" | head -80; done; sed -n '116,132p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_openrouter_pinned_2026-10-16.json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"openrouter\",\n  \"model\": \"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"startedAt\": null,\n  \"finishedAt\": null,\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"streamed completion\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"reply \\\"READY\\\", 5 chars streamed\",\n      \"requestId\": \"3efa772e-eb67-4515-b0aa-cb1f1ea9d9e0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": \"tool call\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"echo_token({\\\"token\\\":\\\"n26a01590\\\"}) complete, 1 call(s)\",\n      \"requestId\": \"79870757-2f11-48a8-9e7b-6a23850c7dc6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": \"tool result round trip\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"final answer cites the tool result\",\n      \"requestId\": \"56fc6f24-e8c6-4f6d-95ab-effcc7da003a\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"receipt\": null\n}\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/live/verify_chatgpt_pinned_2026-10-16.json\n{\n  \"provider\": \"chatgpt\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n  \"passed\": true,\n  \"startedAt\": null,\n  \"finishedAt\": null,\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"step\": \"streamed completion\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"reply \\\"READY\\\", 5 chars streamed\",\n      \"requestId\": \"c71fe00a-c234-4088-ad82-732fff465190\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": \"tool call\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"echo_token({\\\"token\\\":\\\"na60604b1\\\"}) complete, 1 call(s)\",\n      \"requestId\": \"e1e34825-4718-4e66-9157-076ab34edb21\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"step\": \"tool result round trip\",\n      \"ok\": true,\n      \"detail\": \"final answer cites the tool result\",\n      \"requestId\": \"7548f87b-002b-4a81-9d38-12c7bb6caf20\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"receipt\": null\n}\n## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n\n| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n- **`/tdd` / `--tdd`.** Labelled experimental. Fixing the phase enforcement is post-v1.\n- **Team roles.** Reviewer and researcher units run with a **read-only tool set** (cheap and safety-relevant). Other role allowlists are post-v1.\n\n## DEC-08: Version identity and stale v1.x tags\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":781981153}},"started_at_ms":1793038112553,"completed_at_ms":1793038113335}}
