{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:08:52.346Z","ordinal":396114,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17966-a47a-7440-9cb7-f6955396c9fd","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #259 at `15ef30e7985454b05cfcd69a28dbf79dd755fe35` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` (diff SHA-256 `66a4e4c5f7cb76ec3d6f2dc932bdd46a583db044c6998e7f59997cf0aa39a273`).\n\n[READINESS.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9) says “all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`.” The packaging script creates that checksum file for only the archive and `compatibility.json` ([package-linux.sh](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/scripts/package-linux.sh:210)); the evidence note likewise reports checksum validation for those two items ([rc9_artifact_install.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:20)). Narrow the readiness claim to those checksum-covered files.\n\nThe tag-verification distinction is accurately stated, and the terminal matrix remains 0/15 with acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793038132.3462498}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19502}}
