{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:09:34.771Z","ordinal":396135,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a17967-4a33-7073-bae5-e1eb4501165b","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2796)\nTotal output lines: 109\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...406 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-26 6:09pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (18,479t read) | 100,471t work | 82% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1701 RC.4 release gate session recovery — assess PR #175 CR bypass blocker and CI status across main and PR #175 branches (Oct 23, 11:22 PM)\nS1707 RC.4 release gate — monitoring CI for PR #175 (CR bypass fix needed) and main branch while holding merge pending blocker resolution (Oct 23, 11:25 PM)\nS1709 RC.4 release gate — PR #175 CR bypass fix blocked on safe-boundary handoff; monitoring main CI while waiting for claim transfer confirmation (Oct 23, 11:26 PM)\nS1718 Kimi agent handover for agent.ts — monitoring CI for PR #240 refreshed branch while main CI run 40227786412 completes (Oct 23, 11:30 PM)\n### Oct 25, 2026\nS1723 Kimi agent waiting for agent.ts handover — PR #240 REPL checkpoint failure recovery review and CI monitoring (Oct 25, 8:05 PM)\nS1730 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error from nexus upgrade, and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 8:36 PM)\nS1733 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error and relationship to checkpoint fix shipped in RC7 (Oct 25, 9:41 PM)\nS1731 RC7 candidate PR #241 — source verification, independent review, and CI monitoring through linux-x86_64 packaging job (Oct 25, 9:57 PM)\nS1736 RC6 upgrade failure diagnosis — \"Disallowed download origin\" error, checkpoint fix scope, and RC7 readiness (Oct 25, 10:20 PM)\nS1737 RC6 checkpoint failure root cause diagnosis, PR #241 RC7 CI monitoring, and terminal qualification environment preflight (Oct 25, 10:38 PM)\n### Oct 26, 2026\n22501 12:14a ○ RC7 Exact-RC Evidence Claim Held by codex-root on Branch codex/rc7-installed-package-evidence\n22502 12:15a ○ RC7 ACC-SUP-08 Reproducibility Evidence — Identical Artifact SHAs Across Both Runners and Published Release\n22503 \" ○ RC7 Candidate Review Agent Returned ACCEPT — Exact Diff SHA Verified\n22511 \" ○ v1.0.0 Release Qualification Gate Structure — Remaining Human/Independent Gates and Evidence Requirements\n22512 \" ○ Open PRs at RC7 State — Three Active PRs Including Readiness Reconciliation and Checkpoint Fix\n22513 \" ✓ RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claim Status Updated — RC7 ACC-SUP-08 PASS Recorded, Qualification Remains IN_PROGRESS\n22514 \" ○ PR #243 — Checkpoint Git Index Lock Fix Details and Independent Review ACCEPT\n22515 \" ○ PR #244 mergeStateStatus=BLOCKED — RC7 Readiness Reconciliation Doc PR Cannot Merge Yet\n22516 \" ○ Active Claims Snapshot — Checkpoint and Readiness Files Held by codex-root and /root Agents\n22517 \" ○ PR #243 Branch Commit History — Three-Commit Checkpoint Lock Fix Stack on RC7 Base\n22519 12:16a ○ PR #243 Diff SHA Verified Unchanged — All CI Checks Passed, Ready to Merge\n22520 \" ✓ PR #243 Merged — Checkpoint Git Index Lock Fix Landed on Main\n22522 \" ○ PR #243 Merge Confirmed — New Main Commit 0542312a, CI and CodeQL Started\n22523 \" ⚖ RC7 Remains Immutable Post-Checkpoint Fix — New RC Candidate Required if Source Gate Passes\n22527 12:18a ○ Open PR Inventory — 29 PRs Open, Large Dependabot Backlog Accumulating Alongside Release-Critical Items\n22530 12:19a ○ READINESS.md Current Checkpoint Content — RC7 State, Outstanding Evidence, and Next Steps\n22533 \" ○ check_requirements.mjs Passes on Post-PR-243 Main Commit 0542312a — Same Row Distribution as RC7\n22535 12:21a ○ Post-PR-243 Main CodeQL Run 40248550144 Completed Successfully\n22539 12:22a ○ RC7 Release Job Log — Attestation Action Versions and Nod…327 tokens truncated…e Job Created Two Separate Attestation Records — Tarball and SHA256SUMS Each Got Their Own Bundle\n22577 12:46a ○ RC7 SHA256SUMS Attestation (59728626) Certificate Fields Verified — Matches Tarball Attestation Identity\n22578 \" ○ RC7 Attestation Subjects Confirmed — Each Bundle Contains Exactly One Subject\n22579 \" ○ RC7 Attestation Bundle Download URL Is Restricted — Cannot Fetch via Web Crawler\n22580 \" ○ RC7 SHA256SUMS Attestation Verified Successfully — gh attestation verify Returns Exit 0\n22581 \" ✓ RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claim Updated — SHA256SUMS Attestation Discrepancy Corrected in Claims Record\n22582 12:58a ○ CI Run 40248550055 Completed Successfully — All Jobs Passed on Post-PR-243 Main\n22583 \" ○ PR #244 Branch v1/readiness-rc7-current-state Is Behind Main — Rebase Did Not Advance\n22584 \" ○ READINESS.md Current State — RC7 Post-PR-243 Source Gates Pass, Human Qualification Matrix 0/15\n22585 12:59a ✓ READINESS.md Current Checkpoint Refreshed — RC7 Post-PR-243 State, Both Attestations, and 0/15 Matrix Recorded\n22587 \" ○ PR #244 Branch Has Diverged from Remote — 8 Local Commits Ahead, 7 Behind Remote Head\n22589 \" ○ RC7 Installed Package Evidence Claim — codex-root Holds Branch at e924d75, Independent Review Pending\n22591 1:00a ✓ PR #244 Branch Committed — READINESS.md Checkpoint Reconciliation Commit 6dee7e6\n22593 \" ✓ PR #244 Branch Force-Pushed — Remote Updated from dfdd7068 to 6dee7e6\n22594 \" ○ PR #244 CI Checks Queued on New Head 6dee7e6 — Correctly Based on Post-PR-243 Main\n22596 \" ✓ PR #244 Description Updated — Reflects Post-PR-243 Checkpoint Refresh and Pending Independent Review\n22598 \" ✓ RELEASE_PUBLISHER Claim Updated — Post-PR-243 Source Gates PASS, PR #244 CI Queued\n22600 1:01a ○ PR #244 CI Runs Triggered — Two Workflow Runs Started on Head 6dee7e6\n22601 \" ○ KimiCode Defect Remediation Branch Has Uncommitted Changes — 4 Files Modified Including agent.ts\n22603 1:07a ○ PR #244 Diff SHA256 Computed — 1c329cfa42af4e27b328758dff2bb972181d3a111bfbb4d238667cbf3829cf17\n22604 \" ○ PR #244 Independent Review Request Sent to rc5_candidate_review Agent\n\nAccess 100k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem can't save memories right now.\n\nThe memory observer's allowance on claude is used up (since 2026-10-26T15:46:51.209Z).\n\nLatest error: Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.\n\nUntil the allowance resets or you add capacity, nothing from this session — or any\nother — will be remembered.\n\nRestarting will NOT help here: it does not replenish the allowance or clear the\npersisted cooldown — so please leave the worker alone.\nSwitch the observer to another provider in ~/.claude-mem/settings.json if you need\nmemory capture before the allowance resets.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user about this outage at the very start of your first reply,\nquoting the error above. Do NOT restart the worker and do NOT suggest restarting it.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/bda0c7d4-5966-4a50-8afa-79ea52d1efa2.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793038174.7710838,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
