14:- Local `git verify-tag v1.0.0-rc.9` returned a good signature from `Mike Holownych <mike.holownych@aisyndicate.io>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:18:- Published Linux x86-64 archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz`, 4,859,736 bytes, SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:19:- Published `SHA256SUMS` asset SHA-256: `70a80c9afb658c40506534e8fd80eb5e7b4cdd28431aa7fd0e285f136513ce77`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:20:- Downloading all listed release assets and running `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` succeeded for the archive and `compatibility.json`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:21:- `gh attestation verify` exited 0 for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS`, against repository `mikeholownych/nexus-code`. The verified archive attestation subject digest matches the published archive digest above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:28:NEXUS_VERSION=v1.0.0-rc.9 \\\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:35:The installed `--version` output was `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)`. Its `.provenance.json` records source revision `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` and archive SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. The installed `MANIFEST.sha256` file's SHA-256 is `4cf1b288892891c3db6135c8bb9919e4a21e871ef2c5be5c211e39fa13bde0e6`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`, the merge commit for PR #258. Exact-main CI [40363722642](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40363722642) and CodeQL [40363722565](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40363722565) completed SUCCESS on this exact commit; Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging/reproducibility/install checks passed. In a clean detached worktree at this SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirmed all components are `1.0.0-rc.9`, and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These are source-stage results; they do not satisfy deferred qualification gates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:7:**Integrated fixes:** PR #258 fixed the legacy local-provider credential-origin rebinding finding and updated RC9 notes. It was independently source-reviewed ACCEPT on exact diff SHA-256 `1e7a8414b112d895345b14a7e27b9d7769428df6c904cde09ff8ef0f23061fe1`; PR CI [40357724824](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40357724824) and CodeQL [40357724535](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40357724535) passed before merge. The review was a GitHub COMMENT, not an APPROVE. PR #256 local endpoint setup and PR #253 one-reset release-download retry are also integrated. Installed exact-RC provider and upgrade acceptance have not run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC9 candidate artifact:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` (tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6`) points to source commit `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature. GitHub's source-commit verification is `verified: true, reason: valid`, while its separate tag-object verification is `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) completed SUCCESS; the prerelease was published at 17:56 UTC. The archive `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz` is 4,859,736 bytes with SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`; all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`, and `gh attestation verify` exited 0 for the archive and checksum index. The archive identity and isolated desktop install are recorded in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). RC9 remains an unaccepted prerelease; exact-RC product qualification and stable `v1.0.0` release are not claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:13:**Qualification and terminal setup:** Held-out qualification has not started. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6423073471) received a metadata-only custody follow-up at 17:37 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded, and Agent Mail reports no active project window identities. No private corpus payloads were accessed. The Ubuntu desktop `ubuntu-desktop` is reachable over strict-host-key SSH; GitHub CLI authentication is present, the GNOME Wayland session is active, and xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are installed. The GNOME Shell screenshot D-Bus service is available; standalone screenshot utilities are absent, so evidence capture can use the desktop screenshot UI or supplied helper. RC9 installation details are recorded in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). The package is installed in the separate prefix `~/.local/nexus-rc9-qualification`; its binary reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)` and its provenance record contains the verified archive SHA-256. The terminal harness and screenshot helper are staged on the desktop under `~/.cache/nexus-rc9-terminal-matrix`; the 15-cell procedure is in `START-HERE.md`. The human terminal matrix remains 0/15 until an operator records every real terminal/size cell and required screenshots. Automated PTY checks cannot replace this evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source gates are green, and the RC9 artifact is published, verified, and installed. Independent held-out custody, exact-RC qualification, provider/standalone runs, cross-runner checks, the human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain pending.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:50:**RC8 upgrade diagnosis and installed artifact:** The attempted RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC7's updater rejects GitHub's signed release-asset redirect; its error also included the full signed URL. The published RC8 source and packaged upgrade.js accept HTTPS only for the restricted GitHub release-asset path and report only the origin on errors. On the local mike-dev installation, nexus --version reports 1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939) under isolated HOME; the installed package manifest passes, and its recorded archive digest matches the published RC8 Linux archive digest sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e. The downloaded archive and SHA256SUMS both passed gh attestation verify; the archive checksum matched the release index. A synthetic runtime probe of the installed RC8 validator accepted the release-asset path and rejected a generic path and HTTP. These checks establish the RC8 fix and this install's integrity; they are not a qualification run. RC8 remains based on bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752, before current main, so it is not the exact candidate for current-source acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:151:**Release state:** GitHub published signed prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7`; signed tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`. Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) succeeded. The published Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `7b8a5fd1d214919ae939275e59b76406d393fae31cdf4b184c33883b02dc64a9`. RC7 is an unaccepted prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is not published.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:155:**RC7 artifact evidence:** The tag's release workflow produced the public assets and attestations. `gh attestation verify` passed for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS` under the exact repository, workflow, tag, and source constraints; the checksum-index attestation is [59728626](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/attestations/59728626). Cross-runner workflow [40248074777](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40248074777) passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Both manifests validated, and the archive, checksum manifest, notices, compatibility file, installer, and CycloneDX SBOM matched byte-for-byte across the two runner outputs and the public release. An isolated install reports `1.0.0-rc.7 (431cb194931f)`. These are artifact and installation checks, not product qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:193:**RC3 artifact publication and provenance:** The annotated tag object is `dd68c222c57d0be0a4245a5b88092ff9df69201f`; its PGP signature verified good and it points to the source commit above. Release workflow [39927176480](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39927176480) completed successfully and published the [v1.0.0-rc.3 prerelease](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.3). The workflow-produced Linux x86-64 archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.3.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `efb446d2760f2e1aa7890e9d786b8a2ba8e4ebb784fbcac1e66afe827428864d`; `SHA256SUMS` is `9288edb4655a19caa40e1598c0a642ab7f7e93aafbb187c2bfc8cfa9e19f116f`; the CycloneDX SBOM is `3a3176b4b3890c1bc07fb7b3acd80f7372f043819e6a8b296346d014b07f9d3a`. Downloaded checksums and SBOM sidecars passed. GitHub attestations for the archive and `SHA256SUMS` verified against the Release workflow, run `39927176480`, tag `v1.0.0-rc.3`, and source `1b9791f`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:403:- The earlier corpus author supplied pilot overlay v18 at `/tmp/nexus-v1-heldout-author/DEC-05-v1-blackbox-dev-v18` (`SHA256SUMS.json` digest `e830c82c60a7767d4d235cc53764d8298abadc2d22107a5e6ee7ed3664509dd4`), with seven fixture tasks migrated and 33 unmigrated. That overlay remains unsealed historical pilot material and is superseded by the sealed 40-task external-repository corpus `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, PR #16).\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:481:- Release workflow [40193772994](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40193772994) completed successfully and published `v1.0.0-rc.5` as a prerelease. The archive SHA-256 is `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`; `SHA256SUMS` SHA-256 is `2206b35a0aed8a4b9635012c0ad55a6eae34d12fe3255c53d43ab8b1d8e7a8c1`.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":886527628}},"started_at_ms":1793038179507,"completed_at_ms":1793038180394}}
