iedChangesPending=true`. This is useful exploratory dogfood feedback only, not exact-RC, requirement, or acceptance evidence.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md b/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md\nindex 0b07faf..9cc9dfe 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md\n@@ -17,7 +17,8 @@\n - Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) completed successfully. The prerelease was published at 2026-10-26 17:56:16 UTC.\n - Published Linux x86-64 archive: `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.9.tar.gz`, 4,859,736 bytes, SHA-256 `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`.\n - Published `SHA256SUMS` asset SHA-256: `70a80c9afb658c40506534e8fd80eb5e7b4cdd28431aa7fd0e285f136513ce77`.\n-- Downloading all listed release assets and running `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` succeeded for the archive and `compatibility.json`.\n+- All 9 downloaded release assets matched the SHA-256 digests advertised for those assets by the GitHub Release API.\n+- The separate `SHA256SUMS` file contains entries for the Linux archive and `compatibility.json`; `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` succeeded for both entries. It does not cover all 9 release assets.\n - `gh attestation verify` exited 0 for both the archive and `SHA256SUMS`, against repository `mikeholownych/nexus-code`. The verified archive attestation subject digest matches the published archive digest above.\n \n ## Isolated desktop installation\n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n M docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md\n15ef30e docs(release): sanitize terminal host details\nc91a743 docs(release): fix evidence report formatting\n3aded08 docs(release): record RC9 attestation and install evidence\nb6d39ee docs(release): record RC9 artifact verification and install\nd508e19 docs(release): correct RC9 and dogfood checkpoint\n782b737 docs(release): record PR258 integration and current gates\n90537bf docs(release): record PR 256 exact-head checks\nfa396be docs(release): record exact-main source gate results\n1e33abd docs(release): record current CI and review status\nbb5dc76 docs(release): correct PR 256 CI status\ne51853c docs(release): record RC8 install and terminal preflight evidence\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\",\n  \"base\": \"4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566\",\n  \"scope\": \"Add a sanitized, source-bound record of published RC9 artifact checks and isolated desktop installation; no qualification acceptance claim.\",\n  \"head\": \"15ef30e7985454b05cfcd69a28dbf79dd755fe35\",\n  \"status\": \"Sanitized RC9 artifact/install record in PR259; GitHub tag-object bad_email is explicitly distinguished from local signature and source-commit verification; exact-head review and CI pending.\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-26T18:07:58Z\"\n}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"base\": \"4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\",\n  \"checks\": \"PR259 exact head 15ef30e; requirements enforcement PASS (123 rows; 12 exact-RC deferrals); diff-check PASS; CI40374929601 queued; CodeQL40374929207 in progress; prior heads superseded.\",\n  \"head\": \"15ef30e7985454b05cfcd69a28dbf79dd755fe35\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"independent_review\": \"Fresh read-only review requested from plan05_readonly_review at exact head 15ef30e7985454b05cfcd69a28dbf79dd755fe35, diff SHA-256 66a4e4c5f7cb76ec3d6f2dc932bdd46a583db044c6998e7f59997cf0aa39a273.\",\n  \"pr\": 259,\n  \"scope\": \"Update current readiness checkpoint with RC9 release verification, operator-run isolated installation, and staged human terminal procedure; add sanitized artifact/install evidence; preserve historical entries; no acceptance claim.\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-26T14:33:31Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-26T18:07:58Z\"\n}\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\",\"description\":\"Read this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is true. Params: list, includeClosed. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read(args: {\\n  // Also show done and dropped items and closed lists\\n  includeClosed?: boolean;\\n  // Read only this list\\n  list?: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\",\"description\":\"Your canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call appends one entry to a list. To-do item: fields {\\\"task\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"todo\\\" | \\\"doing\\\" | \\\"done\\\" | \\\"dropped\\\", ...details}. State on the list itself: any other fields (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\" closes the list). Returns what is still open in the list. Params: list (required), fields (required). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write(args: {\\n  // Keys to set. Include \\\"task\\\" to update a to-do item. Values are strings, numbers, booleans, or null to clear a key.\\n  fields: { [key: string]: string | number | boolean | null; };\\n  // The to-do list or tracked thing this entry belongs to, e.g. \\\"release\\\" or \\\"auth-refactor\\\"\\n  list: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793038198.347417}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
