{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:10:39.677Z","ordinal":396203,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17968-47bd-7532-b94c-725f6afb96bd","call_id":"call_598272491edb4019865317f2b5b83b3a","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #256 was merged at `1aa8832`; its exact head, `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, is an ancestor of current `origin/main` at `4cae11c`. The feature branch remains clean at `987c73a`, originally based on `ff34938`. [PR #256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256)\\n\\nThe commit fixed pending local-discovery cancellation and late activation, corrected the key-storage message, and isolated invalid provider catalog errors. Its credential-origin fix was incomplete: later review reproduced a legacy key reaching the newly selected endpoint. So that commit alone does not clear the security acceptance blocker.\\n\\nCI passed on PR #256, but GitHub records no reviews, and I found no independent acceptance of exact head `987c73a`. An accepted follow-up exists on branch `v1/defect-malformed-credential-origin` at `0571266`; it has no open PR and is not in current `main`.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for PR #259 at `15ef30e7985454b05cfcd69a28dbf79dd755fe35` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` (diff SHA-256 `66a4e4c5f7cb76ec3d6f2dc932bdd46a583db044c6998e7f59997cf0aa39a273`).\\n\\n[READINESS.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9) says “all release assets match `SHA256SUMS`.” The packaging script creates that checksum file for only the archive and `compatibility.json` ([package-linux.sh](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/scripts/package-linux.sh:210)); the evidence note likewise reports checksum validation for those two items ([rc9_artifact_install.md](/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:20)). Narrow the readiness claim to those checksum-covered files.\\n\\nThe tag-verification distinction is accurately stated, and the terminal matrix remains 0/15 with acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793038239.6776154}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
