{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:11:59.390Z","ordinal":396268,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3c5f4e17-cb07-4c62-9bef-04fe74418f27","process_id":"76292","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '140,168p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg -n \"nvidia/nemotron|providers verify --provider openrouter\" docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | head -60; ls /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CLOUD 2>/dev/null && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CLOUD/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '140,168p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg -n \"nvidia/nemotron|providers verify --provider openrouter\" docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | head -60; ls /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CLOUD 2>/dev/null && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CLOUD/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:488:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:4:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:58:02.236Z\",\"requestId\":\"e5ad5e55-85bd-41a9-b304-459832133c3c\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/n