{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:55.215Z","ordinal":396864,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9d12632c81a08be9ce2bad1ae1cd","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found why the direct-script attempt remained unverified: the acceptance gate supports Node’s native `--test` runner for independent baseline/pass-after evidence. I’m making one corrected, clean attempt with that runner and an unchanged acceptance test; I’ll stop repeating if the same gate still rejects it."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793039634466,"completed_at_ms":1793039635215}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:55.219Z","ordinal":396865,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9d12632c81a08be9ce2bad1ae1cd","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I found why the direct-script attempt remained unverified: the acceptance gate supports Node’s native `--test` runner for independent baseline/pass-after evidence. I’m making one corrected, clean attempt with that runner and an unchanged acceptance test; I’ll stop repeating if the same gate still rejects it.","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793039634.4217303,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9d12632c81a08be9ce2bad1ae1cd","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a1797d-9313-7bb1-bfd6-e205536eaa34","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19523}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:34:00.527Z","ordinal":396866,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9d132cd881a0a5f01fd6b599d11e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3984a0f59a754be2a04187d62285969a","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes mike@10.0.8.3 bash -s <<'REMOTE'\\nset -eu\\ntask_dir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/nexus-e5-rc9-openrouter-node-test.XXXXXX)\\nmkdir -p \\\"$task_dir/src\\\"\\ncat > \\\"$task_dir/README.md\\\" <<'EOF'\\n# E5 synthetic task: strict port parsing\\n\\nFix `src/port.mjs` so `parsePort(raw)` follows this contract:\\n- `undefined` or the empty string selects the default port 3000.\\n- Surrounding whitespace is allowed for a decimal integer string.\\n- Other inputs must consist entirely of decimal digits after trimming; partial parses, signs, fractions, and non-string values are invalid.\\n- The parsed port must be an integer from 1 through 65535 inclusive.\\n- Invalid input throws an Error; do not silently replace invalid input with the default.\\nThe operator acceptance test is `port.test.mjs`. Do not change README.md or port.test.mjs. Make only the source fix and run `node --test port.test.mjs`.\\nEOF\\ncat > \\\"$task_dir/src/port.mjs\\\" <<'EOF'\\nexport function parsePort(raw) {\\n  if (raw === undefined || raw === \\\"\\\") return 3000;\\n  const port = Number.parseInt(raw, 10);\\n  return Number.isNaN(port) ? 3000 : port;\\n}\\nEOF\\ncat > \\\"$task_dir/port.test.mjs\\\" <<'EOF'\\nimport test from \\\"node:test\\\";\\nimport assert from \\\"node:assert/strict\\\";\\nimport { parsePort } from \\\"./src/port.mjs\\\";\\n\\ntest(\\\"default and valid decimal ports\\\", () => {\\n  assert.equal(parsePort(undefined), 3000);\\n  assert.equal(parsePort(\\\"\\\"), 3000);\\n  assert.equal(parsePort(\\\" 8080 \\\"), 8080);\\n  assert.equal(parsePort(\\\"1\\\"), 1);\\n  assert.equal(parsePort(\\\"65535\\\"), 65535);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"invalid values are rejected\\\", () => {\\n  for (const invalid of [null, 0, \\\"0\\\", \\\"65536\\\", \\\"-1\\\", \\\"+80\\\", \\\"80abc\\\", \\\"3.5\\\", \\\"abc\\\"]) {\\n    assert.throws(() => parsePort(invalid), Error, `expected invalid input ${String(invalid)} to throw`);\\n  }\\n});\\nEOF\\ncd \\\"$task_dir\\\"\\ngit init -q\\ngit config user.name \\\"Nexus Qualification\\\"\\ngit config user.email \\\"qualification@example.invalid\\\"\\ngit add README.md src/port.mjs port.test.mjs\\ngit commit -qm \\\"baseline synthetic port parser defect\\\"\\nif node --test port.test.mjs > /tmp/nexus-e5-rc9-node-test-baseline.log 2>&1; then\\n  printf \\\"ERROR: baseline unexpectedly passed\\\\n\\\"\\n  exit 2\\nfi\\nif ! grep -q \\\"not ok\\\" /tmp/nexus-e5-rc9-node-test-baseline.log; then\\n  printf \\\"ERROR: baseline failed for an unexpected reason\\\\n\\\"\\n  head -10 /tmp/nexus-e5-rc9-node-test-baseline.log\\n  exit 3\\nfi\\nprintf \\\"Task directory: %s\\\\n\\\" \\\"$task_dir\\\"\\nprintf \\\"Baseline outcome: Node test runner confirmed failing test cases\\\\n\\\"\\nREMOTE\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026\",\"yield_time_ms\":30000,\"max_output_tokens\":500});\ntext(r.output)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793039635.1773226}}}
