{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:37:56.921Z","ordinal":397013,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9e02b1f481a08414052a39d7a13b","usage":{"input_tokens":222753,"cached_input_tokens":219392,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":155,"reasoning_output_tokens":26,"total_tokens":222908},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":73590729,"cached_input_tokens":72774144,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":250209,"reasoning_output_tokens":142755,"total_tokens":73840938},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7296184499,"cached_input_tokens":7218799360,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20860093,"reasoning_output_tokens":12093879,"total_tokens":7317044592}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:37:58.722Z","ordinal":397014,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6e02bf5d-d49a-43c0-ab05-9d5b7d7f6d3c","process_id":"18813","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '55,104p' docs/USER_MANUAL.md; sed -n '240,320p' cli/src/upgrade.ts; rg -n \"install.sh|--prefix\" docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence scripts | head -80"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc8-install-terminal-20261026","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '55,104p' docs/USER_MANUAL.md","name":"USER_MANUAL.md","path":"docs/USER_MANUAL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '240,320p' cli/src/upgrade.ts","name":"upgrade.ts","path":"cli/src/upgrade.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'install.sh|--prefix' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md docs/v1.0.0/evidence scripts","query":"install.sh|--prefix","path":"READINESS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"nexus audit --tool run_command\n```\n\n### Exposing Nexus Tools via Model Context Protocol (MCP)\nTo expose Nexus Code's native Rust tools to external LLM clients (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Zed):\n```bash\nnexus serve-mcp --workspace /path/to/project\n```\nSee [MCP_GUIDE.md](MCP_GUIDE.md) for full configuration details.\n\n### Upgrading Nexus Code (`nexus upgrade` & `/upgrade`)\nTo check whether an update is available without making changes:\n```bash\nnexus upgrade --check\n```\nExit codes for `--check`:\n- `0`: Up to date (already on latest or requested version).\n- `1`: Update available.\n- `2`: Operational error (network, rate limit, release not found).\n\nTo perform an in-place upgrade to the latest published stable release:\n```bash\nnexus upgrade\n```\nPrompts for confirmation unless `--yes` is passed. In non-interactive environments (scripts or CI), `--yes` is mandatory to perform modifications.\n\nTo target an explicit release (including prereleases):\n```bash\nnexus upgrade --version v1.0.0\n```\n\n#### Recovery, Rollback and Backup Restoration\nNexus maintains a transaction journal (`$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade-journal.json`) and creates protected pre-migration configuration backups (mode `0600`) before modifications:\n\n- Recover from an interrupted upgrade using the transaction journal:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --recover\n  ```\n- Revert the launcher symlink to the previous installed version:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --rollback-binary\n  ```\n- Restore configuration from a pre-migration backup:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --restore-backup ~/.config/nexus/backups/config.env.bak\n  ```\n\nInside the interactive live TUI, run `/upgrade` or `/upgrade --check`. The TUI displays the installed vs target version, destination, and requires deliberate modal confirmation before modifying any files. Running TUI sessions continue uninterrupted on their loaded code and notify when a restart is required.\n\n---\n  hereDir?: string;\n  envPrefix?: string;\n}): InstalledProductInfo {\n  const nexusHome = customOptions?.nexusHome ?? process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\n  const here = customOptions?.hereDir ?? path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n  const envPrefix = customOptions?.envPrefix ?? process.env.NEXUS_PREFIX;\n\n  if (nexusHome) {\n    const resolvedHome = path.resolve(nexusHome);\n    const versionFile = path.join(resolvedHome, \"VERSION\");\n    let versionStr = \"unknown\";\n    if (fs.existsSync(versionFile)) {\n      try {\n        versionStr = fs.readFileSync(versionFile, \"utf8\").trim();\n      } catch {}\n    }\n    if (versionStr === \"unknown\") {\n      versionStr = getBuildIdentity().version;\n    }\n    const prefix = path.resolve(resolvedHome, \"../../..\");\n    const binLink = path.join(prefix, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    const writeCheck = testWritable(resolvedHome);\n    const sem = parseSemver(versionStr);\n\n    const provFile = path.join(resolvedHome, \".provenance.json\");\n    let provRecord: ProvenanceRecord | undefined;\n    if (fs.existsSync(provFile)) {\n      try {\n        provRecord = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(provFile, \"utf8\"));\n      } catch {}\n    }\n\n    if (provRecord && !provRecord.managed && provRecord.packageManager) {\n      return {\n        version: versionStr,\n        normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(versionStr) : versionStr,\n        semver: sem,\n        isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n        provenance: \"package-manager\",\n        installRoot: resolvedHome,\n        prefix,\n        binLink,\n        writable: false,\n        detail: `Installed via package manager (${provRecord.packageManager}). Use ${provRecord.packageManager} to update.`,\n        provenanceRecord: provRecord,\n      };\n    }\n\n    return {\n      version: versionStr,\n      normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(versionStr) : versionStr,\n      semver: sem,\n      isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n      provenance: \"packaged\",\n      installRoot: resolvedHome,\n      prefix,\n      binLink,\n      writable: writeCheck.writable,\n      permissionError: writeCheck.error,\n      detail: provRecord ? `Packaged installation at ${resolvedHome} (verified provenance)` : `Legacy packaged installation at ${resolvedHome}`,\n      provenanceRecord: provRecord,\n    };\n  }\n\n  // Check if running from a development checkout\n  const candidateCheckoutRoot = path.resolve(here, \"../..\");\n  const isGitRepo = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \".git\"));\n  const hasCargo = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \"core\", \"Cargo.toml\"));\n  const hasRootPackage = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \"package.json\"));\n\n  if (isGitRepo || (hasCargo && hasRootPackage)) {\n    const buildInfo = getBuildIdentity();\n    const sem = parseSemver(buildInfo.version);\n    return {\n      version: buildInfo.string,\n      normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(buildInfo.version) : buildInfo.version,\n      semver: sem,\n      isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n      provenance: \"development\",\n      installRoot: candidateCheckoutRoot,\n      prefix: envPrefix || path.join(process.env.HOME || \"\", \".local\"),\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is bound to that exact commit: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. The requirements-enforcement and version synchronization checks previously passed on exact `ff349383`; the version remains `1.0.0-rc.8`. Do not call source CI complete until the Linux job terminates successfully.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:54:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:127:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) passed on that exact commit. CI [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) has Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices passed; its Linux x86-64 job is still running `npm --prefix cli test` and has no final conclusion. Requirements enforcement and Linux packaging are not yet verified for this run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:376:- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` on the corrected exact source tree completed under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 with **1,104 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** across 193 suites; shell exit 0; reported duration 1,615,366 ms. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-corrected.log`. Build ran before the suite, and the source tree was committed without changes while the test ran, binding the result to `4439b7e`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:382:- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:388:- A focused Node 20.20.2 run of `npm --prefix cli test -- test/security_gates.test.ts` against PR #10's pre-fix snapshot reproduced an SBOM test failure: nested `npx` exited with `ENOENT` for the absent `cli/lib` directory after inheriting npm's `npm_config_local_prefix` and `npm_config_prefix`. A prior supplemental command labeled Node 20 was invalid because `node` resolved to Node 24; it is not counted as Node 20 evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:389:- PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132` (and `59dc522` on integration) clears the lowercase and uppercase prefix variables only for the nested CycloneDX `npx` call and adds a regression that injects the lowercase values set by `npm --prefix cli`. The focused security-gate suite then passed 10/10 under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and 10/10 under Node 24.11.1/npm 11.19.0. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and staged Gitleaks also passed. Independent review accepted the scoped fix and confirmed Linux CI compatibility.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:490:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:33:  --prefix none \\\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:157:  npm --prefix \"${ROOT_DIR}/cli\" sbom \\\nscripts/check_notices.mjs:90:  ['tree', '--locked', '--manifest-path', coreManifest, '--prefix', 'none'],\nscripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh:37:  --prefix=/usr \\\nscripts/package-linux.sh:34:npm --prefix \"$ROOT/cli\" ci\nscripts/package-linux.sh:35:npm --prefix \"$ROOT/cli\" run build\nscripts/package-linux.sh:65:npm ci --omit=dev --prefix \"$PKG/lib/cli\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:134:npm ci --ignore-scripts --prefix \"$RELEASE_TOOLS\"\nscripts/package-linux.sh:215:# Publish install.sh as release asset (REQ-REL-109)\nscripts/package-linux.sh:216:cp \"$ROOT/install.sh\" \"$OUT/install.sh\"\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:13:const RELEASE_ASSETS = [\"compatibility.json\", \"SHA256SUMS\", \"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt\", \"sbom.cdx.json\", \"install.sh\"];\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:72:| REQ-REL-11 | D3/R11 | Versioned install, upgrade, rollback; LICENSE/SECURITY/CHANGELOG | TOP_TIER D3/D4 | install.sh + GitHub prereleases v0.1.0-alpha.1/.2 with SHA256SUMS; LICENSE present; **no SECURITY.md, no CHANGELOG, no rollback procedure, no signing/provenance** | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:254:Spot-checks: grep in cli/src/{plugins,mcp,agent,tools,security,tester,parser,worktree,client,index,sandbox}.ts, cli/src/core/{capabilities,egress,candidate}.ts, core/src/{file_ops,search}.rs, scripts/{security_gates,generate_sbom}.sh, install.sh, .github/workflows/*.yml\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:16:| trusted-broker-bundle/install.sh | targeted read (lines 1-60, plus grep for the verify, manifest and prior-install steps) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:31:| demo/test/*.mjs | executed (`npm test --prefix demo`) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:78:| CON-001 | S1 (contest) | Judge deploy / CI | docs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST.md:48-49; .github/workflows/ci.yml:29-39; experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice/package.json:5-9, cloudflare.config.ts:6-12, src/index.ts:3-4,66-95 | RUNTIME + SOURCE. The documented `npm run typecheck/deploy --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice` targets the **Experiment-1 Worker** `artifacts-first-repo`. That Worker has hard-coded namespace `nexus-exp1-oct02`, an **unauthenticated POST /create**, and an unauthenticated GET /readback that returns content. The built `worker.config.json` has name=artifacts-first-repo and namespace=nexus-exp1-oct02; the bundle has 0 occurrences of \"work-state\". The NEXUS_CF_* variables set in CI are inert. The contest Worker (agent-collab-worker/) has no npm scripts, no lockfile, and is never typechecked, built or deployed by any documented command. | A judge following the guide deploys the wrong service: unauthenticated, bound to the operator's namespace name, and lacking `/work-state`. The CI \"contest contract\" job is green without covering the submitted Worker. | Before submission: add build/typecheck/deploy scripts and a lockfile to agent-collab-worker (or point the root config at it); fix CONTEST.md; make CI build the contest Worker. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:82:| CON-005 | S2 (contest) | Broker install | trusted-broker-bundle/BUNDLE.sha256:11; trusted-object-manifest.json:113-121; install.sh:52-60,92 | RUNTIME: `sha256sum -c BUNDLE.sha256` gives `./broker/demo-transport.mjs: FAILED` (actual 0ad7c7da…, recorded 3238d2e9…). install.sh:92 runs `sha256sum --check` under `set -e`, so **the committed bundle cannot be installed**; it fails closed. The installer also *requires* a prior install at /opt/nexus-cloudflare-broker with a pinned prior manifest (:5-7,52-60). There is no fresh-install path. | The parameterized transport has never been reviewed or hashed into the trust root. The \"upgrade-only\" installer cannot bootstrap a clean host. | Re-hash after review. Add a fresh-install mode. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:104:npm ci --prefix demo && npm ci --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:106:  npm run typecheck --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice   # -> rc 0\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:107:... npm run build --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice    # -> built 4.95 kB\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:132:- **The vendored Node trust root checks out (RUNTIME):** the pubring sha256 matches the README; `gpgv` gives \"Good signature\" from 5BE8A3F6…; the SHASUMS line for linux-x64 matches install.sh:11; the manifest sha matches install.sh:13. The installer fails closed on a checksum mismatch.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:147:  3. Run `npm run demo:cloudflare --prefix demo -- --agents real --fast`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:166:| CON-R3 | Fresh-install path for the broker (no prior-manifest requirement); uid and HOME as build parameters; BUNDLE.sha256 and manifest regenerated after review | workflow | BLOCKER (contest) | `install.sh --fresh` on a clean VM, followed by `post-install-qualify.py`, passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:189:- In snap: `npm ci --prefix demo`, `npm ci --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice`, `npm audit --prefix …slice`, and `npm test --prefix demo`. All demo tests passed: adapter PASS, restricted-executor PASS (uid 65534, caps 0), runner 1/1, smoke 8 stages.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:9:| install.sh | full read + RUNTIME (6 install runs, scratch HOMEs, + docker ubuntu:22.04) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:88:env -i HOME=$S/h1 PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=$S bash -c 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2 sh'\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:28:  - `discoverVerifier` (tester.ts:109-138) needs repository evidence and is used for the completion oracle, the baseline and the prompt. Its order is: Makefile `^test:` → `make test`; Cargo.toml / core/Cargo.toml → `cargo test`; package.json `scripts.test` (not \"no test specified\") → `npm test` (also `npm --prefix cli test`); pyproject/setup.py → `pytest`; go.mod → `go test ./...`; `test_*.py` in tests/, test/ or the root → `python3 -m unittest discover`; otherwise null (NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER → UNVERIFIED).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:26:The official `install.sh` asset was run on the connected Ubuntu/GNOME desktop with:\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:31:NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 sh install.sh\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":803620065}},"started_at_ms":1793039877918,"completed_at_ms":1793039878722}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:37:59.681Z","ordinal":397015,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17981-4e01-70b0-854b-c67eb43832dd","call_id":"call_ef65c904787942a7b065525cf9995783","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5207)\nTotal output lines: 175\n\nnexus audit --tool run_command\n```\n\n### Exposing Nexus Tools via Model Context Protocol (MCP)\nTo expose Nexus Code's native Rust tools to external LLM clients (Claude Desktop, Cursor, Zed):\n```bash\nnexus serve-mcp --workspace /path/to/project\n```\nSee [MCP_GUIDE.md](MCP_GUIDE.md) for full configuration details.\n\n### Upgrading Nexus Code (`nexus upgrade` & `/upgrade`)\nTo check whether an update is available without making changes:\n```bash\nnexus upgrade --check\n```\nExit codes for `--check`:\n- `0`: Up to date (already on latest or requested version).\n- `1`: Update available.\n- `2`: Operational error (network, rate limit, release not found).\n\nTo perform an in-place upgrade to the latest published stable release:\n```bash\nnexus upgrade\n```\nPrompts for confirmation unless `--yes` is passed. In non-interactive environments (scripts or CI), `--yes` is mandatory to perform modifications.\n\nTo target an explicit release (including prereleases):\n```bash\nnexus upgrade --version v1.0.0\n```\n\n#### Recovery, Rollback and Backup Restoration\nNexus maintains a transaction journal (`$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade-journal.json`) and creates protected pre-migration configuration backups (mode `0600`) before modifications:\n\n- Recover from an interrupted upgrade using the transaction journal:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --recover\n  ```\n- Revert the launcher symlink to the previous installed version:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --rollback-binary\n  ```\n- Restore configuration from a pre-migration backup:\n  ```bash\n  nexus upgrade --restore-backup ~/.config/nexus/backups/config.env.bak\n  ```\n\nInside the interactive live TUI, run `/upgrade` or `/upgrade --check`. The TUI displays the installed vs target version, destination, and requires deliberate modal confirmation before modifying any files. Running TUI sessions continue uninterrupted on their loaded code and notify when a restart is required.\n\n---\n  hereDir?: string;\n  envPrefix?: string;\n}): InstalledProductInfo {\n  const nexusHome = customOptions?.nexusHome ?? process.env.NEXUS_HOME;\n  const here = customOptions?.hereDir ?? path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));\n  const envPrefix = customOptions?.envPrefix ?? process.env.NEXUS_PREFIX;\n\n  if (nexusHome) {\n    const resolvedHome = path.resolve(nexusHome);\n    const versionFile = path.join(resolvedHome, \"VERSION\");\n    let versionStr = \"unknown\";\n    if (fs.existsSync(versionFile)) {\n      try {\n        versionStr = fs.readFileSync(versionFile, \"utf8\").trim();\n      } catch {}\n    }\n    if (versionStr === \"unknown\") {\n      versionStr = getBuildIdentity().version;\n    }\n    const prefix = path.resolve(resolvedHome, \"../../..\");\n    const binLink = path.join(prefix, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    const writeCheck = testWritable(resolvedHome);\n    const sem = parseSemver(versionStr);\n\n    const provFile = path.join(resolvedHome, \".provenance.json\");\n    let provRecord: ProvenanceRecord | undefined;\n    if (fs.existsSync(provFile)) {\n      try {\n        provRecord = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(provFile, \"utf8\"));\n      } catch {}\n    }\n\n    if (provRecord && !provRecord.managed && provRecord.packageManager) {\n      return {\n        version: versionStr,\n        normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(versionStr) : versionStr,\n        semver: sem,\n        isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n        provenance: \"package-manager\",\n        installRoot: resolvedHome,\n        prefix,\n        binLink,\n        writable: false,\n        detail: `Installed via package manager (${provRecord.packageManager}). Use ${provRecord.packageManager} to update.`,\n        provenanceRecord: provRecord,\n      };\n    }\n\n    return {\n      version: versionStr,\n      normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(versionStr) : versionStr,\n      semver: sem,\n      isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n      provenance: \"packaged\",\n      installRoot: resolvedHome,\n      prefix,\n      binLink,\n      writable: writeCheck.writable,\n      permissionError: writeCheck.error,\n      detail: provRecord ? `Packaged installation at ${resolvedHome} (verified provenance)` : `Legacy packaged installation at ${resolvedHome}`,\n      provenanceRecord: provRecord,\n    };\n  }\n\n  // Check if running from a development checkout\n  const candidateCheckoutRoot = path.resolve(here, \"../..\");\n  const isGitRepo = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \".git\"));\n  const hasCargo = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \"core\", \"Cargo.toml\"));\n  const hasRootPackage = fs.existsSync(path.join(candidateCheckoutRoot, \"package.json\"));\n\n  if (isGitRepo || (hasCargo && hasRootPackage)) {\n    const buildInfo = getBuildIdentity();\n    const sem = parseSemver(buildInfo.version);\n    return {\n      version: buildInfo.string,\n      normalizedVersion: sem ? normalizeTag(buildInfo.version) : buildInfo.version,\n      semver: sem,\n      isPrerelease: Boolean(sem && sem.prerelease.length > 0),\n      provenance: \"development\",\n      installRoot: candidateCheckoutRoot,\n      prefix: envPrefix || path.join(process.env.HOME || \"\", \".local\"),\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:37:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is bound to that exact commit: Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress at `npm --prefix cli test`. Post-merge CodeQL run [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. The requirements-enforcement and version synchronization checks previously passed on exact `ff349383`; the version remains `1.0.0-rc.8`. Do not call source CI complete until the Linux job terminates successfully.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:54:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acce…2207 tokens truncated… experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice   # -> rc 0\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:107:... npm run build --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice    # -> built 4.95 kB\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:132:- **The vendored Node trust root checks out (RUNTIME):** the pubring sha256 matches the README; `gpgv` gives \"Good signature\" from 5BE8A3F6…; the SHASUMS line for linux-x64 matches install.sh:11; the manifest sha matches install.sh:13. The installer fails closed on a checksum mismatch.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:147:  3. Run `npm run demo:cloudflare --prefix demo -- --agents real --fast`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:166:| CON-R3 | Fresh-install path for the broker (no prior-manifest requirement); uid and HOME as build parameters; BUNDLE.sha256 and manifest regenerated after review | workflow | BLOCKER (contest) | `install.sh --fresh` on a clean VM, followed by `post-install-qualify.py`, passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:189:- In snap: `npm ci --prefix demo`, `npm ci --prefix experiments/cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice`, `npm audit --prefix …slice`, and `npm test --prefix demo`. All demo tests passed: adapter PASS, restricted-executor PASS (uid 65534, caps 0), runner 1/1, smoke 8 stages.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:9:| install.sh | full read + RUNTIME (6 install runs, scratch HOMEs, + docker ubuntu:22.04) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:66:| REL-08 | S3 | installer, latest path | install.sh:21-24 | RUNTIME. Without NEXUS_VERSION: `curl: (22) ... 404` / `nexus installer: could not find latest stable release.` (only prereleases exist). The same message appears for API rate-limit (60/h unauthenticated) or network failure. There is no hint to set NEXUS_VERSION and no list of available prereleases. | The first-time \"omit version\" path fails opaquely until v1.0.0 exists, and later under rate limiting. | Tell the 404 apart from other errors. On 404 say \"no stable release yet; use NEXUS_VERSION=vX (latest prerelease: …)\". Fall back to the `releases/latest/download` redirect, which avoids the API. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:67:| REL-09 | S3 | integrity | install.sh:33-35; release.yml:44-48 | SOURCE. SHA256SUMS is fetched from the same release as the archive. There is no signature, cosign/sigstore, or GitHub build-provenance attestation, and the installer script itself is served from mutable `main`. | A compromise of the release or repo is not detectable. The checksum only protects against transport corruption. | v1: add `actions/attest-build-provenance` (verifiable with `gh attestation verify`), or minisign/cosign signatures. Offer an installer pinned to a tag URL. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:68:| REL-10 | S3 | installer, reinstall/repair | install.sh:48-49 | SOURCE + RUNTIME. When the version dir already exists, the verified archive is discarded and the existing tree is reused after checking only 3 executables + VERSION. A corrupted or partially edited install (e.g. deleted dist files) cannot be repaired by re-running the installer. Versions accumulate forever with no prune (two versions measured at 14M+15M). | Reinstall is not a repair path. Disk use grows. | Compare a manifest hash, or reinstall into a temp dir and swap. Add `NEXUS_FORCE=1`. Document or implement uninstall/prune (`nexus self uninstall`). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:69:| REL-11 | S4 | installer input validation | install.sh:26 | RUNTIME. `case v[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*` accepts `v1.2.3/../../x`. That string flows into the URL and into `VERSION_DIR=\"$PREFIX/lib/nexus/$VERSION\"`, though the run failed at download. The input is user-controlled only. | Low. Path traversal is possible if combined with a malicious base URL. | Use a strict SemVer regex via `grep -Eq '^v[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+(-[0-9A-Za-z.]+)?$'`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:70:| REL-12 | S4 | installer UX | install.sh:32-33 | RUNTIME. `curl -fL` without `-s` prints two progress meters inside a `curl \\| sh` pipeline. The PATH hint prints the expanded absolute path. The failure message on Ubuntu 22.04 (distro node v12.22.9) is correct but gives no install pointer. | Cosmetic. | Use `-fsSL --show-error`. Link Node 20 install docs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:88:env -i HOME=$S/h1 PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=$S bash -c 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/main/install.sh | NEXUS_VERSION=v0.1.0-alpha.2 sh'\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:121:- **Installer is safe by default.** It installs as non-root under `$HOME/.local`, never edits shell rc files, and never overwrites a foreign `nexus` (install.sh:41-47; covered by installer-smoke.sh:48-51). Checksum failure leaves the existing install unchanged (installer-smoke.sh:43-46). The symlink swap is atomic (`ln` + `mv -f`). Failures leave HOME untouched (RUNTIME, h2/h3).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/E_distribution.md:174:- Installer runs with `env -i HOME=<scratch>/h{1,2,3,3b,4} PATH=/usr/bin:/bin TMPDIR=<scratch> bash -c 'curl -fsSL …/install.sh | [NEXUS_VERSION=…] sh'`, covering alpha.2, none, v9.9.9, no-v, traversal, and alpha.1→alpha.2→alpha.1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:28:  - `discoverVerifier` (tester.ts:109-138) needs repository evidence and is used for the completion oracle, the baseline and the prompt. Its order is: Makefile `^test:` → `make test`; Cargo.toml / core/Cargo.toml → `cargo test`; package.json `scripts.test` (not \"no test specified\") → `npm test` (also `npm --prefix cli test`); pyproject/setup.py → `pytest`; go.mod → `go test ./...`; `test_*.py` in tests/, test/ or the root → `python3 -m unittest discover`; otherwise null (NO_APPLICABLE_VERIFIER → UNVERIFIED).\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:26:The official `install.sh` asset was run on the connected Ubuntu/GNOME desktop with:\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:31:NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 sh install.sh\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793039879.6814861}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
