 `1.0.0-rc.9`, and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These are source-stage results; they do not satisfy deferred qualification gates.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source gates are green, and the RC9 artifact is published, verified, and installed. Independent held-out custody, exact-RC qualification, provider/standalone runs, cross-runner checks, the human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain pending.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:26:**Authoritative source gates:** `origin/main` is `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`. Exact-main post-merge CI [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) completed SUCCESS on that commit across Node 22, Node 24, and Linux packaging, including the reproducibility build. Post-merge CodeQL [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. Requirements enforcement and `sync-version --check` passed on exact `ff349383`; 123 requirement rows remain with 12 explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. Components remain `1.0.0-rc.8`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:30:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 is a prior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:41:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (12:18 UTC). Private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished. No held-out payload was accessed or run. Exact-current-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 remains an older prerelease, not a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:54:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:62:**Candidate and publication state:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:72:**RC8 construction and reproducibility:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) was published at 07:26 UTC and resolves to the exact source commit above. Its Linux archive has GitHub asset digest `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. Cross-runner RC reproducibility workflow [40286712425](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40286712425) completed successfully against that exact tag, including Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builds and artifact comparison. An installed RC8 copy was also provenance-verified on the Ubuntu desktop in an isolated qualification prefix ([setup record](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3#issuecomment-6411066559)); this was not the user's normal Nexus installation and is not full installed-RC acceptance. The tag's local GPG signature verifies, but GitHub reports it as unverified (`bad_email`); the stable tag must use a signer identity that GitHub verifies against the signing key. The earlier RC6-to-RC7 upgrade attempt failed because RC6 rejected GitHub's signed release-asset redirect. The redirect allowlist and URL-secret redaction are present in RC8; the RC6 installation was not changed by the isolated RC8 check.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:76:The 06:24 checkpoint immediately below is retained as a historical snapshot; this update supersedes its CI conclusion, RC publication state, cross-runner status, and current blocker summary.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:89:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074`. CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. CI passed the Node 22/24 and Linux test matrices, requirements enforcement, security gates, package build and reproducibility, SBOM checks, and package/install smoke checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:99:**Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` remains `62e541c9e170a51d02420753f0807c14d65d7074` (PR #244 merge). CI run [40255529634](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529634) and CodeQL run [40255529667](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40255529667) both completed successfully on that exact commit. The CI run passed Node 22 and 24, Linux CLI and Rust tests, requirements enforcement, security gates, Linux package creation, reproducibility comparisons, SBOM validation, and package/install smoke checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:105:**RC and qualification:** GitHub prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.7` resolves to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`, before PR #243 and later main changes; its Linux archive SHA-256 is `367e9384e6de6df5801c3b015e7965becccb53b6b11ff94cf906da764724c58a`. The tag object contains a PGP signature, but GitHub reports the