t a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:54:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:62:**Candidate and publication state:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\n…6030 tokens truncated…mains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:335:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:338:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:345:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:351:- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:369:- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:438:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:457:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:466:4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:486:### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:490:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:502:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:1:name: Cross-runner RC reproducibility\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:59:            echo \"The selected RC predates or bypasses the locked notices tool and lock deprecation gate; cross-runner reproduction requires an RC whose tag includes them.\" >&2\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:211:            printf '## Cross-runner RC reproducibility: %s\\n\\n' \"$TARGET_TAG\"\n.github/workflows/repro.yml:214:            printf 'Both runner outputs match each other and the six selected reproducibility artifacts.\\n'\nci.yml\ncodeql.yml\nrelease.yml\nrepro.yml\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a","create_time":1793039997.2363522}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
