ifferentiate Nexus Code from competing AI coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex CLI, Aider, etc.).\\n    4 | >\\n    5 | > **Scope:** Architecture, UX, reliability, performance, extensibility, and ecosystem.\\n    6 | >\\n    7 | > **Method:** Deep codebase review of `cli/`, `core/`, `docs/`, and test infrastructure.\\n    8 | \\n    9 | ---\\n   10 | \\n   11 | ## 1. Multi-Agent Orchestration\\n   12 | \\n   13 | ### 1.1 Parallel Subagent Coordination\\n   14 | **Current state:** Single-agent, sequential execution. Subagents are \n[5] role=tool keys=['role', 'tool_call_id', 'name', 'content'] text={   \"content\": \"    1 | # Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\\n    2 | \\n    3 | This package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\\n    4 | \\n    5 | **Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** There are 31 blocker requirements, none of them met. Task-quality, standalone and real-terminal qualification are **unverified**: no qualifying evidence exists yet. The contest entry was submitted, is frozen, and is tracked separately.\\n    6 | \\n    7 | ## How to read it\\n    8 | \\n    9 | | If you want to… | Read |\\n   10 | |---|---|\\n   11 | | Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md)\n[6] role=tool keys=['role', 'tool_call_id', 'name', 'content'] text={   \"content\": \"    1 | # Compaction and task-continuity hardening (2026-10-13)\\n    2 | \\n    3 | Worktree `/home/mike/nexus-cc`, branch `feat/compaction-continuity` from `origin/main` a58f860.\\n    4 | `~/nexus-code` (installed launcher target) is left untouched: it held foreign uncommitted edits written during this\\n    5 | session (instruction-precedence work, plus a partial unbounded-budget change), so this work is isolated.\\n    6 | \\n    7 | Gateway reference (read-only): `/home/mike/Projects/aihost` fb1a2cd, deployed release t5820-gateway-b72a4f5.\\n    8 | \\n    9 | ## A. Continuity without a step ceiling\\n   10 | - [x] Default continuation unbounded (no 300-step / 120-min default); \n[7] role=tool keys=['role', 'tool_call_id', 'name', 'content'] text={   \"content\": \"    1 | # Nexus Code Architecture\\n    2 | \\n    3 | Nexus Code utilizes a split architecture designed for performance, modularity, and security:\\n    4 | \\n    5 | ```\\n    6 | ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n    7 | │                 TypeScript Orchestration Layer              │\\n    8 | │   • REPL / TUI Interface        • Agent Intelligence        │\\n    9 | │   • Skills Engine               • MCP JSON-RPC Client       │\\n   10 | │   • Plugin Lifecycle System     • Checkpoint & Undo Engine  │\\n   11 | │   • Secret Redactor             • Session Persistence       │\\n   12 | └──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘\\n   \n[8] role=assistant keys=['role', 'content', 'tool_calls'] text=Now let me dive deeper into the actual source code to understand what's implemented vs. what's planned:  \n[9] role=tool keys=['role', 'tool_call_id', 'name', 'content'] text={   \"base_path\": \"cli/src\",   \"entries\": [     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/oauth.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 14273     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/team.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 7300     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/search_web.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 4937     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/knowledge.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 6730     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/tester.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 16467     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/embeddings.ts\",       \"size_bytes\": 11512     },     {       \"is_dir\": false,       \"path\": \"cli/src/workspace_trust.ts\n[10] role=tool keys=['role', 'tool_call_id', 'name', 'content'] text={   \"base_path\": \"core/src\",   \"ent