{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T01:55:38.542Z","ordinal":397208,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0048cc9bc81a08146d7be84d420d0","usage":{"input_tokens":149145,"cached_input_tokens":135680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1562,"reasoning_output_tokens":1545,"total_tokens":150707},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":637491,"cached_input_tokens":487680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4455,"reasoning_output_tokens":3362,"total_tokens":641946},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7299421101,"cached_input_tokens":7221826560,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20880569,"reasoning_output_tokens":12106554,"total_tokens":7320301670}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T01:55:39.782Z","ordinal":397209,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17b12-0086-7ed2-8df6-d7cfde05c96c","call_id":"call_90bb657483fb4a27838ce8ebcb341331","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #256 was merged at `1aa8832`; its exact head, `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, is an ancestor of current `origin/main` at `4cae11c`. The feature branch remains clean at `987c73a`, originally based on `ff34938`. [PR #256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256)\\n\\nThe commit fixed pending local-discovery cancellation and late activation, corrected the key-storage message, and isolated invalid provider catalog errors. Its credential-origin fix was incomplete: later review reproduced a legacy key reaching the newly selected endpoint. So that commit alone does not clear the security acceptance blocker.\\n\\nCI passed on PR #256, but GitHub records no reviews, and I found no independent acceptance of exact head `987c73a`. An accepted follow-up exists on branch `v1/defect-malformed-credential-origin` at `0571266`; it has no open PR and is not in current `main`.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** for PR #259 at `8e92af1d2cee6efa9acb5a1b0026a1c6cc17f455` against base `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566` (diff SHA-256 `35c57f75e4dccea579bdc9b309deb277a7a1791ce5383051fc755795c848bd90`).\\n\\nThe wording now distinguishes all nine assets’ GitHub Release API digests from the two files covered by `SHA256SUMS`. The signature-status distinction is clear, and the readiness text keeps the terminal matrix at 0/15 and acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","create_time":1793066139.782322}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
