/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857374) and CodeQL [40401857568](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857568) were still running at this checkpoint; do not call the new main source gate complete yet. PR #261's exact-head CI [40396216500](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216500) and CodeQL [40396216414](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216414) passed before merge. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact head `20170c51ef483319aadb56b6b3f60943d227816b`, diff SHA-256 `26a6761810c00cbd3c05b9e05bdbcb36c3e1e97c78693fa4cfed7293ae88fce3`. The PR's first attempt exposed a CI-only TTY-size assumption in its regression test; this was corrected by rendering a buffer directly through Crossterm and the corrected exact-head checks passed.\n6-\n7:**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\n8-\n9:**RC9 artifact and installation record:** Tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6` targets the source above. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature; GitHub reports source-commit verification `verified: true, reason: valid` and tag-object verification `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) succeeded and published RC9 as a prerelease. All nine downloaded assets matched GitHub Release API digests. `SHA256SUMS` covers the archive and `compatibility.json` (both entries verified), and `gh attestation verify` passed for the archive and checksum index. The archive was installed in an isolated prefix and reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)`. Full artifact details remain in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). This is artifact/install evidence, not product acceptance.\n10-\n11:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n12-\n13:**Next:** Finish exact post-merge CI and CodeQL on `30f1b89`; then prepare a new immutable RC candidate from the validated current source and requalify all affected and still-open gates. Do not promote RC9 to stable.\n14-\n15----\n--\n17-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 15:16 UTC)\n18-\n19:**PR #256 exac