emain unestablished. No held-out payload was accessed or run. Exact-current-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 remains an older prerelease, not a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n40-\n41-The 14:35 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its current-main CI progress and PR #256 candidate/review status.\n--\n46-**Authoritative source and source gates:** origin/main is ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4, the merge commit for PR #255. PR #255's exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is still running Node 22/24 on ff349383; post-merge CodeQL [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. On the exact ff349383 worktree, requirements enforcement passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 rows explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check passed; components remain 1.0.0-rc.8. Do not treat post-merge CI as complete until run 40340228722 terminates successfully.\n47-\n48:**RC8 upgrade diagnosis and installed artifact:** The attempted RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC7's updater rejects GitHub's signed release-asset redirect; its error also included the full signed URL. The published RC8 source and packaged upgrade.js accept HTTPS only for the restricted GitHub release-asset path and report only the origin on errors. On the local mike-dev installation, nexus --version reports 1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868939) under isolated HOME; the installed package manifest passes, and its recorded archive digest matches the published RC8 Linux archive digest sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e. The downloaded archive and SHA256SUMS both passed gh attestation verify; the archive checksum matched the release index. A synthetic runtime probe of the installed RC8 validator accepted the release-asset path and rejected a generic path and HTTP. These checks establish the RC8 fix and this install's integrity; they are not a qualification run. RC8 remains based on bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752, before current main, so it is not the exact candidate for current-source acceptance.\n49-\n50:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\n51-\n52:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n53-\n54:The 13:45 checkpoint below remains as historical evidence; this update supersedes its origin/main, post-merge CI, installed-version, terminal-environment, and current blocker observations.\n55-\n56-## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 13:45 UTC)\n--\n60-**Candidate and publication state:** Public prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.8](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.8) remains the latest release, but its tag resolves to `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, before PR #252 and PR #254. Its Linux archive digest remains `sha256:bbded963a9bcaa9c0764b86d900f752c46ed364bfe30cc67e5bbf23b5fb5f48e`. RC8 reproducibility and isolated-prefix provenance checks apply only to that earlier artifact. It is not an accepted RC for current `main`; a candidate from the current source must be rebuilt and qualified. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The RC8 signing identity remains reported by GitHub as unverified (`bad_email`); stable signing must use a GitHub-verified identity.\n61-\n62:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open. The latest public metadata-only custody request (12:18 UTC) has no custodian response; do not access held-out payloads or begin the held-out run before independent custody acceptance. The last recorded human terminal matrix 