{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T01:57:30.333Z","ordinal":397296,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17b13-b05d-7023-bd19-2385424858c8","call_id":"call_8a9d354149464146aaaad81946cb8c32","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 28064)\nTotal output lines: 436\n\n5-**Current source and post-merge gates:** `origin/main` is `30f1b89a88bac81d8ab2d4f1e6800e1978a61f38`, the merge commit for PR #261. Its post-merge CI [40401857374](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857374) and CodeQL [40401857568](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40401857568) were still running at this checkpoint; do not call the new main source gate complete yet. PR #261's exact-head CI [40396216500](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216500) and CodeQL [40396216414](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40396216414) passed before merge. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact head `20170c51ef483319aadb56b6b3f60943d227816b`, diff SHA-256 `26a6761810c00cbd3c05b9e05bdbcb36c3e1e97c78693fa4cfed7293ae88fce3`. The PR's first attempt exposed a CI-only TTY-size assumption in its regression test; this was corrected by rendering a buffer directly through Crossterm and the corrected exact-head checks passed.\n6-\n7:**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\n8-\n9:**RC9 artifact and installation record:** Tag object `d211d1c7545d2dd629531e4f712e98a240a782c6` targets the source above. Local `git verify-tag` reports a good signature; GitHub reports source-commit verification `verified: true, reason: valid` and tag-object verification `verified: false, reason: bad_email`. Release workflow [40370485753](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40370485753) succeeded and published RC9 as a prerelease. All nine downloaded assets matched GitHub Release API digests. `SHA256SUMS` covers the archive and `compatibility.json` (both entries verified), and `gh attestation verify` passed for the archive and checksum index. The archive was installed in an isolated prefix and reports `1.0.0-rc.9 (4cae11cbc3b0)`. Full artifact details remain in [RC9 artifact verification](evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md). This is artifact/install evidence, not product acceptance.\n10-\n11:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n12-\n13:**Next:** Finish exact post-merge CI and CodeQL on `30f1b89`; then prepare a new immutable RC candidate from the validated current source and requalify all affected and still-open gates. Do not promote RC9 to stable.\n14-\n15----\n--\n17-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-26 15:16 UTC)\n18-\n19:**PR #256 exact-head update:** Following independent source-review acceptance of candidate `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, the reviewed branch was pushed as a normal fast-forward from `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) now targets exact `origin/main` `ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4`; its hosted CI run [40347686120](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40347686120) and CodeQL [40347686125](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40347686125) are in progress. Do not merge until every required exact-head check completes successfully and branch protection/review requirements are satisfied. The 15:15 checkpoint immediately below remains accurate as a pre-push snapshot and is superseded for PR head and CI status by this update.\n20-\n21-\n--\n26-**PR #256 local-provider candidate:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) still points to stale head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a` on base `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`. The refreshed local candidate is `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, based on current main `ff349383` through normal merge commit `9d898eb9bb77a87490d6fcf47b11260193b1e315`; it is not yet pushed and has no hosted exact-head checks. Independent source review ACCEPTed the full candidate diff (SHA-256 `7dc76f1d5d9ee3dd6ebd982eaefc250cd9862043de1f901bf73f58a26d43e376`) and confirmed prior findings are addressed. The implementer reports focused provider-connect tests 33/33, TUI Rust tests 6/6, TypeScript build, and `git diff --check` pass; no local full suite was run. Run exact PR checks after updating the public branch before integration.\n27-\n28:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN; its latest metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Independent private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. Current-candidate provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 is a prior prerelease, not a qualified candidate for this source; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n29-\n30-The 15:02 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its main CI and PR #256 review status.\n--\n37-**PR #256 local-provider change:** Public PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains at head `c3bb2235286a154280f8578458a4dc8570ae542a`, based on `b73b6ecaf753ff3eba8d5e1930ede7a471359421`; its exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed the same PTY model-picker test on Node 22 and 24 because the fixture navigated past the newly added Appliance row incorrectly. The owner’s local candidate `0490db3e9b85edd919fe7a05a4baf7b0b08ecdfa` was normally updated with current `main` by merge commit `9d898eb`; it is not pushed. Its focused build/test results (105/105) were reported by the implementer on the pre-merge head. Independent review of `0490db3` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED with four findings: pending Escape must cancel the matching setup, malformed credential-origin metadata must not rebind legacy keys, provisional-key UI copy is inaccurate, and invalid connected-provider URLs must not fail the entire catalog. The owner reacquired the relevant claims and is implementing regressions; no fixes are yet accepted on the refreshed branch.\n38-\n39:**Acceptance blockers:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (12:18 UTC). Private custody, evaluator-compatible corpus sealing, and held-out acceptance remain unestablished. No held-out payload was accessed or run. Exact-current-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. The human terminal matrix remains **0/15**. RC8 remains an older prerelease, not a current-source candidate; stable v1.0.0 is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authority remains granted but gated.\n40-\n41-The 14:35 checkpoint immediately below is retained as historical evidence; this update supersedes its current-main CI progress and PR #256 candidate/review status.\n--\n46-**Authoritative source and source gates:** origin/main is ff349383537b10ec6198ceb0961e833bd519c2b4, the merge commit for PR #255. PR #255's exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux packaging, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks passed. Post-merge CI run [40340228722](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228722) is still running Node 22/24 on ff349383; post-merge CodeQL [40340228417](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40340228417) passed. On the exact ff349383 worktree, requirements enforcement passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 rows explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check passed; components remain 1.0.0-rc.8. Do not treat post-merge CI as complete until run 40340228722 terminates successfully.\n47-\n48:**RC8 upgrade diagnosis and installed artifact:** The attempted RC6-to-RC7 upgrade failed because RC7's updater rejects GitHub's signed release-asset redirect; its error also included the full signed URL. The published RC8 source and packaged upgrade.js accept HTTPS only for the restricted GitHub release-asset path and report only the origin on errors. On the local mike-dev installation, nexus --version reports 1.0.0-rc.8 (bbafae868…23064 tokens truncated…eating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\n483-\n484-### Provider, PTY and reproducibility evidence\n--\n492-| Gate | State at RC5 | Next executable step / completion condition |\n493-|---|---|---|\n494:| T2/T3 held-out custody | Blocked. Issue #1 has no custodian reply; the public 40-task manifest does not establish private custody acceptance, and the legacy validator contract is incompatible with the current evaluator. No private payload was accessed or run. | Independent custodian confirms author/handoff, compatible immutable corpus or successor, validation, access separation, digests and custody acceptance; only then prepare and execute the approved runs. |\n495:| Evaluator resource/secret boundary | Synthetic current-source host preflight 10/10; no accepted qualification-host/custody result. | Complete independent host and custody acceptance before any held-out execution. |\n496:| Standalone profiles | Not run on the installed RC; T2 subset dependency remains unmet. | After custody and frozen configuration, execute §4.2 profiles and archive exact-artifact receipts. |\n497-| T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n498-| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n499:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n500:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n501:| Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n502-| Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\n503-\n504:Public metadata updates were added to issues [#3](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/3) and [#5](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/5). Publication authority remains granted but gated by acceptance; no additional authorization is requested here.\n\nRC10 docs paths on main\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/platform-e2/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/platform-e2/lifecycle/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/SHA256SUMS\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/manifest.json\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scr