a","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9ed40c6481a0b7aadaa0db76f511","order":19528,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17984-6ff7-7f43-aeaa-798967b1eba1","text":"The export shows a meaningful completion-truthfulness problem: Nexus’s stored outcome is `NOT_ESTABLISHED`, but the final message says the task is complete. I’m checking whether RC8’s source has a matching path that lets final prose overrule failed verification; the export itself does not bind this run to a specific RC artifact.","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016adf9ee9a96081a0bc7b60c31bd2e156","order":19529,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a17984-ca68-7a93-ac60-988780e94efc","text":"I reviewed the export. It **does not qualify as exact-RC8 evidence**: it has no candidate identity, worktree binding, or validation receipts, so the export cannot independently tie the run to RC8.\n\nIt records a concrete dogfooding failure: verification is `FAILED` because `make test` found no matching pre-change baseline; **no tests executed**, the deliverable is unbound, and unverified changes remain. The task outcome is `NOT_ESTABLISHED`, even though the final assistant message says “The task is complete.” That mismatch is worth tracking; the final prose should not imply success when the recorded outcome says otherwise.\n\nI would preserve this as **non-qualifying dogfood evidence**, not an accepted qualification result. The export’s SHA-256 is `6eee8181c62cfc278183ff65f27485d5c224046b6bc5107cc95b0c849a199d87`. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:777-789|note=[Nexus release evidence must be bound to exact revisions and qualification remains distinct from dogfood]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a178fa-f0ed-7ab3-bb71-477460bd1a0a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00460f99081a08fea38602890917c","order":19530,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b11-1c77-7721-b3f2-42835b2f29f1","text":"I’m resuming the release loop from current repository and GitHub state. The shared checkout is dirty, so I’ll keep it untouched and use an authorized isolated worktree for any changes.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae004a66d5881a0bf204535fc81e543","order":19532,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b12-2d32-7f71-8417-058637050ad7","text":"The source branch is now `main@16ee8ca`, with source CI, CodeQL, and exact-tag cross-runner reproducibility passing. RC10 qualification is active but incomplete: the scripted terminal/accessibility probes are partial, and the genuine 15-cell human matrix remains unrun. I’m checking ownership before choosing another qualification lane so I don’t collide with the active RC10 terminal work.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0052c24b481a0984e11f8b20878ac","order":19533,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b14-374a-79c3-b143-71603c50ed3c","text":"The Ubuntu desktop is reachable at `10.0.8.3` with its existing host key, GitHub authentication, Node 22, and all five terminal applications. RC10 is not installed in the isolated qualification prefix yet. I’ll install the published RC10 there with provenance required, without changing the default `nexus` launcher or starting any terminal acceptance cells.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0055bea3481a0aba53026e2de0a57","order":19534,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b14-f953-70d0-840d-508489af3ec0","text":"RC10 is now installed on Ubuntu desktop in a separate qualification prefix. The installer’s digest matched the tagged installer, provenance verification passed for both the archive and checksum index, the installed version reports source `16ee8ca`, and the default launcher still points to RC7. I’m archiving this as installation preflight only; no manual terminal cell has been run or counted.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00594509481a0b7915fb9c4d4dd37","order":19535,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b15-cdb8-7ae3-be45-60d39af089e4","text":"The RC10 desktop preflight is committed in its own isolated worktree. It includes the exact install identity and a 15-cell checklist with the accepted checks and screenshot requirements; every cell is still explicitly marked “Not run.” I’m submitting the evidence for exact-head CI and independent review now.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae005cca50c81a0b7e03cbc78b9aa89","order":19537,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b16-a9f0-7641-8a03-419f86fd893a","text":"The active RC10 overlay probe has ended and failed: it reached command approval, sent the intended key sequence, then timed out before the harmless command completed. I’m preserving this as a failed run and inspecting the captured screen and mock-gateway trace before deciding whether it’s a harness error or product defect.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19539,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f