{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:05:59.323Z","ordinal":397682,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-74397b1e-e097-4eb8-a927-1c019846ab9b","process_id":"48450","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027 -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%P\\n' | sort; sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md; sed -n '1,180p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md 2>/dev/null; git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027 -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%P\\n' | sort; sed -n '1,220p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md; sed -n '1,180p' docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md 2>/dev/null; git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"README.md\ncaptured-8-of-9/gw.log\ncaptured-8-of-9/mockgw_states.py\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.raw\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ncaptured-8-of-9/ptylib.py\ncaptured-8-of-9/run.log\ncaptured-8-of-9/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-original/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-original/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.raw\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ndetail-attempt-original/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-original/run.log\ndetail-attempt-original/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.raw\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ndetail-attempt-runtime/pip.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/run.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/run_overlay.py\n# RC10 installed terminal accessibility state probe\n\nCandidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The installed package was invoked through its installed TUI launcher. Each workspace and outer HOME/XDG tree was isolated. Gateway and workspace contents were synthetic; no credentials, held-out tasks, or provider access were used.\n\n## Scope and result\n\nThe scripted probe sampled ten readable UI states: idle, help, model picker, streaming, cancelled turn, approval, completion, tool running, tool cancellation, and endpoint error. It exercised `xterm-256color` with `NO_COLOR=1` and `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset, each at 40×14 and 100×30. Raw PTY streams and decoded screen snapshots are preserved per attempt.\n\n| Configuration | First attempt | Confirmation attempt |\n|---|---|---|\n| xterm-256color + NO_COLOR=1, 40×14 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| xterm-256color + NO_COLOR=1, 100×30 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| TERM=dumb, 40×14 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| TERM=dumb, 100×30 | tool cancellation remained in `cancelling` beyond 5 s | tool cancellation remained in `cancelling` beyond 5 s |\n\nAn isolated retry of the TERM=dumb 100×30 tool-cancel subcase returned to idle about 0.4 s after Esc. This does not erase the two full-matrix timeouts: the behavior is intermittent. The failure screen says `cancelling — waiting for run_command (5s)` and keeps the running turn visible. All retained raw streams were scanned for color-setting SGR parameters; none were found. The 40-column approval snapshots show the complete decision hint `←→ choose, enter · esc denies`.\n\n## Disposition\n\n`PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`. These captures establish sampled-state readability and no color-setting SGR in the captured streams, but do not establish the full ACC-TUI-A11Y criterion. In addition to the intermittent Esc/tool-cancellation delay, the nine `Overlay` variants in source were not all exercised; checkpoint choice, detail, receipt, connect, paste, and review overlays remain outside this probe. The required real-terminal human matrix remains separate. Do not treat this as accepted accessibility qualification.\n\nThe two failed full-matrix attempts, the successful isolated retry, their runner scripts, synthetic gateway logs, PTY streams, and screen snapshots are retained here without replacing earlier attempts.\n\n## Supplemental overlay-state probe (2026-10-27)\n\nA later installed-RC10 synthetic probe rendered eight of the nine source `Overlay` variants at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14. The `Detail` overlay was not captured. Follow-up attempts displayed the command approval panel but did not complete the synthetic approval sequence; they are classified as harness-incomplete, not product failures. Raw streams, screenshots, driver, mock gateway and attempts are archived under [overlay-expansion-20261027](overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md). This narrows the earlier overlay-coverage gap but does not change the overall `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED` disposition: other terminal configurations are uncovered, the intermittent cancellation timeouts remain, and human terminal acceptance remains pending.\n# RC10 supplemental overlay-state probe\n\nCandidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The probe used the installed RC10 launcher, a synthetic local mock gateway, isolated HOME/XDG/workspaces, and no provider credentials or held-out data.\n\n## Result\n\nThis supplemental probe rendered eight of the nine `Overlay` variants at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14: `Approval`, `CheckpointChoice`, `Help`, `Receipt`, `Models`, `Connect`, `Paste`, and `Review`. The `Detail` overlay was not captured. The successful capture is `captured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt`; its raw PTY stream, driver, mock gateway, and notes are retained alongside it.\n\nThe Detail follow-up attempts did not reach the overlay. The mock returned the synthetic `run_command` tool call and the installed TUI rendered its approval panel, but the scripted operator input did not complete approval; later attempts stopped at that panel. Treat these as harness-incomplete, not as a product failure or pass. Each attempt's logs, raw stream when available, screen, driver, and mock are retained in the neighboring `detail-attempt-*` directories. A pip setup record is included where relevant; no runtime package was installed into the repository.\n\n## Disposition\n\n`PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`. Eight overlays observed in one terminal configuration do not establish all-configuration readability. The Detail overlay remains untested; prior two full `TERM=dumb` 100×30 cancellation timeouts remain unresolved despite one passing isolated retry; the human real-terminal acceptance matrix remains separate and pending. This evidence does not change the gate disposition.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":760871969}},"started_at_ms":1793066758562,"completed_at_ms":1793066759323}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:06:00.479Z","ordinal":397683,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17b1b-791f-7533-8700-8be57a7b09a2","call_id":"call_f5d6ea35c2af4cfba1b01d94b3b07183","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"README.md\ncaptured-8-of-9/gw.log\ncaptured-8-of-9/mockgw_states.py\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.raw\ncaptured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ncaptured-8-of-9/ptylib.py\ncaptured-8-of-9/run.log\ncaptured-8-of-9/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-arrow-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-confirm-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-delayed-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/run.log\ndetail-attempt-direct-key/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-original/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-original/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.raw\ndetail-attempt-original/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ndetail-attempt-original/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-original/run.log\ndetail-attempt-original/run_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/gw.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/mockgw_overlay.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.notes.txt\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.raw\ndetail-attempt-runtime/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt\ndetail-attempt-runtime/pip.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/ptylib.py\ndetail-attempt-runtime/run.log\ndetail-attempt-runtime/run_overlay.py\n# RC10 installed terminal accessibility state probe\n\nCandidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The installed package was invoked through its installed TUI launcher. Each workspace and outer HOME/XDG tree was isolated. Gateway and workspace contents were synthetic; no credentials, held-out tasks, or provider access were used.\n\n## Scope and result\n\nThe scripted probe sampled ten readable UI states: idle, help, model picker, streaming, cancelled turn, approval, completion, tool running, tool cancellation, and endpoint error. It exercised `xterm-256color` with `NO_COLOR=1` and `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset, each at 40×14 and 100×30. Raw PTY streams and decoded screen snapshots are preserved per attempt.\n\n| Configuration | First attempt | Confirmation attempt |\n|---|---|---|\n| xterm-256color + NO_COLOR=1, 40×14 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| xterm-256color + NO_COLOR=1, 100×30 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| TERM=dumb, 40×14 | 10 sampled states passed | 10 sampled states passed |\n| TERM=dumb, 100×30 | tool cancellation remained in `cancelling` beyond 5 s | tool cancellation remained in `cancelling` beyond 5 s |\n\nAn isolated retry of the TERM=dumb 100×30 tool-cancel subcase returned to idle about 0.4 s after Esc. This does not erase the two full-matrix timeouts: the behavior is intermittent. The failure screen says `cancelling — waiting for run_command (5s)` and keeps the running turn visible. All retained raw streams were scanned for color-setting SGR parameters; none were found. The 40-column approval snapshots show the complete decision hint `←→ choose, enter · esc denies`.\n\n## Disposition\n\n`PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`. These captures establish sampled-state readability and no color-setting SGR in the captured streams, but do not establish the full ACC-TUI-A11Y criterion. In addition to the intermittent Esc/tool-cancellation delay, the nine `Overlay` variants in source were not all exercised; checkpoint choice, detail, receipt, connect, paste, and review overlays remain outside this probe. The required real-terminal human matrix remains separate. Do not treat this as accepted accessibility qualification.\n\nThe two failed full-matrix attempts, the successful isolated retry, their runner scripts, synthetic gateway logs, PTY streams, and screen snapshots are retained here without replacing earlier attempts.\n\n## Supplemental overlay-state probe (2026-10-27)\n\nA later installed-RC10 synthetic probe rendered eight of the nine source `Overlay` variants at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14. The `Detail` overlay was not captured. Follow-up attempts displayed the command approval panel but did not complete the synthetic approval sequence; they are classified as harness-incomplete, not product failures. Raw streams, screenshots, driver, mock gateway and attempts are archived under [overlay-expansion-20261027](overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md). This narrows the earlier overlay-coverage gap but does not change the overall `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED` disposition: other terminal configurations are uncovered, the intermittent cancellation timeouts remain, and human terminal acceptance remains pending.\n# RC10 supplemental overlay-state probe\n\nCandidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The probe used the installed RC10 launcher, a synthetic local mock gateway, isolated HOME/XDG/workspaces, and no provider credentials or held-out data.\n\n## Result\n\nThis supplemental probe rendered eight of the nine `Overlay` variants at `TERM=dumb`, 40×14: `Approval`, `CheckpointChoice`, `Help`, `Receipt`, `Models`, `Connect`, `Paste`, and `Review`. The `Detail` overlay was not captured. The successful capture is `captured-8-of-9/overlay_dumb40.screens.txt`; its raw PTY stream, driver, mock gateway, and notes are retained alongside it.\n\nThe Detail follow-up attempts did not reach the overlay. The mock returned the synthetic `run_command` tool call and the installed TUI rendered its approval panel, but the scripted operator input did not complete approval; later attempts stopped at that panel. Treat these as harness-incomplete, not as a product failure or pass. Each attempt's logs, raw stream when available, screen, driver, and mock are retained in the neighboring `detail-attempt-*` directories. A pip setup record is included where relevant; no runtime package was installed into the repository.\n\n## Disposition\n\n`PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`. Eight overlays observed in one terminal configuration do not establish all-configuration readability. The Detail overlay remains untested; prior two full `TERM=dumb` 100×30 cancellation timeouts remain unresolved despite one passing isolated retry; the human real-terminal acceptance matrix remains separate and pending. This evidence does not change the gate disposition.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","create_time":1793066760.4795651}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
