{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:06:29.187Z","ordinal":397698,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0071cd03081a08d514bc9ceb8af53","status":"completed","call_id":"call_5e3b57d7051c40ed8b4d8fbab8ee83bc","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"set -eu\\nsrc=/var/tmp/nexus-rc10-approval-repro-20261027T0203Z\\ndst=/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/corrected-approval-path\\nmkdir -p \\\"$dst\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/run_corrected.py\\\" \\\"$dst/run_corrected.py\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/mockgw_overlay.py\\\" \\\"$dst/mockgw_overlay.py\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/approval_timing.notes.txt\\\" \\\"$dst/approval_timing.notes.txt\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/approval_timing.raw\\\" \\\"$dst/approval_timing.raw\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/approval_timing.screens.txt\\\" \\\"$dst/approval_timing.screens.txt\\\"\\ncp \\\"$src/gw.log\\\" \\\"$dst/gw.log\\\"\\ncat > \\\"$dst/README.md\\\" <<'EOF'\\n# RC10 synthetic approval-path confirmation\\n\\nCandidate: installed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\\n\\nThis focused probe used the installed RC10 launcher, a synthetic localhost mock gateway, an isolated HOME/XDG tree, and a disposable Git workspace. It used `TERM=dumb`, 40×14. No live provider, credential, held-out task, or private evaluation data was involved.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe harmless `echo synthetic-safe` command completed successfully after the approval was selected and confirmed. The visible panel was allowed to settle; `Left` selected Approve; the two Enter presses were separated by the confirmation dwell. The mock log records the initial tool request, a follow-up request containing one tool result, and the final assistant response. The PTY returned to the idle prompt at 7.92 seconds.\\n\\nThis resolves the earlier supplemental harness timeout as a probe-sequencing/fixture issue for this specific approval path. In the preserved attempt, `y` was sent while the panel was still in its recent-typing state, then the arrow and Enter keys arrived before the required quiet/choice dwell. A subsequent diagnostic reached tool execution, but that temporary mock returned the same tool call again after the tool result, so its wait for a final response timed out. The final run corrected both the key timing and mock response condition. No product defect was reproduced.\\n\\nThis is only a synthetic approval-flow probe. It does not qualify all overlays, replace the remaining scripted accessibility checks, satisfy any of the 15 human terminal cells, or change the overall `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED` disposition.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\n`run_corrected.py` launches `mockgw_overlay.py` and the installed RC10 TUI via the existing isolated PTY driver. The driver uses the installed package path documented in the surrounding evidence bundle. `approval_timing.raw`, `approval_timing.screens.txt`, and `approval_timing.notes.txt` preserve the terminal output; `gw.log` preserves the synthetic request/tool-result sequence.\\n\\n## SHA-256\\n\\nSee `SHA256SUMS` for this bundle's file hashes.\\nEOF\\n(cd \\\"$dst\\\" && sha256sum README.md run_corrected.py mockgw_overlay.py approval_timing.notes.txt approval_timing.raw approval_timing.screens.txt gw.log > SHA256SUMS)\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md')\\ns=p.read_text()\\nold='The Detail follow-up attempts did not reach the overlay. The mock returned the synthetic `run_command` tool call and the installed TUI rendered its approval panel, but the scripted operator input did not complete approval; later attempts stopped at that panel. Treat these as harness-incomplete, not as a product failure or pass. Each attempt\\\\'s logs, raw stream when available, screen, driver, and mock are retained in the neighboring `detail-attempt-*` directories. A pip setup record is included where relevant; no runtime package was installed into the repository.'\\nnew=old+' A later focused synthetic follow-up completed the harmless command after using the approval panel\\\\'s required settle and confirmation timing and correcting the mock\\\\'s post-tool response; see [corrected approval-path confirmation](corrected-approval-path/README.md). The earlier timeouts were harness/fixture failures for this path, not reproduced product failures.'\\nif s.count(old)!=1: raise SystemExit(f'expected one paragraph, found {s.count(old)}')\\np.write_text(s.replace(old,new))\\nPY\\n(cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal && git diff --check && sha256sum -c docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/corrected-approval-path/SHA256SUMS)\\ngit -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-scripted-terminal status --short\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2500});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","create_time":1793066780.815559}}}
