rified and done, invoke \\`task_completed\\` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\n3795-8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\n3796-${fewShotSection}${tddSection}${roleSection}\n3797-Always explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\n3798-\n--\n3807-\n3808-  private setupSpineHandlers(): void {\n3809-    registerBridgeCapabilities(this.capabilityRegistry, this.bridge);\n3810-\n3811:    this.spine.registerHandler(\"task_completed\", async (args) => {\n3812-      const validCompletion =\n3813-        Boolean(args) &&\n3814-        typeof args === \"object\" &&\n3815-        !Array.isArray(args) &&\n--\n3820-        return {\n3821-          success: false,\n3822-          output: \"\",\n3823-          error:\n3824:            \"Invalid task_completed payload: summary must be a non-empty string and notes, when present, must be a string.\",\n3825-        };\n3826-      }\n3827-\n3828-      // The operator's acceptance requirements gate completion; a coarse completed plan does not.\n--\n3839-              (open.length ? `Open:\\n  ${list(open)}\\n` : \"\") +\n3840-              (blocked.length ? `Blocked:\\n  ${list(blocked)}\\n` : \"\") +\n3841-              `Finish the open ones and record evidence with update_requirements (implemented/verified). ` +\n3842-              `A requirement that cannot be done here must be marked blocked or descoped with the reason; ` +\n3843:              `a blocked task is not completed — end with a final message stating the blocker instead of calling task_completed.`,\n3844- 