{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:13:33.005Z","ordinal":398024,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae008caa65081a0a60d60d83505e7ca","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I reviewed the [RC8 session export](/home/mike/nexus-code/nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json). It records a task that ended with `make test` **not executed**, verification **failed**, and the result **not established** because there was no trusted pre-change baseline. Yet the assistant’s final message said the task was complete. That mismatch is actionable dogfooding evidence: the user-facing completion message can overstate what the recorded outcome supports.\n\nThe export itself contains no RC8 or mike-dev identifier, and has no candidate identity or worktree binding. So I can’t independently tie it to the RC8 binary; I’m treating that attribution as your report, not verified release evidence. I made no changes to the shared checkout.\n\nCurrent fetched `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; this export does not qualify an RC or release.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":777,"lineEnd":789,"note":"used prior Nexus release qualification context to distinguish dogfooding evidence from exact-RC acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"started_at_ms":1793067210676,"completed_at_ms":1793067213005}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:13:33.009Z","ordinal":398025,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae008caa65081a0a60d60d83505e7ca","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"I reviewed the [RC8 session export](/home/mike/nexus-code/nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json). It records a task that ended with `make test` **not executed**, verification **failed**, and the result **not established** because there was no trusted pre-change baseline. Yet the assistant’s final message said the task was complete. That mismatch is actionable dogfooding evidence: the user-facing completion message can overstate what the recorded outcome supports.\n\nThe export itself contains no RC8 or mike-dev identifier, and has no candidate identity or worktree binding. So I can’t independently tie it to the RC8 binary; I’m treating that attribution as your report, not verified release evidence. I made no changes to the shared checkout.\n\nCurrent fetched `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; this export does not qualify an RC or release.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:777-789|note=[used prior Nexus release qualification context to distinguish dogfooding evidence from exact-RC acceptance]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","create_time":1793067210.6524618,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae008caa65081a0a60d60d83505e7ca","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a17b22-60d1-78f3-9485-e62b3d7824dc","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19553}}
