{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:14:33.066Z","ordinal":398028,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","root_turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a","last_agent_message":"I reviewed the [RC8 session export](/home/mike/nexus-code/nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json). It records a task that ended with `make test` **not executed**, verification **failed**, and the result **not established** because there was no trusted pre-change baseline. Yet the assistant’s final message said the task was complete. That mismatch is actionable dogfooding evidence: the user-facing completion message can overstate what the recorded outcome supports.\n\nThe export itself contains no RC8 or mike-dev identifier, and has no candidate identity or worktree binding. So I can’t independently tie it to the RC8 binary; I’m treating that attribution as your report, not verified release evidence. I made no changes to the shared checkout.\n\nCurrent fetched `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; this export does not qualify an RC or release.\n\n","started_at":1793066076,"completed_at":1793067273,"duration_ms":1196572,"time_to_first_token_ms":4521}}
