{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:18:50.510Z","ordinal":398262,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17b27-390d-79f3-97a2-5a62896541dd","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed exact PR #264 head `2c9ec9f463e2125c75ceb625cecbb5fb3e086311` against base `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Diff SHA-256: `d83f0a87587d7e6ace47bb4fad47a2285e02dd5f3479cba5060d86d6320b2800`.\n\nBoth prior findings are resolved:\n\n- The updated approval-path README hash matches its entry in the top-level `SHA256SUMS` and `manifest.json`; the nested bundle’s seven checksum entries all match.\n- The README now correctly says `gw.log` records the two requests, while the PTY capture shows the final response. The gateway log has two request records; the PTY screen capture shows “Done. The synthetic operation is complete.” The evidence remains synthetic and `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`, with the 15-cell human matrix unperformed.\n\nOne bundle-level issue remains: the top-level `SHA256SUMS` and `manifest.json` reference **60 `.log` files absent from the exact commit tree**. For example, `SHA256SUMS:3` and `manifest.json:22` reference `accessibility/attempt_0150/gw_states_0.log`, which is not committed. I found 332 top-level checksum entries: 60 missing files and no mismatches among the files present. This conflicts with the README’s statement that logs are retained and checksummed and PR #264’s claim that the evidence-bundle manifest verifies. Correct the inventory or narrow that claim before merge."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793067530.5097644}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":19562}}
