nnector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0082b63e081a09cb422c9e34a946f","order":19550,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b1f-ecc3-7f43-a12b-ea9735ed4c63","text":"Independent review found two concrete evidence issues in PR #264: a stale checksum and one sentence that overstates what the mock log contains. Another owner has since advanced the same terminal-evidence worktree, so I’m checking that owner’s current boundary before applying the corrections. The review is attached to the exact PR commit; I won’t let the newer local work be overwritten.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00883148881a0b03566d3d74d438d","order":19551,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b21-41b5-70b0-a2b6-661f603eac79","text":"Memory capture is paused during a provider quota cooldown; I’ll leave it alone. I’ll inspect the RC8 session export as dogfooding evidence, then compare its findings with the current release records without changing the shared checkout.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae008ab368081a09ad223670ef39e64","order":19552,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b21-df6d-7ba0-9e21-8dc00eada7d2","text":"The export is an unverified session record, not release qualification: it has no candidate identity and explicitly records `make test` as failed/unexecuted because no trusted pre-change baseline was available. I’m checking whether the RC8 attribution is captured in the session itself and isolating any actionable product defect from the agent’s self-reported code review.","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae008caa65081a0a60d60d83505e7ca","order":19553,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a17b22-60d1-78f3-9485-e62b3d7824dc","text":"I reviewed the [RC8 session export](/home/mike/nexus-code/nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json). It records a task that ended with `make test` **not executed**, verification **failed**, and the result **not established** because there was no trusted pre-change baseline. Yet the assistant’s final message said the task was complete. That mismatch is actionable dogfooding evidence: the user-facing completion message can overstate what the recorded outcome supports.\n\nThe export itself contains no RC8 or mike-dev identifier, and has no candidate identity or worktree binding. So I can’t independently tie it to the RC8 binary; I’m treating that attribution as your report, not verified release evidence. I made no changes to the shared checkout.\n\nCurrent fetched `origin/main` is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; this export does not qualify an RC or release.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:777-789|note=[used prior Nexus release qualification context to distinguish dogfooding evidence from exact-RC acceptance]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a17b11-0941-7523-8004-970495a9563a"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae0090ed42c81a08686d9145cad3aff","order":19554,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b23-646e-7921-bd9f-83ba5974823d","text":"I’m continuing the release path from the current repository state. First I’m refreshing the exact RC10 PR/check and claim status; the session export exposed a possible completion-reporting defect, but it is not candidate-bound evidence and won’t be used to satisfy a release gate.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00974ae5c81a0a2e44d21f9a72f14","order":19556,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b24-f293-7290-bda4-4f57ba77e707","text":"I found the PR branch already contains the correction to the stale bundle hash. I fixed the remaining inaccurate statement about what the mock gateway log captures, regenerated the linked hashes, and verified the complete evidence bundle. I’m updating PR #264 now; its synthetic evidence remains partial and does not count toward the real terminal matrix.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00a1354a881a08d29aa47888ea309","order":19563,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b27-5eb3-7f01-899f-21ac11c21689","text":"The independent review found a second bundle problem: 60 `.log` entries are listed in the manifest/checksum file but absent from the committed tree. The local checksum check had seen ignored workspace files, so it was weaker than an exact-commit check. I’m reconciling those entries against Git and will repair the evidence bundle before asking for another review.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00a7939e481a086bab0f3abf96df9","order":19565,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b28-ec9a-7813-a208-8761ec286a8e","text":"PR #264 now contains the full hashed evidence set (331 entries; zero files missing and zero digest mismatches in the exact commit tree). Its exact-head CI and CodeQL are running. PR #263’s Node 22 and CodeQL checks have passed; Node 24 has passed, while Node 22 CI is still running.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19568,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nR