{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:24:34.758Z","ordinal":398504,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00b61e4b881a092514e53817f2fdf","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The RC8 export is exploratory dogfooding rather than acceptance evidence: it reviews codebase enhancements, and its task record marks changes unverified. I’ve refreshed the authoritative branch: `origin/main` is `16ee8ca`, with exact-head CI, CodeQL, and cross-runner reproducibility all passing. I’m checking the active review PRs now and will keep working on gates that don’t depend on the rebuilt host’s SSH identity."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793067873923,"completed_at_ms":1793067874758}}
