{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:25:44.730Z","ordinal":398562,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e6e66a53-d96a-4b8c-8bbf-cabe8a6e8a3e","process_id":"33197","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'openrouter.*(model|pinned)|pinned.*openrouter|providers verify' origin/main -- docs eval scripts | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | sed -n '1,160p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'openrouter.*(model|pinned)|pinned.*openrouter|providers verify' origin/main -- docs eval scripts | head -100; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | sed -n '1,160p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:67:   destination and the authorized cloud destinations. `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m>` performs a\norigin/main:docs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:45:Crush's provider catalog loads fresh, cached, or embedded data and preserves a usable catalog when refresh fails. Its coordinator builds separate Fantasy adapters for OpenAI, OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Azure, Bedrock, Google, and Vertex. The provider/model selector accounts for model IDs containing slashes and reports ambiguous unqualified matches. Its agent retains provider-specific reasoning metadata and records usage/cost information.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md:5:Build: branch `feat/cloud-providers` at `1310e3a` (cli/dist). Command: `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m> -j`\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md:17:Model discovery before the checks: OpenRouter listed 458 models; the Codex backend listed 7.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:116:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:25135), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:138:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:30869), model anthropic/claude-x. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:141:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:14271), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:142:▶ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:146:✔ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model (85.324191ms)\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:336:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:12659), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:358:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:13693), model anthropic/claude-x. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:361:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:21615), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:362:▶ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:366:✔ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model (32.443536ms)\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:20:| **5. Inference compatibility** | Built-in providers `openai`, `ollama`, `lmstudio`; `--oss` with `oss_provider = lmstudio|ollama`; custom `model_providers.<id>.base_url`; `wire_api` only `responses` (Responses API required); `request_max_retries` 4, `stream_max_retries` 5, `stream_idle_timeout_ms` 300000 [CX-CFG]. | Anthropic API, Bedrock, Google Agent Platform (Vertex), Microsoft Foundry, LLM gateways exposing a supported (Anthropic-format) API; Anthropic \"doesn't support routing Claude Code to non-Claude models through any gateway\" [CC-GW]. Cost/token metrics via OTel; `-p --output-format json` returns usage and cost [CC-OTEL][CC-SESS]. | \"75+\" providers; Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp (llama-server) via `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` + `options.baseURL`; `@ai-sdk/openai` for `/v1/responses`; per-model context/output limits [OC-PROV]. | ~60 providers; Ollama (warns 4096 default ctx, `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`), LM Studio, Docker Model Runner (llama.cpp path), Ramalama (`--jinja` required), vLLM via `OPENAI_HOST`, custom providers in OpenAI/Anthropic/Ollama formats; \"models without [tool calling] can only do chat completion\" [GS-PROV]. | OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Groq, LM Studio, xAI, Azure, Cohere, DeepSeek, Ollama, OpenAI-compatible, OpenRouter, Copilot, Vertex, Bedrock; text edit formats (no native tool calls needed); warns weaker models may fail to produce applicable edits [AI-LLMS][AI-EDIT]. |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:12:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> -m <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:18:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> --model <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:95:  \"qualificationDisposition\": \"Provider verification passed for ChatGPT sign-in and one explicitly pinned OpenRouter model. The separate required live engineering task per ACCEPTANCE.md §4.3 remains incomplete; this record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:4:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:58:02.236Z\",\"requestId\":\"e5ad5e55-85bd-41a9-b304-459832133c3c\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"failed\",\"failureKind\":\"http_error\",\"usageConfidence\":\"none\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:5:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:04.677Z\",\"requestId\":\"24a6aab0-d91f-443f-a225-6abf69debe3b\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"REDACTED\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":24,\"outputTokens\":54,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":50,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:6:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:06.238Z\",\"requestId\":\"b96adfad-275b-4b96-812b-3e3152ccbfea\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"gen-1792774744-4t2kU7vz1CXEpLIH1nz4\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":321,\"outputTokens\":71,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":36,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:7:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:10.680Z\",\"requestId\":\"6b0abf39-7840-417c-a5c2-9b1585f9f835\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"gen-1792774746-6l3KwgU3yGnMxzaRncSa\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":380,\"outputTokens\":42,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":20,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:83:| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:114:| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:154:| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:25:| Runtime services | The local inference gateway is configured in `~/.config/nexus/config.env`: endpoint `https://10.0.8.5:8443/v1`, model `engineering/b0`, key redacted, `LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL=bash`. The repo-tracked `cli/.env` holds LM Studio defaults (`localhost:1234`, key \"local\"). **The audit sent no requests to the gateway.** With owner authorization (2026-10-14, small spend), it made live cloud calls through the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections: two `providers verify` runs and one `nexus run` bug-fix task. See EVIDENCE §3. | RT (values redacted) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:123:| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:46:| L1 | `nexus providers verify --provider chatgpt -m gpt-6-luna -j` | PASS: streamed completion, tool call, tool-result round trip | `8e910140…`, `1e6c5946…`, `d8595745…` | `evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json` |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:47:| L2 | `nexus providers verify --provider openrouter -m openrouter/free -j` | PASS. The effective model varied per request (nemotron-3-super, then laguna-xs-2.1, then laguna-s-2.1), which shows `openrouter/free` is unsuitable for matched evaluation. | `49b71fc3…`, `b05711f6…`, `2b9cc6c5…` | `evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json` |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:435:| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:486:- On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** openrouter `nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free` PASS (one model served every request), chatgpt `gpt-6-luna` PASS (`evidence/live/verify_*_pinned_2026-10-16.json`). The run found and fixed the option-scope regression (4d82578). openai-key and anthropic not connected. | partial (repeat on the RC) | ACC-PRV-LIVE | RR | B §6 G2 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:19:- Two connection kinds: (a) legacy \"appliance/endpoint\" path (no provider id): OpenAI Chat Completions, `/v1` appended, fallback list, `X-Task-Class`, gateway token file / config.env key scoped by origin (client.ts:123-133), no receipts, no spending limits; (b) provider connections (providers.ts:46-116): openrouter, openai (Responses), anthropic (Messages), compatible, chatgpt (unofficial OAuth), copilot (unofficial OAuth); pinned endpoint, own key only, `redirect:\"error\"`, receipts in `<ws>/.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl`, spending limits (usage.ts).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:92:| G1 No live evidence of standalone LM Studio / llama.cpp / vLLM / Ollama runs. `.nexus/inference_receipts.jsonl` (HISTORICAL, 2026-10-11..14) contains only provider-connection receipts: chatgpt 284 (281 completed), openrouter 12; local/appliance requests are never receipted (client.ts:561-569), so there is no machine-readable local evidence. | On a clean host with no `~/.config/nexus`, run each server with a small tool-capable model; `nexus run` a fixed 3-step edit task; capture `/status` context source, turn status, and transcript; repeat with the server's context set to 4096 to exercise PRV-06. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:93:| G2 Live cloud qualification limited to openrouter + chatgpt (docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md, HISTORICAL). openai, anthropic, copilot, compatible: mock-only. | `nexus providers verify --provider {openai,anthropic,copilot,compatible} --model <m> -j` with operator keys; archive JSON. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:110:| PRV-R9 | Live `providers verify` PASS for each provider listed as supported in docs, or the doc lists it as mock-only/experimental. | compat/docs | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Archived verify JSON per provider. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":724251525}},"started_at_ms":1793067944005,"completed_at_ms":1793067944730}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:25:45.801Z","ordinal":398563,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17b2d-8f49-7f93-bcbe-ae96ab82e5c5","call_id":"call_8c1a1914149c40cbaa1bf74606ce4f23","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5453)\nTotal output lines: 99\n\norigin/main:docs/CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md:67:   destination and the authorized cloud destinations. `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m>` performs a\norigin/main:docs/NEXUS-CLOUD-PROVIDERS-PLAN.md:45:Crush's provider catalog loads fresh, cached, or embedded data and preserves a usable catalog when refresh fails. Its coordinator builds separate Fantasy adapters for OpenAI, OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Azure, Bedrock, Google, and Vertex. The provider/model selector accounts for model IDs containing slashes and reports ambiguous unqualified matches. Its agent retains provider-specific reasoning metadata and records usage/cost information.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md:5:Build: branch `feat/cloud-providers` at `1310e3a` (cli/dist). Command: `nexus providers verify --provider <id> --model <m> -j`\norigin/main:docs/reviews/NEXUS_CLOUD_PROVIDERS_LIVE_QUALIFICATION_2026-10-11.md:17:Model discovery before the checks: OpenRouter listed 458 models; the Codex backend listed 7.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:116:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:25135), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:138:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:30869), model anthropic/claude-x. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:141:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:14271), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:142:▶ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/baseline_57c070d_npm_test.log:146:✔ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model (85.324191ms)\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:336:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:12659), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:358:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:13693), model anthropic/claude-x. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:361:[nexus] Cloud inference: OpenRouter (http://127.0.0.1:21615), model claude-test. Task content — prompts, tool results and file excerpts — is sent to this provider.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:362:▶ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/nexus_maturity_2026-10-11_verification/final_make_test.log:366:✔ OpenRouter: usage, cost and effective model (32.443536ms)\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:20:| **5. Inference compatibility** | Built-in providers `openai`, `ollama`, `lmstudio`; `--oss` with `oss_provider = lmstudio|ollama`; custom `model_providers.<id>.base_url`; `wire_api` only `responses` (Responses API required); `request_max_retries` 4, `stream_max_retries` 5, `stream_idle_timeout_ms` 300000 [CX-CFG]. | Anthropic API, Bedrock, Google Agent Platform (Vertex), Microsoft Foundry, LLM gateways exposing a supported (Anthropic-format) API; Anthropic \"doesn't support routing Claude Code to non-Claude models through any gateway\" [CC-GW]. Cost/token metrics via OTel; `-p --output-format json` returns usage and cost [CC-OTEL][CC-SESS]. | \"75+\" providers; Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp (llama-server) via `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` + `options.baseURL`; `@ai-sdk/openai` for `/v1/responses`; per-model context/output limits [OC-PROV]. | ~60 providers; Ollama (warns 4096 default ctx, `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH`), LM Studio, Docker Model Runner (llama.cpp path), Ramalama (`--jinja` required), vLLM via `OPENAI_HOST`, custom providers in OpenAI/Anthropic/Ollama formats; \"models without [tool calling] can only do chat completion\" [GS-PROV]. | OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Groq, LM Studio, xAI, Azure, Cohere, DeepSeek, Ollama, OpenAI-compatible, OpenRouter, Copilot, Vertex, Bedrock; text edit formats (no native tool calls needed); warns weaker models may fail to produce applicable edits [AI-LLMS][AI-EDIT]. |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json:12:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> -m <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:18:    \"command\": \"nexus providers verify --provider <provider> --model <pinned-model> --json\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023T1659Z.json:95:  \"qualificationDisposition\": \"Provider verification passed for ChatGPT sign-in and one explicitly pinned OpenRouter model. The separate required live engineering task per ACCEPTANCE.md §4.3 remains incomplete; this record does not establish overall RC acceptance.\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:4:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:58:02.236Z\",\"requestId\":\"e5ad5e55-85bd-41a9-b304-459832133c3c\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"costConfidence\":\"unknown\",\"outcome\":\"failed\",\"failureKind\":\"http_error\",\"usageConfidence\":\"none\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:5:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:04.677Z\",\"requestId\":\"24a6aab0-d91f-443f-a225-6abf69debe3b\",\"role\":\"qualification\",\"providerId\":\"openrouter\",\"selectedModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"effectiveModel\":\"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free\",\"endpointOrigin\":\"https://openrouter.ai\",\"protocol\":\"openai-chat\",\"disclosure\":\"cloud\",\"origin_class\":\"cloud\",\"providerRequestId\":\"REDACTED\",\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":24,\"outputTokens\":54,\"cachedInputTokens\":0,\"reasoningTokens\":50,\"costUsd\":0},\"costConfidence\":\"provider-reported\",\"outcome\":\"completed\",\"usageConfidence\":\"provider\"}\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/provider-receipts-20261023T1659Z.jsonl:6:{\"at\":\"2026-10-23T16:59:06.238Z\",\"requestId\":\"b96adfad-275b-4b96-812b-3e3152ccbfea\",\"role\"…1953 tokens truncated…evidence/B_providers.md:110:| PRV-R9 | Live `providers verify` PASS for each provider listed as supported in docs, or the doc lists it as mock-only/experimental. | compat/docs | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Archived verify JSON per provider. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:82:7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: audit and planning package\n\nThis package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n\n**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n\n## How to read it\n\n| If you want to… | Read |\n|---|---|\n| Understand what Nexus is today, what was examined, and what is wrong | [AUDIT.md](AUDIT.md) |\n| See current release readiness and remaining actions | [READINESS.md](READINESS.md) |\n| See every requirement (historical and new), its status, blocker class, and how it is accepted | [REQUIREMENTS.md](REQUIREMENTS.md) |\n| Know the order of work, the effort, and the critical path | [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) |\n| Implement a workstream | Its spec in [specs/](specs/), then its plan in [plans/](plans/) |\n| Qualify a release candidate | [ACCEPTANCE.md](ACCEPTANCE.md) |\n| Check what was actually run and what it proves | [EVIDENCE.md](EVIDENCE.md) and [evidence/](evidence/) |\n| See the decisions taken (all resolved under delegated owner authority) and the remaining owner actions | [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md) |\n| Run several agents on this plan at once without collisions | [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) (also referenced from the root `AGENTS.md`) |\n\n## Workstreams\n\n| # | Workstream | Spec | Plan | Milestone | Blockers |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\n| 02 | Process ownership, cancellation, resource bounds | [SPEC-02](specs/SPEC-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | [PLAN-02](plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md) | M1 | AGT-109, SEC-106 |\n| 03 | Untrusted workspace inputs and egress boundary | [SPEC-03](specs/SPEC-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | [PLAN-03](plans/PLAN-03-untrusted-inputs-and-egress.md) | M1 | SEC-110, 111, 115, 116 |\n| 04 | Continuity, resume, durable work units | [SPEC-04](specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | [PLAN-04](plans/PLAN-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md) | M3 | AGT-101, 102 |\n| 05 | Standalone local inference and provider robustness | [SPEC-05](specs/SPEC-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | [PLAN-05](plans/PLAN-05-standalone-local-inference.md) | M3/M5 | PRV-101, 102, 106 |\n| 06 | Packaged product parity, launcher, versioning, doctor | [SPEC-06](specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | [PLAN-06](plans/PLAN-06-packaged-product-parity.md) | M0/M2 | REL-101, 102, 103 |\n| 07 | Supply chain, compliance, release engineering | [SPEC-07](specs/SPEC-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | [PLAN-07](plans/PLAN-07-supply-chain-and-release-engineering.md) | M2 | REL-107 |\n| 08 | Persistence hygiene | [SPEC-08](specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | [PLAN-08](plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md) | M0/M4 | (prerequisite: PER-103) |\n| 09 | Requirements governance and documentation truth | [SPEC-09](specs/SPEC-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | [PLAN-09](plans/PLAN-09-requirements-governance-and-docs.md) | M0/M6 | OPS-101, 103 |\n| 10 | v1 qualification and evaluation | [SPEC-10](specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | [PLAN-10](plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) | M3/M5 | QUAL-101 to 107 |\n| 11 | Verification and tool-call integrity | [SPEC-11](specs/SPEC-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | [PLAN-11](plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md) | M1/M3 | AGT-112, 113, 114 |\n| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\n| C1 | Contest (separate product; post-contest maintenance; no freeze applies) | [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | [PLAN-C1](plans/PLAN-C1-contest-submission-track.md) | post-contest | — (not a client gate) |\n\n\n## How to execute\n\n0. If more than one agent (or person) will implement in parallel, read [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) first. It covers slice claims, worktrees, hot files, the gateway lock and merge order.\n1. **Start with M0** (ROADMAP). Merge PLAN-08 PR-8a first, so that test runs stop writing into the real `~/.nexus`. Then land PLAN-06 PR-6a (version sync) and PLAN-09 PR-9a (ledger checker, historical banners, cheap doc fixes).\n2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\n3. **For every PR:**\n   - update the matching REQUIREMENTS rows (status, test reference, commit);\n   - keep `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` green;\n   - run `make test` on a snapshot copy, never while editing (tasks/lessons.md).\n4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\n5. Cut `v1.0.0-rc.1` only when G0–G4 pass. Then run ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 against the **installed** RC.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Requirement IDs.** `REQ-<AREA>-0xx` marks a commitment carried over from history. `REQ-<AREA>-1xx` marks a new v1 requirement.\n- **Finding IDs.** These are owned by the scoped evidence files: AGT, VER, PRV, SEC, PER, TUI, REL, DX, MNT, HIST, EVL, CON, PERF, DOC.\n- **Acceptance IDs.** `ACC-<AREA>-NN`. Each is defined in its spec, or in ACCEPTANCE §3.1.\n- **Evidence labels.** SRC, TEST, RT, MEAS, DOC, HIST, INF, UNV (REQUIREMENTS §1).\n- **Status ladder.** open → partial → implemented → tested → visually-accepted → product-qualified. Independent acceptance is recorded separately.\n\nThis package supersedes the Issue #12 matrices and the PHASE and WP documents as the source of current requirements. Those documents remain as historical record.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793067945.8013666}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
