"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_file"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f3-6561-78e2-9f56-cd2b1db5d742","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.rerun_failed_workflow_run_jobs"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch"},{"first_turn_id":"01a156f6-7b50-7a00-9fbb-818f2ac4eed4","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"fetch_topic"},{"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00b9eecb081a0b5af8e1dfd58bd9f","order":19570,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b2d-67a8-7c93-9cb5-19e160ec1547","text":"The supplied RC8 export is already reflected in merged PR #259 as “exploratory only”; it does not add a new acceptance result. I’ve recorded the refreshed revision and PR states in the existing release tracker. The remaining available work includes live provider qualification, so I’m checking its exact pinned-model contract and claim rules before attempting any inference.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00c07a8c881a09b85520d5dffa5a2","order":19571,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b2f-007b-7d82-a1e7-1c4313727be8","text":"The exact installed RC10 on `ubuntu-desktop` passed OpenRouter’s live streamed completion and tool round trip against the pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`. All three provider receipts report the same effective model and zero provider-reported cost. I’m preserving the raw result and receipt digest as exact-RC evidence now; this satisfies the provider-verify row only, not the separate live engineering task or overall acceptance.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00c9e7bb081a0af403902c939901c","order":19573,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b31-4dd7-7c21-8fa8-c353e3dc7375","text":"The standalone E5 task is running on the installed RC10 in a fresh synthetic workspace on `ubuntu-desktop`; it is isolated from repository and held-out data. The task has an operator-defined test command as its completion verifier. I’m waiting for the run to finish and will retain both its task result and the independent test outcome.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00cc682b081a0bf94f889a2b847ae","order":19574,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b31-ea8f-7d22-b2d9-59dced382893","text":"The small task exposed a concrete RC10 failure: the model implemented the change and the external tests pass, but the installed command ended `UNVERIFIED` with `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`, created no validation receipt, and the model still told the user the task was complete. I’m preserving this as a failed live-task result and tracing why the explicit authoritative verifier did not run before treating the behavior as a product defect.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00d20eebc81a0ad168e3aee2dc397","order":19575,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b33-4c9f-7eb0-9984-2fd5b22ff7c6","text":"Root cause found: the first fixture used `python -m unittest`, which RC10’s verifier-definition binder does not support. Nexus correctly refused to treat that run as verified, returned exit code 2, and labeled the result `UNVERIFIED`; the model’s closing prose nevertheless overstated completion. I’m retaining that failed attempt and preparing a fresh, committed fixture with a supported direct test-script verifier so the live-task gate can be evaluated fairly.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00d6e4ef081a0bcf98018cab9d132","order":19577,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b34-79c0-70a1-9b7f-c931447adb3c","text":"The second E5 attempt uses a fresh local Git baseline and a direct verifier form supported by RC10’s evidence binder. It remains separate from the first failed attempt, whose output is being preserved rather than replaced. The provider check itself passed; this task run is the remaining part of OpenRouter’s §4.3 gate.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00e3adf3881a0a8f61d207f6d6dda","order":19578,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b37-9920-7ed0-8cdf-e2b2e6d1e213","text":"The new Python binding regression passes. Running the full focused verification-binding file revealed a separate setup issue: its integration cases need the Rust core binary, which this fresh worktree hasn’t built yet. I’m building that worktree-local binary, then I’ll rerun the focused file; the failure was a missing build artifact, not a failed Python binding assertion.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016ae00f02a7fc81a09dd9a0c883d3e3e9","order":19579,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a17b3a-a5b6-7d00-a51f-0a4c5d62295b","text":"The RC10 provider-verify record is ready, and I found a genuine accuracy gap in the live task: its four tests passed, but an independent Unicode probe found a case outside those tests where the implementation violated the task’s ASCII-only rule. I’m preserving that attempt as a failed outcome and continuing with the verifier fix. The code change now makes root-qualified Python test imports eligible to bind their declared deliverables; its focused regressions pass.","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":19580,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16013,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905","receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17097-c495-7e80-869b-ce412675b905\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answer\":\"Yes, extend PR #200 scope\"}]\nuser: \u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: continue\n\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES END\n"},{"order":16023,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a1709f-8f3b-7fc1-bf6d-113bcbc97fe9","receiver_turn_id":"01a17095-f2fe-7de0-b5cc-460661bc1fe3","text