{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:43:04.988Z","ordinal":399265,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17b3d-6a9c-7dc2-9bed-c20b3c1bdc0d","call_id":"call_65069c525ba64392a826e464e2a95ae2","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #256 was merged at `1aa8832`; its exact head, `987c73a8178390b0ed710474648ca1a71eaf060e`, is an ancestor of current `origin/main` at `4cae11c`. The feature branch remains clean at `987c73a`, originally based on `ff34938`. [PR #256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256)\\n\\nThe commit fixed pending local-discovery cancellation and late activation, corrected the key-storage message, and isolated invalid provider catalog errors. Its credential-origin fix was incomplete: later review reproduced a legacy key reaching the newly selected endpoint. So that commit alone does not clear the security acceptance blocker.\\n\\nCI passed on PR #256, but GitHub records no reviews, and I found no independent acceptance of exact head `987c73a`. An accepted follow-up exists on branch `v1/defect-malformed-credential-origin` at `0571266`; it has no open PR and is not in current `main`.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Since the last audit, Issue #1 gained coordinator comment [#6406940449](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1#issuecomment-6406940449); the issue’s `updated_at` is `2026-10-26T02:33:48Z`. It says the custody request remains unanswered. All 20 comments are from the coordinator; no custodian response or handoff is visible.\\n\\nAt `main@bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, the T2 and T3 manifest hashes are unchanged: `50895b84…1f3e89b` and `85fb9caf…c9f1383`. The evaluator still rejects T2’s legacy `hidden.command` for qualification and requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, repeated custody checks, and a new immutable manifest.\\n\\nNo active held-out ownership or handoff appears in the claims records. The same external dependency remains; there is no new custody readiness.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed PR #264 at exact head `78ce94b5c1755658a17a8474f597a7b3ef8f87da` against base `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. Diff SHA-256: `b4ed30ebcff7a0ab43504619710288a8fd815f08eaf99d204fd635b372cd3312`.\\n\\nAll 331 entries in `manifest.json`, all 332 entries in the top-level `SHA256SUMS`, and all 7 nested approval-path checksums match files in the exact commit. The earlier attribution corrections remain intact: `gw.log` is described as recording requests, and the PTY capture as showing the final assistant response.\\n\\nThe evidence remains synthetic and explicitly `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`; the human terminal matrix is still unperformed. No acceptance or release claim is introduced.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793068984.988657}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
