efault: proceed on\n                                      the labelled estimate)\n  --max-turn-minutes <number>         Continuation: an explicit wall-clock\n                                      limit for one turn in minutes (default:\n                                      none)\n  --stagnation-steps <number>         Continuation: stop after this many steps\n                                      without progress (default 12)\n  --no-continuation                   End a turn at --max-steps instead of\n                                      continuing while it makes progress\n  -t, --temperature <number>          Model temperature (default: \"0.2\")\n  --shell <type>                      Linux shell to use: bash, zsh, or sh\n                                      (default: bash or $LOCAL_HARNESS_SHELL)\n                                      (default: \"bash\")\n  --fallback <urls>                   Comma-separated fallback LLM endpoints if\n                                      primary is unavailable\n  --context-limit <tokens>            Context window limit in tokens; below the\n                                      provider's advertised capacity it is\n                                      kept, above it the advertised capacity\n                                      applies (default: advertised capacity,\n                                      else 65536)\n  --dry-run                           Simulate file modifications without\n                                      writing changes to disk\n  --read-only                         Reject all mutating tool executions and\n                                      commands\n  -y, --yes                           Run non-interactively without approval\n                                      prompts (forces auto mode)\n  --approve                           Require human approval before destructive\n                                      actions (forces review mode)\n  --mode <mode>                       Execution mode: auto, review, or\n                                      read-only (default: review; folder trust\n                                      does not change it)\n  --sandbox [mode]                    Isolate command execution using\n                                      bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default:\n                                      auto)\n  --worktree                          Isolate execution inside an ephemeral git\n                                      worktree under .nexus/worktrees/<task-id>\n  --authoritative-verifier <command>  Trusted command that must pass before any\n                                      task completion; its success may\n                                      authorize automatic worktree merge\n  --deliverable-file <path>           Operator-declared workspace-relative\n                                      product file used for VERIFIED binding\n                                      (repeatable) (default: [])\n  --record-flight                     Record execution into an append-only\n                                      deterministic .flightlog\n  --planner-model <name>              Deep reasoning model for architecture\n                                      planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n  --planner-endpoint <url>            Dedicated inference endpoint for planner\n                                      model\n  --coder-model <name>                High-throughput model for surgical code\n                                      implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n  --coder-endpoint <url>              Dedicated inference endpoint for coder\n                                      model\n  --tdd                               Enforce strict RED-GREEN-REFACTOR\n                                      Test-Driven Development protocol\n  --provider <id>                     Cloud inference provider: openrouter,\n                                      openai, anthropic, compatible (default:\n                                      appliance endpoint)\n  --base-url <url>                    Override the provider's base URL\n                                      (operator-only; required for\n                                      'compatible')\n  --planner-provider <id>             Cloud provider for the planner model\n                                      (requires --planner-model)\n  --coder-provider <id>               Cloud provider for the coder model\n                                      (requires --coder-model)\n  -j, --json                          Output machine-readable JSON structured\n                                      result (UI-002, UI-003)\n  -r, --resume [id]                   Resume previous session or task state\n  -h, --help                          display help for command\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":884163524}},"started_at_ms":1793069042647,"completed_at_ms":1793069043531}}
