{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:50:17.424Z","ordinal":399584,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae011625f3481a0a69336d53c604da9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9113cc9929fd4213910d6b8c3e6d1ce2","name":"exec","input":"const patch=\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-openrouter-e5/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md\\n+# RC10 OpenRouter live task\\n+\\n+Disposition: `PASS` for the small live-task portion of provider E5, based on the final synthetic task below. Earlier attempts are retained as failures and are not counted as passes.\\n+\\n+## Candidate and environment\\n+\\n+- Candidate: signed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, tag target `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\\n+- Published Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\\n+- Installed binary: `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`); it reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` during independent validation.\\n+- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\\n+- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\\n+- Baseline commit: `d3cfb387f62ca7ff20b4ed5a4bd8e90ee871cb41`.\\n+- Task run: 2026-10-27, 7 model requests, 36.215 seconds, provider-reported cost `$0`; the exact model is recorded in each receipt.\\n+\\n+## Accepted attempt\\n+\\n+`attempt-js-ascii/` contains the raw JSON result, stderr, inference receipts, flight log, baseline identity and hashes, final deliverable, unchanged test, and independent validation transcript.\\n+\\n+The configured verifier was `node --test tests/slug.test.mjs`. Nexus reported `COMPLETED`, `PASSED`, and `isDeliverableBound: true`, with `unverifiedChangesPending: false`. The verifier executed one test case covering ASCII lowercasing, delimiter collapsing, non-ASCII handling, and trimming. Independent validation reran that verifier and added three assertions (`İ`, emoji separation, and whitespace-only input); all passed. Only `src/slug.mjs` was modified in the task workspace.\\n+\\n+## Failed attempts retained\\n+\\n+- `attempt-unsupported-verifier/`: the original Python run used unsupported unittest discovery syntax. Nexus failed closed with `UNVERIFIED` / `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`; it is not acceptance evidence.\\n+- `attempt-python-verifier-unbound/`: a supported Python verifier executed and passed its four tests, but Nexus did not bind the declared deliverable (`REGRESSION_FREE`, `isDeliverableBound: false`). Independent validation also found that Unicode-wide lowercasing violated the ASCII-only objective. This is a product/evaluator failure, not a pass.\\n+- The Python binding fix is tracked separately and has not been accepted; the independent reviewer requested a conservative correction for ambiguous Python `from package import name` syntax.\\n+\\n+## Scope limits\\n+\\n+This evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in the sibling `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl` and `openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json` files.\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r=await tools.apply_patch(patch);text(r)\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793069410.3743722}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:50:17.453Z","ordinal":399585,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-ccc1216f-298c-42a0-a652-9be1a3fadd01","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-openrouter-e5/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md":{"type":"add","content":"# RC10 OpenRouter live task\n\nDisposition: `PASS` for the small live-task portion of provider E5, based on the final synthetic task below. Earlier attempts are retained as failures and are not counted as passes.\n\n## Candidate and environment\n\n- Candidate: signed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, tag target `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\n- Published Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\n- Installed binary: `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`); it reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` during independent validation.\n- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\n- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\n- Baseline commit: `d3cfb387f62ca7ff20b4ed5a4bd8e90ee871cb41`.\n- Task run: 2026-10-27, 7 model requests, 36.215 seconds, provider-reported cost `$0`; the exact model is recorded in each receipt.\n\n## Accepted attempt\n\n`attempt-js-ascii/` contains the raw JSON result, stderr, inference receipts, flight log, baseline identity and hashes, final deliverable, unchanged test, and independent validation transcript.\n\nThe configured verifier was `node --test tests/slug.test.mjs`. Nexus reported `COMPLETED`, `PASSED`, and `isDeliverableBound: true`, with `unverifiedChangesPending: false`. The verifier executed one test case covering ASCII lowercasing, delimiter collapsing, non-ASCII handling, and trimming. Independent validation reran that verifier and added three assertions (`İ`, emoji separation, and whitespace-only input); all passed. Only `src/slug.mjs` was modified in the task workspace.\n\n## Failed attempts retained\n\n- `attempt-unsupported-verifier/`: the original Python run used unsupported unittest discovery syntax. Nexus failed closed with `UNVERIFIED` / `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`; it is not acceptance evidence.\n- `attempt-python-verifier-unbound/`: a supported Python verifier executed and passed its four tests, but Nexus did not bind the declared deliverable (`REGRESSION_FREE`, `isDeliverableBound: false`). Independent validation also found that Unicode-wide lowercasing violated the ASCII-only objective. This is a product/evaluator failure, not a pass.\n- The Python binding fix is tracked separately and has not been accepted; the independent reviewer requested a conservative correction for ambiguous Python `from package import name` syntax.\n\n## Scope limits\n\nThis evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in the sibling `openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl` and `openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json` files.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc10-openrouter-e5/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793069417451,"completed_at_ms":1793069417453}}
