{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:55:38.443Z","ordinal":399938,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ae012a8a30881a0b54e322dc502dd6f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_fab3b53c21234b828c44c687584e556b","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_create_pull_request({repository_full_name:\"mikeholownych/nexus-code\",head:\"v1/rc10-openrouter-e5\",base:\"main\",title:\"docs(qualification): record RC10 OpenRouter E5 evidence\",body:\"## Summary\\n\\n- Record OpenRouter verification on the exact installed v1.0.0-rc.10 artifact: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\\n- Record a fresh synthetic live task using the pinned OpenRouter model. Its configured verifier passed, Nexus bound the declared deliverable, and independent edge assertions passed.\\n- Preserve two earlier Python task attempts as failures, including the verifier-binding gap and a concrete ASCII-versus-Unicode correctness miss.\\n\\n## Evidence boundary\\n\\nThe task workspace was synthetic and contained no user project or held-out content. This establishes only the OpenRouter verification and one small live task on RC10. It does not establish held-out, T3/T4, standalone long-task, terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release acceptance.\\n\\nAll evidence bundles include checksum manifests. Independent review of this exact commit is requested.\"});text(JSON.stringify(r))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793069736.6386747}}}
