 unmeasured=\\\"the connection advertises no request counting\\\"\\n  ✔ a mutating command between attempts (here: a file outside the workspace) reruns the verifier (1488.759208ms)\\n[provider_capabilities] reason=step model=m context 65536 (client_default); output allowance 8192 (client_default); discovery unsupported (catalog lists no limits); token counting unsupported\\n[context_admission] step=1 request_id=eb46f105-6c0d-4c30-8dff-c47fcb1e385f state=admitted estimated_tokens=4735 completion_reserve=8192 tool_response_reserve=4096 limit=65536 compacted=false messages=2\\n[token_count] step=1 request_id=eb46f105-6c0d-4c30-8dff-c47fcb1e385f source=client_estimate prompt_tokens=4735 client_estimate=4735 context_limit=65536 (client_default) output_allowance=8192 (client_default) tool_headroom_policy=4096 unmeasured=\\\"the connection advertises no request counting\\\"\\n[context_admission] step=2 request_id=f4ee0599-7863-4ea1-8049-4834295d0573 state=admitted estimated_tokens=4913 c…2798 tokens truncated…erve=8192 tool_response_reserve=4096 limit=65536 compacted=false messages=2\\n[token_count] step=1 request_id=b1c0ff41-489d-4e3d-bb24-dc370f45dca3 source=client_estimate prompt_tokens=4482 client_estimate=4482 context_limit=65536 (client_default) output_allowance=8192 (client_default) tool_headroom_policy=4096 unmeasured=\\\"the connection advertises no request counting\\\"\\n  ✔ steering pending when the turn is cancelled is returned, not applied or lost (227.910516ms)\\n✔ steering during active work (2801.06599ms)\\n▶ durable state keeps tool-call relationships through redaction\\n  ✔ long provider ids become distinct stable ids instead of one redaction marker (3.776048ms)\\n  ✔ a saved session round-trips its objective, steering and history completeness (76.326271ms)\\n✔ durable state keeps tool-call relationships through redaction (80.52955ms)\\n✔ continuation prompt strips only the same trailing punctuation (3.211459ms)\\n✔ continuation prompt handles long untrusted punctuation suffixes (7.186926ms)\\n✔ operation account IDs are opaque, same-account within one operation, and unlinkable across operations (56.359324ms)\\n✔ configured primary, fallback, planner, and coder share IDs only for matching credentials in one operation (32.598165ms)\\n✔ legacy operation JSON migration preserves account condition scope and is durable across restart (308.720967ms)\\n✔ keyed state remains resumable after key loss, but unsafe key permissions fail closed (119.500851ms)\\n✔ symlinked account identity directory is rejected without following it (3.99821ms)\\n✔ a FIFO at the account identity key path is rejected without blocking or migrating state (730.358019ms)\\n✔ explicit delimiter-containing labels keep account scope while legacy IDs migrate stably (129.039577ms)\\n✔ account identity store repairs a fully written key left linked by an interrupted creator (33.476316ms)\\n✔ concurrent first use converges on one private key without leaking the key (285.709137ms)\\n✔ an EEXIST key entry is synced before use and interrupted-link cleanup (24.63107ms)\\n✔ key setup and write failures remove temporary files and never publish a key (22.290113ms)\\n✔ stale cleanup is scoped to the current PID namespace (32.021685ms)\\n✔ account identity repair tolerates another reader removing the same interrupted link (41.506883ms)\\n✔ group- or world-writable credential homes fail closed (1.209807ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","create_time":1793069921.6480017}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
