{"timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:59:48.719Z","ordinal":400195,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17b23-4ce0-7c11-90c6-74e78e580449","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-79922b56-d61e-41e6-a207-0635a75ff5ec","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.fetch_pr","arguments":{"repo_full_name":"mikeholownych/nexus-code","pr_number":265},"connectorId":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","linkId":"link_68d2673aabd08191a10c1849bf534da6","appName":"GitHub","actionName":"fetch_pr","readOnlyHint":true,"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Action completed.\"}],\"structuredContent\":{\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/265\",\"number\":265,\"state\":\"open\",\"merged\":false,\"mergeable\":true,\"draft\":false,\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Record OpenRouter verification on the exact installed v1.0.0-rc.10 artifact: streamed completion, tool call, and tool-result round trip.\\n- Record a fresh synthetic live task using the pinned OpenRouter model. Its configured verifier passed, Nexus bound the declared deliverable, and independent edge assertions passed.\\n- Preserve two earlier Python task attempts as failures, including the verifier-binding gap and a concrete ASCII-versus-Unicode correctness miss.\\n\\n## Evidence boundary\\n\\nThe task workspace was synthetic and contained no user project or held-out content. This establishes only the OpenRouter verification and one small live task on RC10. It does not establish held-out, T3/T4, standalone long-task, terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release acceptance.\\n\\nAll evidence bundles include checksum manifests. Independent review of this exact commit is requested.\",\"title\":\"docs(qualification): record RC10 OpenRouter E5 evidence\",\"base\":\"main\",\"base_sha\":\"2622663313132864677cfdc93c94944d26a3ac06\",\"head\":\"v1/rc10-openrouter-e5\",\"head_sha\":\"5e5cfd06ca52e5e1d6f1aa73a314e902fc197a46\",\"head_repo_id\":1416386345,\"head_repo_full_name\":\"mikeholownych/nexus-code\",\"merge_commit_sha\":\"33be8e6c9c1a48bdda6dfd4d8bc7ad1f4e494d34\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"mikeholownych\",\"email\":null,\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751780?v=4\",\"id\":7751780},\"requested_reviewers\":null,\"requested_team_reviewers\":null,\"diff\":\"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\\n+# RC10 OpenRouter live task\\n+\\n+Disposition: `PASS` for the small live-task portion of provider E5, based on the final synthetic task below. Earlier attempts are retained as failures and are not counted as passes.\\n+\\n+## Candidate and environment\\n+\\n+- Candidate: signed `v1.0.0-rc.10`, tag target `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`.\\n+- Published Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256: `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`.\\n+- Installed binary: `/home/mike/.local/nexus-rc10-qualification/bin/nexus` on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`); it reported `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)` during independent validation.\\n+- Provider/model: OpenRouter, `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free`.\\n+- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\\n+- Baseline commit: `d3cfb387f62ca7ff20b4ed5a4bd8e90ee871cb41`.\\n+- Task run: 2026-10-27, 7 model requests, 36.215 seconds, provider-reported cost `$0`; the exact model is recorded in each receipt.\\n+\\n+## Accepted attempt\\n+\\n+`attempt-js-ascii/` contains the raw JSON result, stderr, inference receipts, flight log, baseline identity and hashes, final deliverable, unchanged test, and independent validation transcript.\\n+\\n+The configured verifier was `node --test tests/slug.test.mjs`. Nexus reported `COMPLETED`, `PASSED`, and `isDeliverableBound: true`, with `unverifiedChangesPending: false`. The verifier executed one test case covering ASCII lowercasing, delimiter collapsing, non-ASCII handling, and trimming. Independent validation reran that verifier and added three assertions (`İ`, emoji separation, and whitespace-only input); all passed. Only `src/slug.mjs` was modified in the task workspace.\\n+\\n+## Failed attempts retained\\n+\\n+- `attempt-unsupported-verifier/`: the original Python run used unsupported unittest discovery syntax. Nexus failed closed with `UNVERIFIED` / `VERIFICATION_NOT_RUN`; it is not acceptance evidence.\\n+- `attempt-python-verifier-unbound/`: a supported Python verifier executed and passed its four tests, but Nexus did not bind the declared deliverable (`REGRESSION_FREE`, `isDeliverableBound: false`). Independent validation also found that Unicode-wide lowercasing violated the ASCII-only objective. This is a product/evaluator failure, not a pass.\\n+- The Python binding fix is tracked separately and has not been accepted; the independent reviewer requested a conservative correction for ambiguous Python `from package import name` syntax.\\n+\\n+## Scope limits\\n+\\n+This evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in [`../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`](../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl) and [`../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json`](../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json).\\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\\n+388f73d9a2e137787ff85454ecbeee73676f7d6ee4ee6c38041f1d15f45928e3  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md\\n+af2883c11345d2370bd4886060fe8b80b78455e0f6b50252b14a5b185afc9918  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/baseline-commit.txt\\n+1f0a92f306a3078ee3d8cccdb0d3bee7d2e4a160177e4dc1416a9810eae10ca2  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/baseline-sha256.txt\\n+9a271f2a916b0b6ee6cecb2426f0b3206ef074578be55d9bc94f6f3fe3ab86aa  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/exit-code.txt\\n+9dd6b8f453169e47548cc0b991d88b2c6a2824ad5fd513ccb017b71dbe1986e5  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/flightlog\\n+0dd177ed2dcaca847bba5cd88dc0186c03a898f2246ba4f00e50db3f2d2ee011  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/independent-validation.txt\\n+d70b26150032dc2930ac02edabe12e439272b272543b89ffef732ad4c07383a2  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/receipts.jsonl\\n+ee1d1d52e78b64925d4a6c25d6406c32c63ea30b03af3ecf0c7c77035b3c7ac1  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/run.json\\n+f7cf6a6733e54e0a3581448fe66a1496f36153d6cc20257b7ccd48ef41ba168b  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/run.stderr\\n+2d80f9d4b477ce73b3cc42733a35b4cd9bb147244e8025d7cbc13353ad29a974  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/slug.mjs\\n+53363655c295e9ed637bf7a65caeb6b856b6ef8e702535e94d8f547002efd810  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-js-ascii/slug.test.mjs\\n+d5de3e41e593ee5e26c90cb532eccb66cdf45c72a3a74c22384eb728f1087725  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-python-verifier-unbound/receipts.jsonl\\n+a4628d77dbab686a51ae895e267dffb9eae3e55b60d7f6f105120eb259b78e94  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/attempt-python-verifier-unbound/run.json\\n+5efbc86f08afde86322e575384858ef9e53c1e715872395f27aecfd4589710ac  docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-t